{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread","id":1501118,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get A Simple Answer (Changeling) [new thread]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-22T23:39:19-08:00","id":1501118,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get A Simple Answer (Changeling) [new thread]","content":"The old thread is huge and is now closed, so I'm starting a new one for all your Changeling questions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T08:20:54-08:00","id":1501137,"title":"","content":"Are there rules (official or homebrew) for making hobgoblins as player characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T12:21:04-08:00","id":1501157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1501137#post1501137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules (official or homebrew) for making hobgoblins as player characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>None officially. Kind of counter-productive for the goals of Chronicles on the whole. Wouldn't be too surprised if someone's done a homebrew though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T00:17:33-08:00","id":1501218,"title":"","content":"Thanks for starting a new thread TheStray7!<br /> <br /> This is something I have been pondering on for a while. I was in a discussion a while back with someone over the nature of Contracts and their writeups - that anything not about the strict mechanics of a contract was up for changes, including things like &quot;Pipes of the Beast Caller&quot; not requiring a silver flute to be used or &quot;Tumult&quot; not needing a leaf at all, much less origami folding. This always struck me as off because these bits are mingled with how the Contracts function mechanically, and at times even end up in the Loopholes of the contracts (such as with &quot;Pipes of the Beast Caller&quot; and &quot;Tumult&quot;).<br /> <br /> Am I off here? Are these bits just flavour, or are they part of how the Contracts are evoked and thus not subject to change with the visuals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-24-2023, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T00:38:54-08:00","id":1501221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1501137#post1501137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules (official or homebrew) for making hobgoblins as player characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>No official rules for making a regular hobgoblin playable, but there are the Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen Conditions for playing a non-hobgoblin character becoming a goblin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T06:33:32-08:00","id":1501315,"title":"","content":"Do Changelings have the ability to draw glamour from the air without getting involved in 2e anymore? I was in a game where this was a thing but I can\u2019t find it in the book proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T08:12:18-08:00","id":1501318,"title":"","content":"Harvesting Glamour in 2e has to harvest from a person and drains one point of Willpower from the target, but doesn't have to involve direct interaction with the person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T06:27:42-08:00","id":1501534,"title":"","content":"How would you update the Goblin Contract <u>Seven-Year Gift*</u> to 2e? Just a Goblin Contract? A Token (&quot;Flask of Youth&quot;)? Or a type of Goblin Fruit (&quot;Fruit of the Tree of Life&quot;)?<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Spend 2 Glamour and a dot of Willpower to halt the target's aging for seven years, or permanently reverse their aging by seven years on an exceptional success</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-28-2023, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T12:30:43-08:00","id":1501972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1501534#post1501534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you update the Goblin Contract <u>Seven-Year Gift*</u> to 2e? Just a Goblin Contract? A Token (&quot;Flask of Youth&quot;)? Or a type of Goblin Fruit (&quot;Fruit of the Tree of Life&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Option 1:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Seven-Year Gift (Goblin)</b><br /> <br /> Seven Years. The changeling summons terrifying power that saps the will to continue on into longevity. This Contract only works on mortals, and to use this Contract, the changeling must touch the target. However, the target does not need not know what is being done.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 DOT of Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> Effect: The target will not age for the next seven years (though she is not protected from disease or other potential ills). \u200b<br /> <br /> Loophole: The target is a blood relative of the changeling within three generations.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Option 2:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Flask of Youth (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Effect: Anyone who drinks the entirety of the contents from the Flask of Youth will not age for the next seven years. Only works on mortals.<br /> <br /> Catch: You give the Flask of Youth to someone else with the intent of giving them eternal youth.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The Flask of Youth, to be active once again, must have a DOT of Willpower sacrificed into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:11:41-08:00","id":1501978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super Vlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1501972#post1501972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>Option 1:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Seven-Year Gift (Goblin)</b><br /> <br /> Seven Years. The changeling summons terrifying power that saps the will to continue on into longevity. This Contract only works on mortals, and to use this Contract, the changeling must touch the target. However, the target does not need not know what is being done.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 DOT of Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> Effect: The target will not age for the next seven years (though she is not protected from disease or other potential ills). \u200b<br /> <br /> Loophole: The target is a blood relative of the changeling within three generations.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Option 2:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Flask of Youth (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Effect: Anyone who drinks the entirety of the contents from the Flask of Youth will not age for the next seven years. Only works on mortals.<br /> <br /> Catch: You give the Flask of Youth to someone else with the intent of giving them eternal youth.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The Flask of Youth, to be active once again, must have a DOT of Willpower sacrificed into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! &quot;Mortals&quot; here applies to most splats, right? Only those who don't age, like Vampires, aren't affected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:14:42-08:00","id":1502045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1501978#post1501978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! &quot;Mortals&quot; here applies to most splats, right? Only those who don't age, like Vampires, aren't affected?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, sort of? Usually mortals tends to regard anyone who doesn't have a Supernatural Tolerance (half-splats are ok).<br /> The reason why I put it like that is so Mages, Werewolves, Geists, etc. don't go living forever with a simple Goblin Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T15:51:06-08:00","id":1502059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super Vlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502045#post1502045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, sort of? Usually mortals tends to regard anyone who doesn't have a Supernatural Tolerance (half-splats are ok).<br /> The reason why I put it like that is so Mages, Werewolves, Geists, etc. don't go living forever with a simple Goblin Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I was actually asking because I think it makes a good plot-point for a Mage game. Liches aren't usually seen as a good thing, self-harm to achieve Lichdom is bad, and relying on the gifts of the Hedge to achieve it is worse. If the Heirarch never seems to get older, but doesn't have active magic keeping them that way, people'll start asking questions.<br /> <br /> I'll admit to being quite uninformed on Werewolf and Giest, but aren't both functionally unaging? I though Werewolves aged like sharks, and Giests were age-locked to when they take their bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T16:28:52-08:00","id":1502063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502059#post1502059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, I was actually asking because I think it makes a good plot-point for a Mage game. Liches aren't usually seen as a good thing, self-harm to achieve Lichdom is bad, and relying on the gifts of the Hedge to achieve it is worse. If the Heirarch never seems to get older, but doesn't have active magic keeping them that way, people'll start asking questions.<br /> <br /> I'll admit to being quite uninformed on Werewolf and Giest, but aren't both functionally unaging? I though Werewolves aged like sharks, and Giests were age-locked to when they take their bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno how sharks age, but IIRC, werewolves had about twice a human\u2019s lifespan (it\u2019s just that they have a far shorter life expectancy\u2026) and Sin-Eaters are still open to death by old age. (Their Geists are, well, ephemeral entities.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T09:24:17-08:00","id":1502610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502063#post1502063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno how sharks age, but IIRC, werewolves had about twice a human\u2019s lifespan (it\u2019s just that they have a far shorter life expectancy\u2026) and Sin-Eaters are still open to death by old age. (Their Geists are, well, ephemeral entities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Sin-eater could due, become a Ghost, get to the required Rank to become a Geist, and Bind a new sin-eater... Reproducing in a very slow but weird way.<br /> <br /> Question:<br /> <br /> Someone suggested Mages meeting in the Astral (possibly as a security measure).<br /> <br /> Could Changelings do similar? Have a regular freehold meeting in someone's dreams? Would it be safer/more secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T10:42:27-08:00","id":1502614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502610#post1502610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Sin-eater could due, become a Ghost, get to the required Rank to become a Geist, and Bind a new sin-eater... Reproducing in a very slow but weird way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intro fiction from 1e aside, I'm pretty sure being metaphysically dead precludes the Bound leaving ghosts since they're functionally already a weird type of ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could Changelings do similar? Have a regular freehold meeting in someone's dreams? Would it be safer/more secret? </div> </div> </div>Bastions do have the benefit of putting an extra layer of defense between you and whoever's outside, but the nature of oneiromancy is such that it's a bit fraught even without the hike you'd need to take to get there through the Dreaming Roads \u2014 without some special Contract or token or other circumstance, you can only show up straight into someone's dreams in their physical presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T19:22:33-08:00","id":1502665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502614#post1502614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intro fiction from 1e aside, I'm pretty sure being metaphysically dead precludes the Bound leaving ghosts since they're functionally already a weird type of ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember it being mentioned in the GTS2e core that a Bound character who dies completely may start playing as an Absent, though I can't find it and don't know of any search terms to help find it. Perhaps it didn't make it through errata","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:25:43-08:00","id":1502842,"title":"","content":"Do the Seasonal Loeg (Core p. 283) access the same Court Contracts and merits that the regular Seasonal Courts?<br /> <br /> This is specially relevant for Regular Summer and Winter Lag, thematically both courts have the same function but are opposed seasons. The Firebrand (Summer court) merit for example is perfect for Winter Lag courtiers.<br /> <br /> Also, do they keep the same Court Crowns?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T13:03:51-08:00","id":1502952,"title":"","content":"Is there a collective term for all the stuff beyond a hedgegate?<br /> <br /> And is it more than Arcadia and the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:50:41-08:00","id":1503187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502952#post1502952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a collective term for all the stuff beyond a hedgegate?<br /> <br /> And is it more than Arcadia and the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK: There is neither a term nor more of a location.<br /> <br /> You could say that the Hollows being subdimensions of the Hedge could count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T00:49:36-08:00","id":1503210,"title":"","content":"I'm going with the Otherworld. Mostly because I'm trying to make a cosmological map...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T07:05:15-08:00","id":1503236,"title":"","content":"In the same spirit that Earth and surrounding space is referred to in some books as the material realm (though technically speaking, the Hedge and Arcadia are both also material realms), one might refer to them as the fae realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T09:20:17-08:00","id":1503320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502842#post1502842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Seasonal Loeg (Core p. 283) access the same Court Contracts and merits that the regular Seasonal Courts?<br /> <br /> This is specially relevant for Regular Summer and Winter Lag, thematically both courts have the same function but are opposed seasons. The Firebrand (Summer court) merit for example is perfect for Winter Lag courtiers.<br /> <br /> Also, do they keep the same Court Crowns?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a question without an objective answer right now, since no books have been made for them. The simplest answer is to just reskin the current seasonal contracts and crowns, the hardest is to homebrew your own. Unfortunately courts take a sizeable part of the book, and contracts are a big part of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T05:26:43-08:00","id":1503371,"title":"","content":"Does the 9-again bonus of Professional Training skills apply to Contract rolls?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling Core p. 112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling gains access to a court\u2019s Mantle effects<br /> at two dots lower than his dots in that court\u2019s Goodwill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Court Goodwill allow to buy Court specific merits (Firebrand, Grounded, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T14:36:27-08:00","id":1503400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503371#post1503371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 9-again bonus of Professional Training skills apply to Contract rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tentatively say yes, so long as the Skill is an Asset Skill. That is, I would Ok it at my table, but RAW doesn't have a position that I could find at a glance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503371#post1503371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Court Goodwill allow to buy Court specific merits (Firebrand, Grounded, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow it, under the auspices of those Merits being tied into the Mantle that Goodwill can give you access to. However, I would use the same Mantle limitations as listed in the Goodwill merit. That is, only Court Goodwill (Autumn) 5 would allow you to purchase Cloak of Leaves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T12:26:12-08:00","id":1503627,"title":"","content":"Questions about Hollows:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hollow enhancements p.116 Core Changeling 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luxury Goods (\u2022): <b>A variety of mundane supplies<br /> and Hedgespun treats fills the Hollow, which allows a<br /> changeling to hold out for the long haul.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Size Matters (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022): Without purchasing this<br /> enhancement, the Hollow is only big enough for two<br /> changelings to sleep comfortably. With one dot, a motley<br /> of five to six changelings has enough room to stay without<br /> immediate cabin fever. <b>The second dot turns the Hollow<br /> into a vast estate or small town, and members of a motley<br /> might not even see each other for the duration of a stay.</b><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Size Matters 2</b> does it allow you to pick the ornaments and contents of the place? I am thinking of making a Hollow a refuge for large numbers of people.</li> <li>Tied with the previous questions, does <b>Luxury Goods</b> provide you with enough food for how many people?</li> <li>How is the hygiene or at least the waste disposal of a Hollow handled?</li> </ol>Essentially, I was thinking of having a large place to stay for a long while, while having enough amenities so people dont go crazy: gym, pool, gardens, etc. But there is also the matter of what do these people eat and drink, and they place can become inhospitable if soiled enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T13:15:54-08:00","id":1503628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503627#post1503627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about Hollows:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Size Matters 2</b> does it allow you to pick the ornaments and contents of the place? I am thinking of making a Hollow a refuge for large numbers of people.</li> <li>Tied with the previous questions, does <b>Luxury Goods</b> provide you with enough food for how many people?</li> <li>How is the hygiene or at least the waste disposal of a Hollow handled?</li> </ol>Essentially, I was thinking of having a large place to stay for a long while, while having enough amenities so people dont go crazy: gym, pool, gardens, etc. But there is also the matter of what do these people eat and drink, and they place can become inhospitable if soiled enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer to all three would be &quot;whatever makes sense narratively&quot;. Literally, since it's the Hedge.<br /> <br /> A small town could provide houses for... let's ballpark and say around twenty households, so anywhere between 20 and 100 people, depending on what kind of housing you've decided to include.<br /> <br /> I'd personally rule that the food restocks itself (infinite larders, fruit trees that bear new fruit daily, etc) at regular intervals, with enough food to keep the population on starvation rations regardless of how many people are actually present. That is, there's always enough food to survive solely on what's present, but doing so is not properly nutritious.<br /> <br /> Is the Hollow something with plumbing, like a manor house? Or is it a network of caves, with a river running through it and a &quot;latrine&quot; room situated above where the river becomes a waterfall and moves out of your fresh-water collection area. Maybe there's a latrine pit that never seems to fully fill. It really depends on what you've created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T13:22:21-08:00","id":1503629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503627#post1503627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about Hollows:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Size Matters 2</b> does it allow you to pick the ornaments and contents of the place? I am thinking of making a Hollow a refuge for large numbers of people.</li> <li>Tied with the previous questions, does <b>Luxury Goods</b> provide you with enough food for how many people?</li> <li>How is the hygiene or at least the waste disposal of a Hollow handled?</li> </ol>Essentially, I was thinking of having a large place to stay for a long while, while having enough amenities so people dont go crazy: gym, pool, gardens, etc. But there is also the matter of what do these people eat and drink, and they place can become inhospitable if soiled enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The general idea is that you fill up the hollow with whatever you bring to it, both from the Hedge and from Ironside. Usually the exact details don't <i>really</i> matter unless the items in questions are intended to allow for benefits, but there is a general thift store/junkyard/trash chateau vibe to a lot of Hollows unless you have have Resources or otherwise have the general downtime expectation of players steadily improving their Hollow over time (And even then, the hand-me-down, second hand feel probably never fully leaves). But as a general rule, you have freedom of description over your Hollow, within reason.<br /> 2) Yeah, it's not too unreasonable to permit Luxury Goods to cover the regular food angle of a Hollow for large numbers of people. There are other answers, like Resources, or enough Mantle-as-Status as well.<br /> 3) However you think to handle it. An Autumn court sorcerer of mine basically used medieval outhouses for his answer (with the fecal matter also factoring into compost and other material for his goblin garden), and in another game designing a plumbing and sewage system for a community of Hollows was a significant b-plot for an arc of the game. Which means, yes, going to pop a squat on a toilet was turned into a horror scenario-after all, if the community didn't do a good enough job, who knows what could crawl out of your toilet. Then again, you may just have a Token toilet that takes all of that....somewhere else, but guarentees it's not <i>your</i> problem.<br /> <br /> It's pretty easy to imagine that most freeholds have at least one way station for the newly returned or recently dismantled, whether it's a freehold project or the interests of an individual. The general state of homelessness for changelings is the sort of thing you can usually rely on someone to deal with, and a Freehold that doesn't can safely be assumed to be cold and heartless. *cough*[insert modern societal commentary here]*cough*<br /> <br /> While a 1E product, Rites of Spring remains ever pertinent for questions, and if you want any more follow up, Dancers in the Dusk and Goblin Market should provide additional information.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, if you're going to play Changeling, you should have Rites of Spring, even if you're playing 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-21-2023, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:25:28-08:00","id":1503633,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> I was thinking on the lines, what does the Freehold do when they need to hunker down? And if another supernatural would use the Hollow as a way to isolate themselves from the ordinary world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question, the core book states that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core Book p. 108</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fae beings and <b>other supernatural creatures with<br /> mystical senses can see through the Mask</b>.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean that a Werewolf always sees a Changeling as they are? Do Vampires need to use Auspex? What about Mages? Other supers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:57:52-08:00","id":1503639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503633#post1503633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> I was thinking on the lines, what does the Freehold do when they need to hunker down? And if another supernatural would use the Hollow as a way to isolate themselves from the ordinary world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question, the core book states that:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So does this mean that a Werewolf always sees a Changeling as they are? Do Vampires need to use Auspex? What about Mages? Other supers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages... I remember the Contagion Chronicles player book stating that Mages with Mind or Fate Mage Sight up automatically see through the Mask, and those using other Arcana's Mage Sight will see relevant parts. Forces Mage sight, for example, might see how the cold radiating off a Snowskin or a Winter Countier is supernatural and pierce that specific part of their Mask.<br /> <br /> Werewolves... I think they can smell their way through the Mask? I'll see what I can find and edit in anything I locate. But the general assumption I take is that any Supernatural using sensory enhancement should be able to see throught relevant parts of the Mask - Werewolves get an accurate smell-sense of the Changeling, Auspex picks up on inconsistencies, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-21-2023, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:57:34-08:00","id":1503655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503633#post1503633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> I was thinking on the lines, what does the Freehold do when they need to hunker down? And if another supernatural would use the Hollow as a way to isolate themselves from the ordinary world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question, the core book states that:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So does this mean that a Werewolf always sees a Changeling as they are? Do Vampires need to use Auspex? What about Mages? Other supers?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first question, it depends on the courts and the agreements between them for emergency responses, and what particular emergencies are planned for. Changelings on the whole are more prone to flight than than fight or defend as a reaction, but that's mostly something to keep in the back of your mind while establishing what that looks like. A unified freehold will react differently than a freehold in conflict with itself, the response to a hurricane is different from the response to a True Fae, and the way the Seasonal Courts handle a scenario would be different from how the Rose Courts would challenge it.<br /> <br /> For the other supernaturals, a lot of it depends on the ability to access such, but as a broad rule, the Hedge is a pretty reliable safe space against anything on the whole given it's over all general subversive hostility, and the world of fortifying and defending a Hollow multiplies that. A demon might still want a Bolthole in that hollow, but pretty much anyone else with a pursuing antagonist can hole up pretty well in ther, so long as the particulars of that antagonist don't facilitate access. The downside is that unless they have a friend in a changeling willing to compromise their Hollow a little bit of that ficilitation, they don't have any more of a guarentee to keeping a Hollow than anyone else, and the Hedge is just as hostile to them as anyone else.<br /> <br /> On the issue of the Mask, this is something that can kind of get variable across books. The general rule is that the Mask is a potent enough kitch of magic that it's not idly broken through, but within the purview of what they can do and more specifically specialize in, it can be apparent enough. As a general run down (and a caveat, assume a lot of these carry a rider of &quot;particularly if a changeling's Wyrd is high):<ul><li>Vampires can probably tell there's something off about a changeling's blood and heartbeat by the scent and sound and will definitely realize something's up when they try to drink the blood (subject to rules on Unnatural Affinity and The Player's Guide to the Contagion as applied), and Auspex 2 is usually enough to pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Werewolves can usually smell through the Mask, can usually taste something off in their blood, and if they're in an environment that let's them take advantage of their hearing may be able to hear oddities from a changeling's Mien. Gift Facets like Scent the Unnatural and Know the Prey are pretty reasonable excuses to just pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Active Mage Sight can usually pierce parts of the Mask based on the relevant Arcane to the changes, and Fate or Mind AMS can pierce it outright.</li> <li>Prometheans have no particular innate feature that lets them note changelings (though as a spot of fun, you might rule a Promethean sleeping next to a changeling whose kith is elementally aligned with their Lineage might restore Pyros, leading to <i>questions</i> and <i>shipping</i>), but Distillitions of the Bestiae Alembic in Metamorphosis might pick up on details leaking through, and the Vitreous Alembic of Sensorium and the Veritas Alembic of Spiritus are viable for piercing the Mask.</li> <li>Hunter's entire schtick is investigating and poking at incongruities, which often entails long-term observation, so as a general rule they don't, though obviously some Conspiracy Hunters have particulars-off hand without going to the book, the Malleus Maleificarum, Lucifuge, and Ascending Ones all probably have ways of piercing the Mask.</li> <li>Sin-Eaters and other Bound may be able see parts of the mien of changelings with death/ghost associated Kiths, may be able to pick up something off with certain Caul transformations, and could properly reveal the changeling unto themselves with Oracle.</li> <li>The Arisen don't have any particular ability to sense incongruities or pierce the mask on their own, but may perceive the changeling's lacerated soul with Soulsight, pierce the Mask with Godsight, and might see some bleed through of death/ghost associated Kiths with Deathsight. Reasonably, the third tier of Secrets Ripped from the Sky could pierce the Mask. I also wouldn't consider it too wild if someone evoking Tier 3 of Blessed is the God-King also got to pierce through the Mask, but that's a me thing.</li> <li>Demons have no particular gift for breaching the Mask on their own, but there are so many tools for doing getting the hint or otherwise piercing the Mask. Inquisitorsrs may reasonably be able to use their Prepared for Anything Condition to get that something's off with the changeling. In terms of Demonic Forms, Electrical Sight, Sonic Acuity, and Blind Sense migt pick up on elements of the Mien bleeding through, and Aura Sight can pierce the Mask. A demon who knows, broadly, that they're looking for a changeling can use Special Someone to point one out in a crowd, though that won't pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Family Resemblance may allow a Beast to know a changeling is a changeling, but doesn't pierce the Mask. The Eye of Heaven may be able to discern the changeling's deep ties to the Wyrd, and Low Satiety Needs Must can pierce the Mask on a Clash of Wills. It's not inconceivable that a Nightmare might able to affect the Mask in some kind of way, but no such Nightmare is currently textual.</li> <li>Deviant has too many variations for me go through, so no inante ability, but probably have something that can do the job.</li> </ul>As general aids on the subjects go, Kith and Kin, Rites of Spring, and Players Guide to the Contagion are probably the most useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T18:08:18-08:00","id":1503656,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, the Mask is the second most potent passive concealment power amongst all the major templates after Cover, and is in some ways superior to it*. How much of a bother it should be to pierce the Mask is dependent on the context of the game primarily, but it's not something you should idly just <i>breach</i>. Changelings, after all, might be liars, unless they're willing to vulnerable.<br /> <br /> *Cover's main weakness that the Mask doesn't have is that Cover theoretically applies to all aspects of the Cover's life, and investigation into incongruities of the Cover can cause it to wear away-even if strictly speaking, it's not investigating the Demon in cover at the moment. The Mask does not wear away, even after death, and can only be removed by the changeling at will or at the subjection to otherwise hella fucking powerful magic, perfectly conceals a changelings Mien at low levels (barring their shadow), and only really leaks without prodding when a changeling starts to become exceptionally powerful (Wyrd 6+). It's a <i>tough</i> bit of passive concealment to punch through, and while active concealment powers are always more powerful and and active perception powers can always be argued to have leeway to pierce it, anything lesser will pretty usually fail.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1502952#post1502952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a collective term for all the stuff beyond a hedgegate?<br /> <br /> And is it more than Arcadia and the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Faerie is usually reserved for the domain of the True Fae on the opposite side of the Hedge, it has been applied as a collective term for the Hedge and Arcadia by certain parties (usually non-fairies). That said, most people refer to what's beyond the gates as The Hedge and Arcadia, unsurprisingly.<br /> <br /> So far, the only demarcations of Faerie (in the sense of everything beyond the Hedge Gates) are the Hedge and Arcadia. The night woods of the Huntsmen may become particularly demarcated in their own way but by and large are just a part of the Hedge, in the same way the Dreaming and Wishing roads are technically their own distinct partitions in the Hedge but are still the Hedge. Otherwise, there are no distinct worlds beyond the Hedge Gates, unshockingly.<br /> <br /> Hollow are not subdimensions anymore than rooms in a house are subdimensions. Wards might create the illusion of such, though.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-21-2023, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T18:23:43-08:00","id":1503658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503655#post1503655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the first question, it depends on the courts and the agreements between them for emergency responses, and what particular emergencies are planned for. Changelings on the whole are more prone to flight than than fight or defend as a reaction, but that's mostly something to keep in the back of your mind while establishing what that looks like. A unified freehold will react differently than a freehold in conflict with itself, the response to a hurricane is different from the response to a True Fae, and the way the Seasonal Courts handle a scenario would be different from how the Rose Courts would challenge it.<br /> <br /> For the other supernaturals, a lot of it depends on the ability to access such, but as a broad rule, the Hedge is a pretty reliable safe space against anything on the whole given it's over all general subversive hostility, and the world of fortifying and defending a Hollow multiplies that. A demon might still want a Bolthole in that hollow, but pretty much anyone else with a pursuing antagonist can hole up pretty well in ther, so long as the particulars of that antagonist don't facilitate access. T<b>he downside is that unless they have a friend in a changeling willing to compromise their Hollow a little bit of that ficilitation, they don't have any more of a guarentee to keeping a Hollow than anyone else, and the Hedge is just as hostile to them as anyone else.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I think we discussed on the previous Ask Thread, that at least Mages can also own Hollows with the <b>Malleable Thorns</b> spell to get subtle or paradigm shifts, right? There is a Paradigm shift that allows them to modify a Hollow and another to bank successes, so those two seem to me to be the basis of the mages ability to keep a Hollow on their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503655#post1503655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the issue of the Mask, this is something that can kind of get variable across books. The general rule is that the Mask is a potent enough kitch of magic that it's not idly broken through, but within the purview of what they can do and more specifically specialize in, it can be apparent enough. As a general run down (and a caveat, assume a lot of these carry a rider of &quot;particularly if a changeling's Wyrd is high):<ul><li>Vampires can probably tell there's something off about a changeling's blood and heartbeat by the scent and sound and will definitely realize something's up when they try to drink the blood (subject to rules on Unnatural Affinity and The Player's Guide to the Contagion as applied), and Auspex 2 is usually enough to pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Werewolves can usually smell through the Mask, can usually taste something off in their blood, and if they're in an environment that let's them take advantage of their hearing may be able to hear oddities from a changeling's Mien. Gift Facets like Scent the Unnatural and Know the Prey are pretty reasonable excuses to just pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Active Mage Sight can usually pierce parts of the Mask based on the relevant Arcane to the changes, and Fate or Mind AMS can pierce it outright.</li> <li>Prometheans have no particular innate feature that lets them note changelings (though as a spot of fun, you might rule a Promethean sleeping next to a changeling whose kith is elementally aligned with their Lineage might restore Pyros, leading to <i>questions</i> and <i>shipping</i>), but Distillitions of the Bestiae Alembic in Metamorphosis might pick up on details leaking through, and the Vitreous Alembic of Sensorium and the Veritas Alembic of Spiritus are viable for piercing the Mask.</li> <li>Hunter's entire schtick is investigating and poking at incongruities, which often entails long-term observation, so as a general rule they don't, though obviously some Conspiracy Hunters have particulars-off hand without going to the book, the Malleus Maleificarum, Lucifuge, and Ascending Ones all probably have ways of piercing the Mask.</li> <li>Sin-Eaters and other Bound may be able see parts of the mien of changelings with death/ghost associated Kiths, may be able to pick up something off with certain Caul transformations, and could properly reveal the changeling unto themselves with Oracle.</li> <li>The Arisen don't have any particular ability to sense incongruities or pierce the mask on their own, but may perceive the changeling's lacerated soul with Soulsight, pierce the Mask with Godsight, and might see some bleed through of death/ghost associated Kiths with Deathsight. Reasonably, the third tier of Secrets Ripped from the Sky could pierce the Mask. I also wouldn't consider it too wild if someone evoking Tier 3 of Blessed is the God-King also got to pierce through the Mask, but that's a me thing.</li> <li>Demons have no particular gift for breaching the Mask on their own, but there are so many tools for doing getting the hint or otherwise piercing the Mask. Inquisitorsrs may reasonably be able to use their Prepared for Anything Condition to get that something's off with the changeling. In terms of Demonic Forms, Electrical Sight, Sonic Acuity, and Blind Sense migt pick up on elements of the Mien bleeding through, and Aura Sight can pierce the Mask. A demon who knows, broadly, that they're looking for a changeling can use Special Someone to point one out in a crowd, though that won't pierce the Mask.</li> <li>Family Resemblance may allow a Beast to know a changeling is a changeling, but doesn't pierce the Mask. The Eye of Heaven may be able to discern the changeling's deep ties to the Wyrd, and Low Satiety Needs Must can pierce the Mask on a Clash of Wills. It's not inconceivable that a Nightmare might able to affect the Mask in some kind of way, but no such Nightmare is currently textual.</li> <li>Deviant has too many variations for me go through, so no inante ability, but probably have something that can do the job.</li> </ul>As general aids on the subjects go, Kith and Kin, Rites of Spring, and Players Guide to the Contagion are probably the most useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very detailed list, thanks. I do not have access to all books but I will try to get those you mention.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T18:34:23-08:00","id":1503659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503658#post1503658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I think we discussed on the previous Ask Thread, that at least Mages can also own Hollows with the <b>Malleable Thorns</b> spell to get subtle or paradigm shifts, right? There is a Paradigm shift that allows them to modify a Hollow and another to bank successes, so those two seem to me to be the basis of the mages ability to keep a Hollow on their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a very detailed list, thanks. I do not have access to all books but I will try to get those you mention.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, Mages should be able to do that with Malleable Thorns. I forgot to follow up with what Rites of Spring said on the subject, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> On that note, because everyone should know this: if you get one book after the Changeling Core Book, Get Rites of Spring. Doesn't matter if you're playing Second Edition (though if you are, the next big suggestion is Kith and Kin), Rites of Spring covers so much ground work of how Changeling works that it still generally works in Second Edition, or at least certainly answer questions that probably won't be answered for some time (though when The Hedge comes out, *drools*). Doesn't matter what you are specifically doing with your game (Yes, even if you are doing an intensive antagonistically driven game [Autumn Nightmares, Night Horrors: Grim Fears], deeply self-exploratory stories or far ranging and maybe even global stories[Winter Masques], deeply politically intriguing games [Lords of Summer, Goblin Market, Oak, Ash, and Thorn], high fantasy, grand powered, and end-gamey stories [The Equinox Road], or highly variable stories [Dancers in the Dusk, Swords at Dawn, and Victorian Lost]), you want Rites of Spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T12:19:13-08:00","id":1503691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503658#post1503658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I think we discussed on the previous Ask Thread, that at least Mages can also own Hollows with the <b>Malleable Thorns</b> spell to get subtle or paradigm shifts, right? There is a Paradigm shift that allows them to modify a Hollow and another to bank successes, so those two seem to me to be the basis of the mages ability to keep a Hollow on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>So getting back to this, a few things: Okay, the crossover Hedge mechanics are actually in Equinox Road, while the mechanics behind first edition's Hollow maintanence are in Rites of Spring, and it(crossover mechanics) doesn't quite entail what a non-fairy can do to shape the Hedge or otherwise keep a Hollow. Thusly, I might suggest some quick and dirty ideas on what a non-fairy might do to wrestle the Hedge into shape later on, keeping in mind that's inclined to not make it easy.<br /> <br /> That said, the easiest option is to find a way to conscript a hobgoblin or changeling into an ongoing bargain for the upkeep. Goblin Markets aren't only open to the fae, after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T18:11:13-08:00","id":1503711,"title":"","content":"When hedgespinning can successes be allocated to multiple shifts or can you only do one effect per hedgespinning action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T20:03:47-08:00","id":1503724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503711#post1503711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When hedgespinning can successes be allocated to multiple shifts or can you only do one effect per hedgespinning action?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T00:17:43-08:00","id":1503739,"title":"","content":"For Steal Influence, from Kith and Kin, it notes that a Changeling can use the Influence by spending the appropriate amount of glamour. However, Influence works based off a roll, Power + Finesse, which Changelings possess as three attributes apiece. How would this be amended, given I don't see an answer in Steal Influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T02:23:39-08:00","id":1503744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503739#post1503739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Steal Influence, from Kith and Kin, it notes that a Changeling can use the Influence by spending the appropriate amount of glamour. However, Influence works based off a roll, Power + Finesse, which Changelings possess as three attributes apiece. How would this be amended, given I don't see an answer in Steal Influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Straightforward answer would be to treat it like the Influence Dread Power on p. 254 of the corebook.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has Facets that give specific Influences with dice pools composed of set Attribute + Skill + Renown combinations. Especially if requiring a roll even unopposed, you might possibly consider picking specific Power and Finesse Attributes or a specific Attribute and Skill thematically appropriate to the Influence and the being it was stolen from, and then adding Mantle if the Influence is suitably near the purview of your Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T04:52:45-08:00","id":1503747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503739#post1503739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Steal Influence, from Kith and Kin, it notes that a Changeling can use the Influence by spending the appropriate amount of glamour. However, Influence works based off a roll, Power + Finesse, which Changelings possess as three attributes apiece. How would this be amended, given I don't see an answer in Steal Influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the &quot;Influence&quot; Dread Power hobgoblins use:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> INFLUENCE (\u2022 TO \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Much like a Hedge ghost, this hobgoblin has Influence over a certain phenomenon. <b>Using Influence doesn\u2019t require a roll unless a character directly opposes the activation. For contested or resisted actions, decide on an Attribute + Skill dice pool that fits with the hobgoblin\u2019s nature.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T16:59:09-08:00","id":1503785,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for that. It helps a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T12:37:16-08:00","id":1503836,"title":"","content":"Changelings are the only ones who can aquire a Mantle, correct? Mantles are &quot;Changeling&quot; merits, and as such wouldn't be valid to aquire via Borrowed Favor + Court Goodwill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-24-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T21:42:49-08:00","id":1503876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503836#post1503836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are the only ones who can aquire a Mantle, correct? Mantles are &quot;Changeling&quot; merits, and as such wouldn't be valid to aquire via Borrowed Favor + Court Goodwill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantle is an alteration of a changeling's mien, which things that aren't fae don't have in the strict sense, hence why fetches, fae-touched, and non-changelings with Borrowed Favor use Court Goodwill instead of Mantle.<br /> <br /> Court Goodwill being more than a purely social construct means the court's patron still extends some mystical benefits to particularly dedicated characters, but until the level of Goodwill at which a changeling could learn outside Royal Contracts those benefits tend to amount to mundane dice bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:03:04-08:00","id":1504568,"title":"","content":"Supernatural population levels are generally kept vague by design, and individual Freeholds will vary by location, but is there a good rule-of-thumb number of Changelings per Freehold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:14:22-08:00","id":1504656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504568#post1504568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural population levels are generally kept vague by design, and individual Freeholds will vary by location, but is there a good rule-of-thumb number of Changelings per Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have one or more thumbs, a freehold has changelings in it.<br /> <br /> if you have no thumbs, I'm sorry how hard this all is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:29:20-08:00","id":1504659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504656#post1504656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have one or more thumbs, a freehold has changelings in it.<br /> <br /> if you have no thumbs, I'm sorry how hard this all is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While humorous, that's... not really helpful. For example, Mage Core has Tokyo being a relatively large Consilium with somewhere between 100 and 200 mages, with the upper limit depending on how the Arrow section is supposed to be read. And it's noted as being disproportionately densely populated with Mages, so it's fairly easy to extrapolate that to other areas.<br /> <br /> I'm much less versed in Changeling, so I dont know if there is a similar tidbit about how many Changelings you'd expect to find in the average city. I don't need a hard-and-fast answer, just a ballpark if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:38:18-08:00","id":1504661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504659#post1504659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While humorous, that's... not really helpful. For example, Mage Core has Tokyo being a relatively large Consilium with somewhere between 100 and 200 mages, with the upper limit depending on how the Arrow section is supposed to be read. And it's noted as being disproportionately densely populated with Mages, so it's fairly easy to extrapolate that to other areas.<br /> <br /> I'm much less versed in Changeling, so I dont know if there is a similar tidbit about how many Changelings you'd expect to find in the average city. I don't need a hard-and-fast answer, just a ballpark if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but the problem is that there's no real way to toss out a number except by feel. Olivia Hill figured those figures in the most populous city on the world is a pretty soild number, particularly since it has all six orders of the three sects in activity and a fair number of nameless orders on the side. <br /> <br /> I mean, you need a number, for very populous cities, 50 changelings per Court is a pretty decent number, particularly since you don't have to allot all of those <i>to</i> their respective Court, or even the freehold, but as a general rule, I prefer understanding populations as being particularly notable as either excessive, minimal, or appropriate for the location's population and leave it at the adjectival or adverbial level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T18:01:26-08:00","id":1504680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504661#post1504661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer understanding populations as being particularly notable as either excessive, minimal, or appropriate for the location's population and leave it at the adjectival or adverbial level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I don't even really have a sense of whether 4-5 changelings would qualify as &quot;minimal&quot;. <i>Mechanically,</i> there's nothing stopping a Freehold forming with only one rep per Bargain, and it <i>could</i> be a very interesting setting of being alone in the dark. It could even be a spliter off of a larger Freehold in the same area, for whatever reason, or just a Motley unaware of anyone else on &quot;their&quot; turf. But the fluff on Courts and Freeholds in general implies the populations are large enough to have traditions and/or prejudices -or even just their Bargains- passed down among them, which would be much harder to have achieved with such a small group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504661#post1504661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you need a number, for very populous cities, 50 changelings per Court is a pretty decent number, particularly since you don't have to allot all of those <i>to</i> their respective Court, or even the freehold</div> </div> </div> </div>Average of 50 Changelings per Court, 3-5 Courts per Freehold, 1-3 Freeholds per city, in a big city? Ok, those sound reasonable, I can extrapolate generalities from there. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T18:30:30-08:00","id":1504687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504680#post1504680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but I don't even really have a sense of whether 4-5 changelings would qualify as &quot;minimal&quot;. <i>Mechanically,</i> there's nothing stopping a Freehold forming with only one rep per Bargain, and it <i>could</i> be a very interesting setting of being alone in the dark. It could even be a spliter off of a larger Freehold in the same area, for whatever reason, or just a Motley unaware of anyone else on &quot;their&quot; turf. But the fluff on Courts and Freeholds in general implies the populations are large enough to have traditions and/or prejudices -or even just their Bargains- passed down among them, which would be much harder to have achieved with such a small group.</div> </div> </div> </div> A lot of those traditions and prejudices are things that are passed on or otherwise carried as the Court Bargain spreads geographically, and the truth of the matter is a lot of them are more guidelines than actual practices. Not every Winter Court* has the same Radio operation, or the appointed DJ role, and it'd be impossible for any Black Rose Court outside of Paris to have a dedicated executioner of the Severe (god, I need to finish updating the Rosiere).<br /> <br /> As for the sense of numerics, best I can say is that 5 changelings in Tokyo is a drop in the bucket**, but for 1,700 and change population of Enterprise, Utah, five'll make waves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Average of 50 Changelings per Court, 3-5 Courts per Freehold, 1-3 Freeholds per city, in a big city? Ok, those sound reasonable, I can extrapolate generalities from there. Thanks! </div> </div> </div>The foremost is a pretty usable number, 2 to 5 Courts per Freehold is part of the Freehold design in the books.<br /> <br /> 1 to 3 Freeholds in a city is......not typical? I'd say unless the setting conceit is built around the politics of two or more freeholds, I wouldn't assume it outside of the most populous cities in the world, and even there, the main example of that in Tokyo** is bad given it's not even the Tokyo Freehold. Most cities have the one freehold, relying on Courts for it's political intrigue.<br /> <br /> *Okay, bad example, given that the Unbidden Lords are textually one of the most globally coordinated Court groups out there, and other facets of Winter are thereore likely to also be more globally mandated, but still, not every Winter Court needs a radio DJ.<br /> **Also a bad reference, given that the Honshu Freehold is a) covering a whole damn island of Japan, and b) also Underhill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T20:30:44-08:00","id":1504716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504568#post1504568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural population levels are generally kept vague by design, and individual Freeholds will vary by location, but is there a good rule-of-thumb number of Changelings per Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assume a typical court in an average-size city has about enough people to fill out a school classroom (my general ballpark for local supernatural organizations is 20-60 monsters overall in a large population center like most cities this side of Manhattan). Assume motleys larger than half a dozen changelings are not particularly common, and assume the number of courts in a freehold does not have a significant influence on its total population. My quick-reference Dramatis Personae list for the Loop has a dozen characters in it split between the two courts, including local movers and shakers and the motley whose focal issue drove the first story, and I understand that as being a significant fraction of the population of that freehold, albeit not a majority.<br /> <br /> First Edition gave the general note that you get more changelings in places where people come and go regularly, for the simple reason that it's easier for people to go missing or show up unremarked-upon; Los Angeles is the largest freehold I've seen discussed, with about 400 changelings across four courts in the second largest city in the United States. Most freeholds are not going to be anything like that size, and the Lost's general longevity and predisposition toward formalization makes it not terribly hard for them to codify traditions even without a thematic pressure from courtly patrons to uphold a Bargain giving those traditions practical purpose. Freeholds are small communities in big host cities, and Chronicles does not typically use supernatural beings as throwaway characters in the context of the mortal world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T20:34:59-08:00","id":1504717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504716#post1504716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume a typical court in an average-size city has about enough people to fill out a school classroom (my general ballpark for local supernatural organizations is 20-60 monsters overall in a large population center like most cities this side of Manhattan). Assume motleys larger than half a dozen changelings are not particularly common, and assume the number of courts in a freehold does not have a significant influence on its total population. My quick-reference Dramatis Personae list for the Loop has a dozen characters in it split between the two courts, including local movers and shakers and the motley whose focal issue drove the first story, and I understand that as being a significant fraction of the population of that freehold, albeit not a majority.<br /> <br /> First Edition gave the general note that you get more changelings in places where people come and go regularly, for the simple reason that it's easier for people to go missing or show up unremarked-upon; Los Angeles is the largest freehold I've seen discussed, with about 400 changelings across four courts in the second largest city in the United States. Most freeholds are not going to be anything like that size, and the Lost's general longevity and predisposition toward formalization makes it not terribly hard for them to codify traditions even without a thematic pressure from courtly patrons to uphold a Bargain giving those traditions practical purpose. Freeholds are small communities in big host cities, and Chronicles does not typically use supernatural beings as throwaway characters in the context of the mortal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go into it more in my current held-hostage post, so I won't go on about, but [insert obligatory &quot;Honshu Freehold is largest freehold&quot; commentary here].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T01:44:02-08:00","id":1504736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504687#post1504687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Underhill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Underhill?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T02:35:11-08:00","id":1504738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504736#post1504736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underhill?</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been behind-the-scene upsets during development of Changeling 2nd. At first, Olivia Hill was the developer/writer, but those duties ended up with someone else, and her material remains unpublished. It's still available if you look for it, and the fandom nicknamed it as the Underhill version. It means &quot;Changeling under Olivia Hill&quot; and it also sounds like a name of a Hobbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T02:39:27-08:00","id":1504740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504738#post1504738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been behind-the-scene upsets during development of Changeling 2nd. At first, Olivia Hill was the developer/writer, but those duties ended up with someone else, and her material remains unpublished. It's still available if you look for it, and the fandom nicknamed it as the Underhill version. It means &quot;Changeling under Olivia Hill&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504738#post1504738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it also sounds like a name of a Hobbit.</div> </div> </div> </div> I come from under the hill, and under the hills and over the hills my paths led. And through the air, I am he that walks unseen.<br /> <br /> I am the clue-finder, the web-cutter, the stinging fly. I was chosen for the lucky number.<br /> <br /> I am he that buries his friends alive and drowns them and draws them alive again from the water. I came from the end of a bag, but no bag went over me.<br /> <br /> I am the friend of bears and the guest of eagles. I am Ringwinner and Luckwearer; and I am Barrel-rider.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T00:29:02-08:00","id":1504818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504738#post1504738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been behind-the-scene upsets during development of Changeling 2nd. At first, Olivia Hill was the developer/writer, but those duties ended up with someone else, and her material remains unpublished. It's still available if you look for it, and the fandom nicknamed it as the Underhill version. It means &quot;Changeling under Olivia Hill&quot; and it also sounds like a name of a Hobbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect to get credit for the name, much like Ironside, but I continue to be surprised no one makes the Tuatha de Danann/Sidhe connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T01:50:30-08:00","id":1504823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504818#post1504818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect to get credit for the name, much like Ironside, but I continue to be surprised no one makes the Tuatha de Danann/Sidhe connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspected it might be yours, but I wasn't sure. They're both good names. Still, since Frodo used the pseudonym of &quot;Underhill&quot; verbatim in possibly the most famed fantasy story of modern times, one that influenced many others, including D&amp;D and Warhammer, people's minds won't go &quot;I wonder if there are more obscure references beneath that&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T11:23:05-08:00","id":1504859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504568#post1504568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural population levels are generally kept vague by design, and individual Freeholds will vary by location, but is there a good rule-of-thumb number of Changelings per Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main bottleneck for a Changeling population is &quot;access to Arcadia,&quot; not anything correlating to human populations. I've picked out some quotes from Lords of Summer, a 1e supplement that covers courts and freeholds. Nothing I'm about to share has been contradicted by 2e sources, so this is probably as good a rule a thumb as any:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one knows how many changelings there are, and their numbers vary wildly by city. A very few cities, like Miami, are home to a hundred or more changelings. The Miami freehold contains slightly more than 100 changelings. Between them, the four Los Angeles freeholds may contain a total of more than 400 Lost \u2014 the largest number in an US city \u2014 and before Hurricane Katrina, the New Orleans freehold contained almost 90 changelings.\u200b<br /> <br /> The reason for these high concentrations of changelings is largely that the paths between Arcadia and these cities and others like them are in some way easier or shorter than those between Arcadia and most locations. Unfortunately, these paths also go both ways, and so the fae are more likely to visit these same cities. The connections between these cities and Arcadia are also not always static. Occasionally there are unusual events that result a dozen or sometimes as many as a hundred changelings successfully escaping Arcadia and all ending up in the same location in the mortal world at the same time, typically a location in or near a city that already has an unusual number of paths leading from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Some supernatural event or supernatural reflection of a mundane event creates a multitude of short-lived paths between Arcadia and a specific location. Oddly, the individuals who escape via these paths do not all escape from Arcadia together and often come from different decades. Some changelings assume that these escapees may have left Arcadia years or even decades apart, but all made it back to the mortal world together, because some event briefly made the paths from Arcadia to one specific location easier and faster to traverse. The mystics of the Lost work diligently to understand whether some celestial conjunction, calendar numerology, or other cycle is at work in these conditions.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, it is definitely true that the freeholds of the early 21st century are seeing a population boom because an unusual number of changelings have recently escaped. It strains freehold resources a bit to accommodate the growing numbers, but most find it a small price to pay for the greater number of Lost enjoying new freedom.<br /> <br /> Unlike the numbers of some supernatural beings, like vampires, changeling populations have no direct correlation to mortal populations. Changelings aren\u2019t predatory and don\u2019t need a certain number of humans to \u201csupport\u201d them. The Mask also aids larger populations of Lost to remain concealed. In some large cities, there are either no changelings at all or no more than one or two small motleys. Most cities possess only difficult access to Arcadia and so a much smaller number of changelings make it back to these cities. In many cities, there are as few as one changeling for every 500,000 mortal inhabitants. Despite being the largest city in the United States, New York City has a single small freehold with only 37 members. Similarly, in the entire greater Chicago metropolitan area, there are only 21 changelings. It\u2019s said that few changelings escape to rural areas or small towns. Also, the Lost wish to remain inconspicuous and hide amidst the mass of humanity, not stand out as the few eccentrics in a small town. As a result, very few small towns or rural areas contain enough changelings to form a freehold. Cities usually need a population of more\u200b than 20,000 before they are likely to become home to even a single motley. That said, there are certainly rural freeholds here and there, in strange communities where strange stories circulate. Peculiar things walk down dirt roads, and sometimes the distracted weather-beaten old men watching you from the hardware store\u2019s porch are something else entirely under the Mask.<br /> <br /> Many changelings speculate about why some cities are so much easier for changelings to escape to. The most common theory is that large-scale mortal migrations and more specifically the dreams of the many thousands of mortals who have recently arrived in a new location somehow creates or strengthens paths to and from Arcadia, or create beacons for the Lost. Ports filled with immigrants tend to have more changelings, while cities that see little shift in their population also see fewer changelings on average. Between 1900 &amp; the late 1920s, New York City had two large and thriving freeholds containing between them more than 200 changelings. Most notably, these factors seem to affect changelings who weren\u2019t previously residents of a city \u2014 those who find their way through the Thorns, but not to the exact place they remembered growing up.<br /> <br /> Cities that are growing rapidly also seem to be easier for non-native changelings to get to, just as cities that are losing population can be more difficult for changelings escaping from Arcadia to find. However, mortal immigration is not the only reason a place becomes open to changelings, and it certainly doesn\u2019t tell the whole story. A growing city erodes away many of its landmarks, which may make it more difficult for once-residents to find their way home through the Thorns. Although New York is less of a center for immigration than it once was, many mortal immigrants still come there and yet far fewer changelings arrive there today than did so 80 years before. Ultimately, no one fully understands why escaping from Arcadia to some cities is so much easier and more common than escaping to others. However, at least some of the reason is a combination of the number of immigrants to a city, how rapidly the city is growing and the number and power of the myths and legends people tell about that city. These factors seem to have the most influence over the arrival of changelings who weren\u2019t native to a given city in the first place.\u200b </div> </div> </div>From this we can glean a few things:<ul><li>Changeling populations fluctuate wildly, and will depend entirely on your needs as a Storyteller.</li> <li>Freeholds that have numbers of members in the triple-digits are rare, and cities with more than a hundred changelings often have multiple separate Freeholds.The ballpark for a Freehold seems to be between 20 to 100 members before it starts getting unwieldy enough to break into two or more Freeholds.</li> <li>The main justification for freehold size is mystical in nature, rather than anything correlating to human population numbers. If you want to justify large Freeholds, then the best way of going about that is including some sort of mystical event in your lore.</li> <li>Freeholds tend to be Urban, rather than Rural.</li> <li>Changelings might find their way to cities other than those they remember, or may have traveled to a Freehold away from a location that doesn't have one.</li> <li>Freehold sizes can change drastically over time, if you need them to.</li> <li>One Changeling per 500,000 mortals seems to be a ballpark number for areas without strong ties to Arcadia.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T13:51:17-08:00","id":1504871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1504859#post1504859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From this we can glean a few things:<ul><li>Changeling populations fluctuate wildly, and will depend entirely on your needs as a Storyteller.</li> <li>Freeholds that have numbers of members in the triple-digits are rare, and cities with more than a hundred changelings often have multiple separate Freeholds.The ballpark for a Freehold seems to be between 20 to 100 members before it starts getting unwieldy enough to break into two or more Freeholds.</li> <li>The main justification for freehold size is mystical in nature, rather than anything correlating to human population numbers. If you want to justify large Freeholds, then the best way of going about that is including some sort of mystical event in your lore.</li> <li>Freeholds tend to be Urban, rather than Rural.</li> <li>Changelings might find their way to cities other than those they remember, or may have traveled to a Freehold away from a location that doesn't have one.</li> <li>Freehold sizes can change drastically over time, if you need them to.</li> <li>One Changeling per 500,000 mortals seems to be a ballpark number for areas without strong ties to Arcadia.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, this helps immensely. Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T12:19:55-07:00","id":1507776,"title":"","content":"Can Glamour be harvested from non-humans: animals, ephemeral entities, cryptids, other supernaturals, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T12:33:57-07:00","id":1507779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1507776#post1507776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Glamour be harvested from non-humans: animals, ephemeral entities, cryptids, other supernaturals, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>It says in the first paragraph of the &quot;Harvesting Glamour&quot; section on page 103 that Glamour can be harvested from any non-fae intelligent being with emotions. It says in the third-from-last paragraph of that same section that it can't be harvested from animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T09:12:32-07:00","id":1507868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1507779#post1507779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says in the first paragraph of the &quot;Harvesting Glamour&quot; section on page 103 that Glamour can be harvested from any non-fae intelligent being with emotions. It says in the third-from-last paragraph of that same section that it can't be harvested from animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I have lost access to my files and I wasnt sure.<br /> <br /> Another question, is there any way to block Glamour harvesting / reaping? Will a Mage's Mental Shield work against it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T09:36:09-07:00","id":1507872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1507868#post1507868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, is there any way to block Glamour harvesting / reaping? Will a Mage's Mental Shield work against it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing published in Changeling so far, possibly because harvesting is an Attribute + Skill roll that requires strong emotions and is penalized by attempts to do it quickly.<br /> <br /> Given that Glamour is derived from emotions rather than being a thing non-fae people have themselves, I don't think Mental Shield would stop harvesting from working any more than a Life Shielding spell would stop a vampire from making Vitae out of your blood. Clear Thoughts could suppress a few types of strong emotion such that it would probably at least prompt a Clash with attempts to reap or harvest from them if not stopping it from working altogether on those emotion, but you don't generally &quot;block&quot; harvesting any more than you &quot;block&quot; someone gaining sustenance from food \u2014 the way you stop them from benefiting is by stopping them from doing the thing they do to get the benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T21:50:08-07:00","id":1508991,"title":"","content":"So, what happens if a Changeling doesn't play their assigned role in a Bastion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T11:01:50-07:00","id":1509217,"title":"","content":"Hey, what happens if a normal human is kidnapped from their Bastion? Can they just wake up, or is their body left in a coma until they can return to the Bastion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T19:42:25-07:00","id":1509247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1509217#post1509217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, what happens if a normal human is kidnapped from their Bastion? Can they just wake up, or is their body left in a coma until they can return to the Bastion?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it works anything like for lucid dreamers, as long as they haven't left the bounds of the Dreaming Roads they should be able to wake up normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T18:42:10-07:00","id":1509334,"title":"","content":"What seeming and kith would a knight or a samurai be? Note i am talking about 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T19:31:36-07:00","id":1509339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1509334#post1509334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What seeming and kith would a knight or a samurai be? Note i am talking about 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I imagine that most of such \u2018noble\u2019 roles would be taken by the Gentry themselves, and changelings be relegated to squires and lovers\u2026 In that vein, we could have Chatelaines, Playmates, and even Notaries who took up knighthood only after their escape.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could have been made into killers and marauders in armor, historical brutality ramped up to eleven by Faerie. Such changelings could be Hunterhearts, Gristlegrinders, and Draconics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T21:22:55-07:00","id":1509442,"title":"","content":"A True Fae hides a Huntsman's heart inside a mortal's bastion to send it into the mortal world, but... what happens when the mortal wakes up? Do they not, and just remain comatose? Does the heart move to another dream? Does the Huntsman only exist when the mortal sleeps? Does a heart infested Bastion somehow persist during the mortal's waking hours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T22:17:07-07:00","id":1509446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1509442#post1509442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A True Fae hides a Huntsman's heart inside a mortal's bastion to send it into the mortal world, but... what happens when the mortal wakes up? Do they not, and just remain comatose? Does the heart move to another dream? Does the Huntsman only exist when the mortal sleeps? Does a heart infested Bastion somehow persist during the mortal's waking hours?</div> </div> </div> </div>The heart is there when the mortal dreams and inaccessible otherwise, just like their childhood traumas or their fondest memories don't cease to exist when they wake up.<br /> <br /> A given mortal's Bastion doesn't have a consistent location on the Dreaming Roads, and the way Hedge navigation works means the Huntsmen having a specific block against being able to track down their hearts is as simple as not being able to use that paradigm shift to find their way to the right Road, whereupon the Huntsman's presence being a Key to the Bastion should suffice for narrowing it down further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T16:18:23-07:00","id":1510283,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a changeling to become True Fae? From the book\u2019s explanation of how a changeling can take a True Fae\u2019s Title I feel like it\u2019s totally possible. (PS I have a chronicle idea that hinges on whether or not I can do this w/ a specific NPC)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T16:19:10-07:00","id":1510284,"title":"","content":"1e had it as a possible endgame outcome. I don't think 2e has pursued that path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T18:13:11-07:00","id":1510300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1510283#post1510283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a changeling to become True Fae? From the book\u2019s explanation of how a changeling can take a True Fae\u2019s Title I feel like it\u2019s totally possible. (PS I have a chronicle idea that hinges on whether or not I can do this w/ a specific NPC)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Equinox Road has a mechanic in a section titled Becoming Nightmare that allows for play groups to explore that as an option. Second Edition has not addressed this notion, but the Becoming Nightmare mechanic is easy to port over if you want to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:22:45-07:00","id":1510363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1510300#post1510300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Equinox Road has a mechanic in a section titled Becoming Nightmare that allows for play groups to explore that as an option. Second Edition has not addressed this notion, but the Becoming Nightmare mechanic is easy to port over if you want to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I will definitely check that out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T07:04:23-07:00","id":1510702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huntsmen do not suffer the frailties of other fae creatures, which is one reason the Gentry risk sending their Titles into the world this way. - page 265 </div> </div> </div>Do huntsman have frailties (taboos and banes, excluding iron)? I saw that Reighnhell made them have frailties, and I always found that they're more interesting if they do, but I wanted an outside opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T10:54:30-07:00","id":1510711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super Vlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1510702#post1510702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do huntsman have frailties (taboos and banes, excluding iron)? I saw that Reighnhell made them have frailties, and I always found that they're more interesting if they do, but I wanted an outside opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per page 265 of the core book, they do not;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huntsmen do not suffer the frailties of other fae creatures[...] </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:14:04-07:00","id":1511002,"title":"","content":"<b>What are the limits on the information provided by the &quot;Book of Things Strange and Wondrous&quot; (2ed Core Book p. 226)?</b><br /> <br /> Seems from the item description that is the information that is written somewhere (libraries, document repositories, etc) because the result from extraordinary success is &quot;<i>more details, including things not written down elsewhere\u200b</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> IF this interpretation is correct, this is likely to be the strongest Token of them all, since you can find any information in that exists in a document as long as you roll right, even if it is not written but you get an extraordinary success, you know it.<br /> <br /> A government register has the names, addresses, bank accounts, peccadilloes of someone? Lost library item? Secret name of a mage? The things that the vampire court has hidden for centuries?<br /> <br /> If you boost your rolls for the extraordinary success (and have enough Glamour to activate the item), then you are the most knowledgeable person in the world, about any topic.<br /> <br /> How is this not rated at 5 dots? Or am I missing something on how it is used and what it can provide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T13:31:08-07:00","id":1511015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511002#post1511002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What are the limits on the information provided by the &quot;Book of Things Strange and Wondrous&quot; (2ed Core Book p. 226)?</b><br /> <br /> Seems from the item description that is the information that is written somewhere (libraries, document repositories, etc) because the result from extraordinary success is &quot;<i>more details, including things not written down elsewhere\u200b</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> IF this interpretation is correct, this is likely to be the strongest Token of them all, since you can find any information in that exists in a document as long as you roll right, even if it is not written but you get an extraordinary success, you know it.<br /> <br /> A government register has the names, addresses, bank accounts, peccadilloes of someone? Lost library item? Secret name of a mage? The things that the vampire court has hidden for centuries?<br /> <br /> If you boost your rolls for the extraordinary success (and have enough Glamour to activate the item), then you are the most knowledgeable person in the world, about any topic.<br /> <br /> How is this not rated at 5 dots? Or am I missing something on how it is used and what it can provide?</div> </div> </div> </div>The roll is Intelligence + a relevant Mental Skill and you have entirely invented the explanation of &quot;the information exists in a document somewhere. The two examples of information an exceptional success can give you are semi-architectural details of a deserted building and the Title of a True Fae, and the description of the token's mien combined with its effect being to provide <i>knowledge</i> of the sort you can't just hit the library or phone a friend for, indicate that this is not &quot;learn any and all information in the universe.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a fairy search engine that shares all your inquiries with the next person who uses it, and you don't become &quot;the most knowledgeable person in the world&quot; from having access to Google. This is a game where there's markets that allow you to get just about anything for the right price, and the primary type of supernatural real estate penalizes rolls to find information about its owner while they're at home \u2014 being able to dig up dirt on conspiratorial monsters or access trivia at the cost of needing to be very secure about where and how you're keeping your reference book safe is not legendary-item territory, least of all when it requires a roll that any hobgoblin can take dice off of just by being at home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T15:10:26-07:00","id":1511568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511015#post1511015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The roll is Intelligence + a relevant Mental Skill and <b>you have entirely invented the explanation of &quot;the information exists in a document somewhere</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, but I gave a rationale of why I thought so, and I clearly stated that the this was a question. First sentence on the third paragraph, bolded and underlined for your convenience <b><u>IF this interpretation is correct.</u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511015#post1511015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two examples of information an exceptional success can give you are semi-architectural details of a deserted building and the Title of a True Fae, and the description of the token's mien combined with its effect being to provide <i>knowledge</i> of the sort you can't just hit the library or phone a friend for, indicate that this is not &quot;learn any and all information in the universe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but what are the limits of the book? What difference is there between having the Title of a True Fae and the secrets of the Invictus leader? Or the birth name of a mage? I am copying from the book and it does seem to be ANY information in the universe, as per the item effect description:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Should the user succeed, he gains the knowledge<br /> he sought, about any topic he chooses</b>. On an exceptional<br /> success, he <b>gains the Informed Condition regarding the<br /> subject and learns more details, including things not writ-<br /> ten down elsewhere</b>\u200b...<br /> <br /> <br /> Gains the knowledge sought about any topic IS the definition of any information. What am I missing? You say no, but do not provide a counterexample or a stated limitation. As it is written, you roll Intelligence + Mental skill and if you get 3 successes you are REALLY well informed on the topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511015#post1511015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fairy search engine that shares all your inquiries with the next person who uses it, and you don't become &quot;the most knowledgeable person in the world&quot; from having access to Google. This is a game where there's markets that allow you to get just about anything for the right price, and the primary type of supernatural real estate penalizes rolls to find information about its owner while they're at home \u2014 <b>being able to dig up dirt on conspiratorial monsters or access trivia</b> at the cost of needing to be very secure about where and how you're keeping your reference book safe is not legendary-item territory, least of all when it requires a roll that any hobgoblin can take dice off of just by being at home.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded my peeve, it <u>seems</u> that is not limited to trivia, that is the whole point I am trying to get across. And value is relative, a mage with Fate + Mind can generate Glamour, and try to activate it somehow... Or Prime 1 + Fate 1 plus some mana (Word of Command spell), for mages a device that gives hidden accurate information is not the Holy Grail, but right up in the priority list.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T19:39:44-07:00","id":1511577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511568#post1511568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but what are the limits of the book? What difference is there between having the Title of a True Fae and the secrets of the Invictus leader? Or the birth name of a mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would ask you to seriously think about what the difference is between &quot;what is the name of the consistently-manifested thematic portfolio a godlike being from another dimension used to kidnap your friend?&quot; and &quot;What are the secrets of a powerful vampire or the name a mage could use to make sympathetic magic against another mage easier?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gains the knowledge sought about any topic IS the definition of any information. What am I missing? You say no, but do not provide a counterexample or a stated limitation. </div> </div> </div>Right. You have the book. Everyone on these forums who has the book except the writers and people who have access to the writers has the same information as you do. If you know this then you are coming here for an interpretation, not a citation, and I am not interested in trying to produce a citation that does not exist, much less arguing interpretations in a thread for simple questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it is written, you roll Intelligence + Mental skill and if you get 3 successes you are REALLY well informed on the topic. </div> </div> </div>Yes. Mental Skills. The Skills corresponding to Academics, Computers, Crafts, Investigation, Medicine, the Occult, Politics, and Science, which subtract three dice from the roll if you have no dots in them and which using the token rolls a <i>relevant</i> Skill. You are getting information couched in stuff the Wyrd is telling you through a big grimoire full of dead languages and strange drawings. It's far from useless, but this is pretty definitely in the same neck of the woods as Common Sense and other &quot;ask questions from this list&quot; Merits, as modeled with &quot;let's take a look in the Big Book Of Everything&quot; with the primary throttle being that if you use it for free you'd best hope nobody finds out what for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bolded my peeve, it <u>seems</u> that is not limited to trivia, that is the whole point I am trying to get across. </div> </div> </div>Friend, if you're going to get catty about how you are read it does not then do to ignore the fact that there was an &quot;or&quot; before &quot;access trivia&quot; in my sentence about the things this two-dot token allows you to find out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And value is relative, a mage with Fate + Mind can generate Glamour, and try to activate it somehow... Or Prime 1 + Fate 1 plus some mana (Word of Command spell), for mages a device that gives hidden accurate information is not the Holy Grail, but right up in the priority list. </div> </div> </div>Any vampire in the Invictus with two dots of Status in the covenant is able to buy a two-dot Merit that allows them to access sensitive information about any vampire whose name and affiliation you know without a roll at least twice per story. Any Prelate of the Panopticon Ministry more invested than the level of &quot;you can use Patron Yantras without complications&quot; can target sympathetic magic at anyone they can produce a sketch of in addition to cutting past half of the normal maximum defenses of Occultation.<br /> <br /> Changeling was not written under the assumption that mages would be the primary concerned users of tokens, producing Glamour with Awakened magic requires a character to be a double Adept in two Subtle Arcana, and this is pretty definitely not the same sort of situation as required Words of Truth to have caveats added to its use requirements to prevent characters from fishing for objective truths about the setting by saying things to random people. The token's limits are not strictly delineated in writing and mages with sufficient Arcana can get up to some silly nonsense; you will have to make your peace with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T10:52:33-07:00","id":1511814,"title":"","content":"For Shadow Puppet from Kith and Kin, it notes the puppet &quot;may act in an action scene, taking the character's turn and acting on his Initiative&quot;. I'm not sure if that means that the Changeling's turn is effectively given to the puppet, or if they simply act at the same time. Any interpretations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T19:06:44-07:00","id":1511838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511814#post1511814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Shadow Puppet from Kith and Kin, it notes the puppet &quot;may act in an action scene, taking the character's turn and acting on his Initiative&quot;. I'm not sure if that means that the Changeling's turn is effectively given to the puppet, or if they simply act at the same time. Any interpretations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former; the line immediately preceding the quoted note says that it follows the changeling's instructions, and the puppet possesses a basic intelligence and counts as a Retainer with a rating equal to half the changeling's Wyrd with an area of expertise chosen from one of their Specialties, plus a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> This being a Common Contract that fashions some or all of your shadow into a servant for a scene, it seems reasonable enough that in scenes where the timing of what is happening from second to second matters you don't get the same sort of independent actor by doing a puppet show for a couple minutes as you'd get from doing a favor for a houseplant to create a negligibly strong/smart/charismatic assistant with decent Finesse and no magic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T19:08:55-07:00","id":1511953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511838#post1511838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former; the line immediately preceding the quoted note says that it follows the changeling's instructions, and the puppet possesses a basic intelligence and counts as a Retainer with a rating equal to half the changeling's Wyrd with an area of expertise chosen from one of their Specialties, plus a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> This being a Common Contract that fashions some or all of your shadow into a servant for a scene, it seems reasonable enough that in scenes where the timing of what is happening from second to second matters you don't get the same sort of independent actor by doing a puppet show for a couple minutes as you'd get from doing a favor for a houseplant to create a negligibly strong/smart/charismatic assistant with decent Finesse and no magic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very reasonable. I was leaning towards the former interpretation myself, but I just wanted to be sure. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:25:51-07:00","id":1512072,"title":"","content":"Did they add new clauses to the Contracts in the revised versions for more variety? Such as Darkness, Fang &amp; Talon or Smoke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:36:41-07:00","id":1512074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1512072#post1512072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they add new clauses to the Contracts in the revised versions for more variety? Such as Darkness, Fang &amp; Talon or Smoke?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the examples you wrote in the last sentence, I assume you come from 1e? 2e\u2019s Contracts are organized very differently. Where 1e Contracts were like Disciplines (any Vampire), 2e\u2019s are organized more like Gifts from Apocalypse; you have a few broad fairy-tale-ish themes, and Contracts are spread across. (Only two tiers of power in each theme, though, not 1-5 dot ratings)<br /> <br /> In any case; yes it\u2019s more variable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:43:37-07:00","id":1512076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1512072#post1512072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they add new clauses to the Contracts in the revised versions for more variety? Such as Darkness, Fang &amp; Talon or Smoke?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Second Edition, the organization of contracts is entirely changed. Instead of themed Contract categories consisting of five sequential clause powers of increasing strength, there are themed Regalia categories consisting of weaker Common Contract powers and stronger Royal Contract powers, without any required order to them. There are fewer 2e Regalia than there were 1e Contracts, but they are broader defined and more powers available within each. For instance, the Mirror Regalia's purview isn't just mirrors but perception and changing forms. It contains not only powers to see through mirrors, but to glimpse the past or future, talk to inanimate objects, or take the shape of objects or people.<br /> <br /> Catches still exist (now called loopholes, but largely the same concept), and each contract now also has expanded powers available to characters of a given seeming who use it (though you can set out to learn a different seeming's contract benefit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T01:53:14-07:00","id":1512264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1511002#post1511002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What are the limits on the information provided by the &quot;Book of Things Strange and Wondrous&quot; (2ed Core Book p. 226)?</b><br /> <br /> Seems from the item description that is the information that is written somewhere (libraries, document repositories, etc) because the result from extraordinary success is &quot;<i>more details, including things not written down elsewhere\u200b</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> IF this interpretation is correct, this is likely to be the strongest Token of them all, since you can find any information in that exists in a document as long as you roll right, even if it is not written but you get an extraordinary success, you know it.<br /> <br /> A government register has the names, addresses, bank accounts, peccadilloes of someone? Lost library item? Secret name of a mage? The things that the vampire court has hidden for centuries?<br /> <br /> If you boost your rolls for the extraordinary success (and have enough Glamour to activate the item), then you are the most knowledgeable person in the world, about any topic.<br /> <br /> How is this not rated at 5 dots? Or am I missing something on how it is used and what it can provide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having had one of these in-game, here's how I saw it:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The book knows what information you asked it for. It does not know <i>why</i> you want it, so the answer it provides is based solely on the effectiveness of the inquiry made, and the answer it provides may be missing crucial context. It can tell you exactly what you asked to know, no more, no less. Picture how looking up stuff on Google or Wikipedia works, and interpret that through the lens of an artifact manufactured by the Fae. How would you have a Hobgoblin who knew the thing they asked about and an obligation to give them an honest answer respond? <i>That's</i> how the book should dispense its information.</li> <li>The major benefit of using the Book is to get answers that help you start asking better questions. I'm generally a fan of the <a href=\"https://thealexandrian.net/wordpress/1118/roleplaying-games/three-clue-rule\" target=\"_blank\">Three-Clue Rule</a> when constructing mysteries for RPG games, and The Book of Things Strange And Wondrous is merely another tool in the PC's arsenal to give out clues -- but hey, so is a phone with an internet connection. Hiding information from players is usually a great way to bring your game to a screeching halt -- the book is immensely helpful for getting unstuck.</li> <li>The book provides answers about a topic. It does <i>not</i> provide information about how best to apply/exploit said knowledge for maximal gain, because, as mentioned, the book only looks up what it's told to look up, and how it presents the information can influence a lot. It's also up to the reader to actually <i>parse</i> the information being given to them -- the book is under no obligation to dispense its content in a dry, matter-of-fact manner. Again, picture how you'd have a Hobgoblin NPC answer the same question.</li> <li>Does the Book have an agenda (either from the creator of it or as an active sentience)? Then the answers it provides will be biased around that agenda. (Did you know that <a href=\"https://dhmo.org/facts.html\" target=\"_blank\">Dihydrogen Monoxide</a> is a constituent of many known toxic substances, diseases and disease-causing agents, environmental hazards and can even be lethal to humans in quantities as small as a thimbleful? Sounds really scary, unless you know that DHMO is just a fancy term for water). You can throw in all manner of Technical Truths, False Reassurances, or Specifically Suspicious Denials to shape what info the PCs learn, if you decide that the Book has some Aspiration it's trying to fulfill. The Book absolutely <i>should not</i> be treated as a perfectly truthful, unbiased, or neutral information source. It's Faerie Wikipedia and should be treated as such.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T07:05:08-07:00","id":1513070,"title":"","content":"Can the Asclepian's Grafting kith blessing actually remove damage and if yes, how much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T08:20:08-07:00","id":1513077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513070#post1513070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Asclepian's Grafting kith blessing actually remove damage and if yes, how much?</div> </div> </div> </div>It explicitly says it can heal injuries and the rules for healing damage with the Medicine Skill are in the corebook on page 188.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T23:50:24-07:00","id":1513168,"title":"","content":"Does the Mask cover the obviously supernatural effects of Contracts, or are they plainly visible to anyone involved? I'm in a discussion with someone who could swear they read it does, but they cannot find the passage that states it and I cannot remember that being the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T00:40:36-07:00","id":1513172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513168#post1513168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Mask cover the obviously supernatural effects of Contracts, or are they plainly visible to anyone involved? I'm in a discussion with someone who could swear they read it does, but they cannot find the passage that states it and I cannot remember that being the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 107 of the book implies that all fae magic is hidden behind the mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T15:11:34-07:00","id":1513239,"title":"","content":"Do you need to have a Wyrd trait to benefit from Goblin fruits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T15:40:09-07:00","id":1513242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513239#post1513239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to have a Wyrd trait to benefit from Goblin fruits?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e specified that goblin fruits only provide their benefits to changelings and the True Fae, and the only specified changed in that regard in 2e so far are that Huntsmen, Hedge ghosts, and hobgoblins list them as a source of Glamour in their respective writeups. 2e likewise specifies that a character's Wyrd score affects how many goblin fruits they can keep outside of the Hedge, with the excess rotting away, though it lacks 1e's three-day preservation lead and explicitly says that unless a type of goblin fruit specifically spoils it won't go bad otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T18:08:16-07:00","id":1513253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513242#post1513242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1e specified that goblin fruits only provide their benefits to changelings and the True Fae, and the only specified changed in that regard in 2e so far are that Huntsmen, Hedge ghosts, and hobgoblins list them as a source of Glamour in their respective writeups. </b>2e likewise specifies that a character's Wyrd score affects how many goblin fruits they can keep outside of the Hedge, with the excess rotting away, though it lacks 1e's three-day preservation lead and explicitly says that unless a type of goblin fruit specifically spoils it won't go bad otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> Assuming a human is inside the hedge, would they be able to get nutrition from the fruits? Benefits from that fruit that heals damage? I bolded the part that makes me doubt because in 2ed AFAIK (I dont have the books with me right now) nothing states that the nutrition or non-Glamour benefits are only for Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Editing. 05-29-2023, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T18:35:47-07:00","id":1513254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513253#post1513253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> Assuming a human is inside the hedge, would they be able to get nutrition from the fruits? Benefits from that fruit that heals damage? I bolded the part that makes me doubt because in 2ed AFAIK (I dont have the books with me right now) nothing states that the nutrition or non-Glamour benefits are only for Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general assumption is that if you're a non-fae in the Hedge and you don't manage to get ahold of food that isn't goblin fruit, after a certain point you either die, get out, or go native.<br /> <br /> Worth remembering that not everything that lives and grows in the Hedge is goblin fruit, as evidenced by the fact that they're listed separately from &quot;food&quot; in the set of things the Hedge Sense Merit helps you find there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T06:03:32-07:00","id":1513283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513254#post1513254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general assumption is that if you're a non-fae in the Hedge and you don't manage to get ahold of food that isn't goblin fruit, after a certain point you either die, get out, or go native.<br /> <br /> Worth remembering that not everything that lives and grows in the Hedge is goblin fruit, as evidenced by the fact that they're listed separately from &quot;food&quot; in the set of things the Hedge Sense Merit helps you find there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks again.<br /> <br /> Would a <b>Hollow </b>with the <b>Luxury Goods </b>option provide food nutritive enough for non-fae?<br /> <br /> Essentially what is &quot;mundane supplies&quot; that the option refers? Non edible stuff only?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T18:05:26-07:00","id":1513347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513283#post1513283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially what is &quot;mundane supplies&quot; that the option refers? Non edible stuff only?</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples specifically include a type of beverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:46:28-07:00","id":1513769,"title":"","content":"Is it normal to indulge in hedge spinning whilst travelling in the Hedge? Or is it best for scenes between navigating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27092-satbunny","name":"satbunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T08:07:34-07:00","id":1513774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satbunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1513769#post1513769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it normal to indulge in hedge spinning whilst travelling in the Hedge? Or is it best for scenes between navigating?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use Hedge navigation rolls for Hedgespinning, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T20:28:51-07:00","id":1514073,"title":"","content":"How much different from an human can a changeling be? Like, can a changeling have more than 2 arms and 2 legs? Or have no legs and a snake tail instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T21:01:09-07:00","id":1514075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1514073#post1514073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much different from an human can a changeling be? Like, can a changeling have more than 2 arms and 2 legs? Or have no legs and a snake tail instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming 1e material from Equinox Road still holds mostly true, things can get increasingly nonstandard at higher Wyrd. By the opposite token, at low Wyrd the overt magical reminders of your Durance are usually comparably minor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:21:34-07:00","id":1514088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1514073#post1514073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much different from an human can a changeling be? Like, can a changeling have more than 2 arms and 2 legs? Or have no legs and a snake tail instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be a lost opportunity not to be able to make really weird changelings in a game about fantastical fairy tales. But if you want any mechanical effects you'd better make it in the form of Merits (like Lethal Mien, or Fleet of Foot for a quadripedal changeling). Or persistent Conditions if it's detrimental instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:03:13-07:00","id":1516782,"title":"","content":"Can you reforce your Mask in the Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T14:45:03-07:00","id":1516826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1516782#post1516782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you reforce your Mask in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The Mask doesn't exist in the Hedge, at least not in a form changelings can make use of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T05:27:27-07:00","id":1517265,"title":"","content":"My question is with regards to the summer mantle. Does a &quot;fae threat&quot; have to be explicitly fae itself or can it be a non-fae acting on the behalf of the fae. <br /> <br /> To me, if the threat has to be explicitly fae in origin then they could have just said &quot;against the fae&quot; and left the word threat off. After all, you're in combat, that's inherently threatening. To me, the use of fae as an adjective rather than a noun was intentional and indicates a wider variety of foes than fae as a noun would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T06:18:16-07:00","id":1517271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1517265#post1517265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is with regards to the summer mantle. Does a &quot;fae threat&quot; have to be explicitly fae itself or can it be a non-fae acting on the behalf of the fae.<br /> <br /> To me, if the threat has to be explicitly fae in origin then they could have just said &quot;against the fae&quot; and left the word threat off. After all, you're in combat, that's inherently threatening. To me, the use of fae as an adjective rather than a noun was intentional and indicates a wider variety of foes than fae as a noun would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I wouldn't allow a changeling character to resolve the Addicted, Broken, Fugue, or Madness Conditions by exceptionally succeeding at contesting a Discipline from a vampire who happened to be working for a loyalist because that is definitionally not a &quot;fae power,&quot; I would not count things that aren't changelings or otherwise coming from the Hedge and beyond as &quot;fae threats&quot; \u2014 the Fae may sometimes use patsies and catspaws, but changelings don't talk about the Wild Hunt in terms of loyalists and Huntsmen pointing Reapers and Pure in their direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T16:13:50-07:00","id":1517316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1517265#post1517265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is with regards to the summer mantle. Does a &quot;fae threat&quot; have to be explicitly fae itself or can it be a non-fae acting on the behalf of the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interpret &quot;threat&quot; locally. What's the actual immediate threat you're using the Mantle to defend against? If a fae creature wields a mundane sword and swings it, the threat isn't the sword, it's that somebody is swinging it at you, and that somebody is fae: apply Mantle. If a fae creature hires a mortal assassin to shoot you with a gun, the threat is that somebody is trying to shoot you, and that somebody is not fae: don't apply Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T12:11:42-07:00","id":1518263,"title":"","content":"The Court Goodwill Merit gives some of a Mantle's <i>effects</i>, but isn't the Mantle in full. It's just a form of Dramaturgy bringing the Changeling in to the outermost edge of that Bargain. I assume then that it doesn't add that Mantle's composite changes to the Changeling's Mien, correct? A Crystal Web Courtier with Court Goodwill in the House of In isn't going to start sprouting a tapestry-cape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-18-2023, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T20:28:32-07:00","id":1518677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1518263#post1518263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Court Goodwill Merit gives some of a Mantle's <i>effects</i>, but isn't the Mantle in full. It's just a form of Dramaturgy bringing the Changeling in to the outermost edge of that Bargain. I assume then that it doesn't add that Mantle's composite changes to the Changeling's Mien, correct? A Crystal Web Courtier with Court Goodwill in the House of In isn't going to start sprouting a tapestry-cape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, albeit learning the Contracts of a court's patron has symbolic effects on your mien regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T17:26:06-07:00","id":1520245,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has already been brought up, but here's a thought: why do the True Fae need mortals to change them into something, when they can simply create servants out of straws and hays like Fetches and they can pick up Hobgoblins to mess with as they are the closest things from the Hedge rather than from Earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T17:57:03-07:00","id":1520248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1520245#post1520245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has already been brought up, but here's a thought: why do the True Fae need mortals to change them into something, when they can simply create servants out of straws and hays like Fetches and they can pick up Hobgoblins to mess with as they are the closest things from the Hedge rather than from Earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume the act of seizing a creature from a faraway world to turn into a slave or a bauble or a heating element is something done for practical purposes. They do it because they can and they said they would.<br /> <br /> Why does the billionaire cut sections of centuries-old Persian rug to carpet his yacht when he can afford the most expensive store-bought flooring money can buy? Why does the exotic pet trade exist when pet stores sell dogs, cats, birds, lizards, and rodents in ample variety? Why did Renaissance patrons fund Michelangelo and the rest when they could more cheaply pay to get some paint slapped on a canvas or a chisel hucked into some stone?<br /> <br /> Fetches aren't created and maintained in a vacuum, and hobgoblins are cheap pickings for those Fae who just want something to serve a function. As a group, the Fae want the entire world, and the Wyrd is the signing bonus they received for having sworn to make it theirs. For some of them, that means they want mortal souls to decorate their ballrooms or dig their ditches or stock their kitchens, and they would be no happier substituting a hobgoblin from the midland Thorns than if you asked them to satisfy their craving for five-star cuisine with a gutterburger from your choice of bad fast food joint.<br /> <br /> It might also have something to do with humans being the only things with human souls, but frankly &quot;Why do the infamously capricious supernatural beings thematically analogous to the hyper-rich do something that ruins people's lives?&quot; is a question where a consistent and universal answer isn't terribly interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T12:31:35-07:00","id":1520700,"title":"","content":"Are Fae Miens fixed or can they be partially altered? For example, can fur, horns, hooves, wings, etc be trimmed, painted on, broken off, etc? And if such things are broken off, what happens to those broken pieces? Do they appear as broken sticks and straws to mortal eyes or do they simply vanish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T17:39:42-07:00","id":1520729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1520700#post1520700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Fae Miens fixed or can they be partially altered? For example, can fur, horns, hooves, wings, etc be trimmed, painted on, broken off, etc? And if such things are broken off, what happens to those broken pieces? Do they appear as broken sticks and straws to mortal eyes or do they simply vanish?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're part of the character's body and react to change accordingly based on what they are, and the Mask means things that aren't fae or otherwise able to see them for what they are perceive them as something mundane and not intrinsically remarkable. You can paint your rack of antlers and mortals will see an elaborate process of painting your brow and temples. Getting your little cosmetic devil wings chopped off will leave a bodily remnant that might be interpreted as parts of a dead bat or an abandoned theater prop. Loose fur and feathers will almost certainly be read as human hair or sheddings from a mundane specimen of whatever animal your mien evokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T23:16:52-07:00","id":1520796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1520729#post1520729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're part of the character's body and react to change accordingly based on what they are, and the Mask means things that aren't fae or otherwise able to see them for what they are perceive them as something mundane and not intrinsically remarkable. You can paint your rack of antlers and mortals will see an elaborate process of painting your brow and temples. Getting your little cosmetic devil wings chopped off will leave a bodily remnant that might be interpreted as parts of a dead bat or an abandoned theater prop. Loose fur and feathers will almost certainly be read as human hair or sheddings from a mundane specimen of whatever animal your mien evokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this! It's perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T07:10:15-07:00","id":1520877,"title":"","content":"Can changeling escape again after being caught by True Fae? Is there a possibility of multiple Durances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T07:25:44-07:00","id":1520879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1520877#post1520877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can changeling escape again after being caught by True Fae? Is there a possibility of multiple Durances?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s pure ST-fiat-land, I think.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019m inclined to say that a second capture and a following second escape is possible, but a second Durance (which I consider different from mere captivity) is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T17:18:38-07:00","id":1520911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1520879#post1520879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I\u2019m inclined to say that a second capture and a following second escape is possible, but a second Durance (which I consider different from mere captivity) is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd concur with this. Or to be more precise: A changeling can be once again captured to Faerie, and can escape Faerie a second time. The result is &quot;just&quot; a changeling who's been through a period of captivity and bears the normal scars of whatever experience they went through in Faerie. It's not transformative in the same way it is for a mortal human undergoing their Durance and becoming a changeling. You don't become a changeling-changeling.<br /> <br /> If a player and Storyteller agree they're interested, they might tell a story where a changeling is captured by another of the Others and returns with an altered mien. I wouldn't assume this by default, and even if another changeling were to be captured and escape in the same chronicle, the same might not happen to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T06:12:19-07:00","id":1520940,"title":"","content":"While I mostly agree with both of you, I'd like to add that to make it dramatically appropriate, any escape should require a hefty price. Something truly significant that's left behind much like how a first time escapee's soul is torn apart and left behind as scraps in the form of Icons scattered in the Hedge. It could be as simple as just additional Icons (lowering the character's max Clarity) and/or something more novel like their past experiences (not just memories, but the actual events themselves instead never happened to that changeling; maybe they instead happened to someone who picked up that particular Icon), etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T15:41:55-07:00","id":1521624,"title":"","content":"Is there a list of homebrewed Dramaturgy or magic anywhere? It would be nice if someone started a thread on Dramaturgy akin to the Creative Thaumaturgy from Mage the Awakening 2e. I think that Changeling the Lost is just as magical as Mage and it needs more fae magic contents. There's Wyrd Sorcery, which I think is based on 1e. Maybe someone could update it to 2e? Or create a PDF and put it in the Storytellers' Vault. With the Hedge book being the last one, it's not the end of it because people can create more contents, either paid or free and I'm willing to pay for more. And I want more fae magic and power, items of wonders, and more.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T14:02:53-07:00","id":1521784,"title":"","content":"Sorry to post another question so soon. I'm wondering how long can a Changeling stay in the Hedge before it starts to affect them before going back to the mortal world? My guess is that the higher their Clarity is, the more they have to go back to the mortal world and the more higher their Wyrd is, the more they can stay in the Hedge? Or am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T20:53:27-07:00","id":1521802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1521784#post1521784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to post another question so soon. I'm wondering how long can a Changeling stay in the Hedge before it starts to affect them before going back to the mortal world? My guess is that the higher their Clarity is, the more they have to go back to the mortal world and the more higher their Wyrd is, the more they can stay in the Hedge? Or am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Time is a little wonky in the Hedge, but lack of human or changeling contact is going to eventually ping your Clarity into nonfunctionality, particularly given that your Touchstones probably aren't hanging around in the Hedge long-term if they're to fulfill the function your relationship with them serves, and the higher your Wyrd the more likely a successful Clarity attack is to inflict Clarity damage; the Hedge also specifically doesn't make Clarity attacks that stem from it and its creations less impactful.<br /> <br /> Dice rolls being what they are, the odds of getting into a situation that requires Goblin Debt to extricate yourself from approach 1 over time, and too many of those in too short a time will se eyou reduced to a Hedge Denizen stuck relying on resolving Clarity Conditions to hover around Clarity 3 and below.<br /> <br /> If the Hedge &quot;starting to affect them&quot; is not a question about Clarity and/or Goblin Debt then I am not sure what you are asking. It's a borderland where you can forage or barter for food that can sustain a changeling, and by virtue of not being Arcadia it's not like just being in the place is going to accelerate your transformation into a more inhuman state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T02:35:11-07:00","id":1522147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1521784#post1521784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to post another question so soon. I'm wondering how long can a Changeling stay in the Hedge before it starts to affect them before going back to the mortal world? My guess is that the higher their Clarity is, the more they have to go back to the mortal world and the more higher their Wyrd is, the more they can stay in the Hedge? Or am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it is worth, i have seen an Actual Play set entirely in the Hedge, where the characters have escaped Arcadia but not made it back to the material world (mostly because of plot reasons).<br /> <br /> They form a Motley and meet other Changelings and Hobs. They spend a lot of time figuring out how to get somewhere safe, but they aren't particularly affects by clarity attacks more so than they might be if they were facing a return Ironside to reclaim their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T16:37:46-07:00","id":1522240,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys! I have hundreds more questions. Here's another one. Is it possible to relocate a Hollow with Hedgespinning? Or do we have to build a new Hollow, while still retaining the Merits for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T17:15:27-07:00","id":1522242,"title":"","content":"Hedgespinning it seems reasonable to me, just have it be a difficult one unless mobility was a distinct Hollow feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T18:15:43-07:00","id":1522245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522242#post1522242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedgespinning it seems reasonable to me, just have it be a difficult one unless mobility was a distinct Hollow feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a Howl's Moving Hollow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T18:25:10-07:00","id":1522246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522245#post1522245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like a Howl's Moving Hollow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Baba Yaga's chicken-hut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T18:55:52-07:00","id":1522248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522240#post1522240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys! I have hundreds more questions. Here's another one. Is it possible to relocate a Hollow with Hedgespinning? Or do we have to build a new Hollow, while still retaining the Merits for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;relocate.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can reshape the environment quite drastically with enough Hedgespinning, and by the same token you can move the terrain &quot;into&quot; or &quot;out of&quot; the Thorns and gradually build up established routes that make your Hollow &quot;closer&quot; to another landmark or other location, and there's always the &quot;interact with the environment to do the impossible&quot; paradigm shift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T20:14:59-07:00","id":1522376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522248#post1522248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;relocate.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can reshape the environment quite drastically with enough Hedgespinning, and by the same token you can move the terrain &quot;into&quot; or &quot;out of&quot; the Thorns and gradually build up established routes that make your Hollow &quot;closer&quot; to another landmark or other location, and there's always the &quot;interact with the environment to do the impossible&quot; paradigm shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it sounds like it's doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T20:17:00-07:00","id":1522377,"title":"","content":"What are some benefits of entering one's own Dreams by themselves through oneiromancy, besides practicing the art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T20:35:06-07:00","id":1522378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522377#post1522377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some benefits of entering one's own Dreams by themselves through oneiromancy, besides practicing the art?</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-defense and self-knowledge, particularly for stuff you'd otherwise have to brave Arcadia to investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T03:26:59-07:00","id":1522393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522378#post1522378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-defense and self-knowledge, particularly for stuff you'd otherwise have to brave Arcadia to investigate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you please elaborate on this, if you don't mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T09:12:37-07:00","id":1522402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522393#post1522393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please elaborate on this, if you don't mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things can get in your dreams and entering your own dreams is useful for stopping them from messing with you.<br /> <br /> Your dreams say things about you and even without the ability to use Shift Conditions oneiromancy can provide you with information about yourself that you might not otherwise have realized.<br /> <br /> Your memories of Arcadia get stronger the higher your Wyrd is and this is useful (if dangerous, because of how Clarity works) for trying to examine things about your time in Arcadia without e.g. actually returning to your Keeper's domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T09:45:09-07:00","id":1522404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522393#post1522393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you please elaborate on this, if you don't mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, dreams are a system that the mind use to elaborate experiences and thraumas.<br /> You could use lucid dream to train in skills, merits, and to heal persistent mental conditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T11:27:49-07:00","id":1522637,"title":"","content":"The video game Cultist Simulator has a whole system about gaining occult knowledge from dreams. The actual mechanics are simple and not that useful for Chronicles, but the fiction is basically that these specific dreams contain all sorts of improbable stuff, including spirits of the dead, visions of divinity, and knowledge from other timelines that reflect your timeline in important ways, and learning secrets from them can be used, with some effort, to find mysterious people, places, and things in the real world once you wake up. It's very focused within the limits of its gameplay but it's very evocative and gave me lots of ideas for putting useful stuff inside eldritch dreamscapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T14:10:37-07:00","id":1522763,"title":"","content":"Hi, I an trying to grasp oneiromancy and failing to understand why one would use gate of horn. You lose all the protections provided by the dream form, and only benefit I was able to find is lack of resolve+composure roll to leave a bastion. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25483-seregnore","name":"Seregnore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T19:51:12-07:00","id":1522771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seregnore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522763#post1522763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I an trying to grasp oneiromancy and failing to understand why one would use gate of horn. You lose all the protections provided by the dream form, and only benefit I was able to find is lack of resolve+composure roll to leave a bastion. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes your Social Attributes are markedly worse than your other stats. Sometimes you don't want to risk your Health track getting smaller whenever you encounter a breaking point (or you're Giant and want to actually benefit from that). Sometimes you don't want to blow Glamour on oneiromantic efforts to locate an exit before you even get to the Roads. Dream Form is only consistently a protection in the sense that dying doesn't kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T21:54:38-07:00","id":1522777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seregnore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522763#post1522763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I an trying to grasp oneiromancy and failing to understand why one would use gate of horn. You lose all the protections provided by the dream form, and only benefit I was able to find is lack of resolve+composure roll to leave a bastion. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, in physical form you can carry all your equipment with you, and i think you can carry out items from the dream itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T13:39:33-07:00","id":1522856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522771#post1522771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes your Social Attributes are markedly worse than your other stats. Sometimes you don't want to risk your Health track getting smaller whenever you encounter a breaking point (or you're Giant and want to actually benefit from that). Sometimes you don't want to blow Glamour on oneiromantic efforts to locate an exit before you even get to the Roads. Dream Form is only consistently a protection in the sense that dying doesn't kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in any situation there size of health track becomes a concern I would take an ability to wake up incited of dying. Also was not able to find anything about spending additional Glamour on using gates of ivory (other then taking extras with you) - and using gates of horn requiters you to spend Glamour on entering the Hedge, and locating them - a separate can of worms and risk on itself. About social attributes - it seems that characters with high social attributes would just use oneiromancy more often. Another question about attributes there are a lot to mentions of Resolve + Composure rolls, some of them are unique to the dream form. Would it be a Composure*2 roll? Or there are some exception I overlooked - for me changing Mental attributes for Social is a bit odd. And is there description who and why uses Social attributes and who uses mental - there are only changelings and others mentioned, but what about Others? Fetches? Are everyone in a same bucket as mortals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522777#post1522777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, in physical form you can carry all your equipment with you, and i think you can carry out items from the dream itself</div> </div> </div> </div>This look promising, and I do vaguely remember stuff like this in a first edition - dream poison or something like this. But as far as I remember in first edition you would always use a dream body dreamwalking. Either way it can lead to a nice dynamic - you start a heist in a dream form and after all the preparations you move in physically for a final extraction. Is there any material to read on it? I do know about Hunter's hearts somehow hidden in some bastions, but other then that - it seems that bastion gets reset every time sleeper wakes up, no?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25483-seregnore","name":"Seregnore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T19:23:40-07:00","id":1522875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seregnore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522856#post1522856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in any situation there size of health track becomes a concern I would take an ability to wake up incited of dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going into a situation where your Clarity is at risk, it is to your advantage to not be forced out of the dream faster because you got spooked too many times. Not every fight is to the death, but most setbacks cost time to make up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also was not able to find anything about spending additional Glamour on using gates of ivory (other then taking extras with you) - and using gates of horn requiters you to spend Glamour on entering the Hedge, and locating them - a separate can of worms and risk on itself. </div> </div> </div>Oneiromancy costs Glamour, finding the exit to a Bastion is substantially trickier without it, and you definitionally have to find an exit to a Bastion if the starting point on your journey to the Dreaming Roads is your own Bastion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About social attributes - it seems that characters with high social attributes would just use oneiromancy more often. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and characters who don't have high Social Attributes still have cause to mess around in dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another question about attributes there are a lot to mentions of Resolve + Composure rolls, some of them are unique to the dream form. Would it be a Composure*2 roll? Or there are some exception I overlooked - for me changing Mental attributes for Social is a bit odd. </div> </div> </div>Use the character's Resolve + Composure. They still have those stats and the roll in no way benefits from how a character's Dream Form interacts with the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is there description who and why uses Social attributes and who uses mental - there are only changelings and others mentioned, but what about Others? Fetches? Are everyone in a same bucket as mortals? </div> </div> </div>Things that are not changelings are others. If you're using another monster type with specific rules for Dream Form (e.g. mages using the higher of their Mental and Social Attributes, the Begotten using their highest Attribute in each category, mummies using various combinations of Pillar ratings, etc), those entities use their respective rules.<br /> <br /> Changelings use Social Attributes for their Dream Forms because the world they inhabit is an interpersonal one, for a broad definition of &quot;people,&quot; and control of emotional state and affect matter more to their ability to project power in dreams than the exercises of will and wit and intellect that characterize the more meditative approach to dream-diving mortal methods are familiar with. Mages have had their souls transformed by their connection to celestial power and thus can get the best of both those worlds; the Dark Mother's children keep their inner selves in the realest part of the Astral Realms and are accordingly able to draw on their Physical might as well as the other methods; and for the Arisen everything boils down to the various strengths of their souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typo. 09-20-2023, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T07:58:17-07:00","id":1522959,"title":"","content":"What are Changelings' defenses to supernatural stealth and mental domination in 2E? I am planning to restart a game on a long hiatus and I expected changelings to have some pretty nifty tricks to go with their paranoia and a way to ensure their freedom from the Gentry or anyone else, but I'm not seeing them.<br /> <br /> What defenses would a reasonably s<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b well-off freehold in the 90s have against vampire, mage or other infiltration and possible assassination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T09:29:35-07:00","id":1522960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522959#post1522959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Changelings' defenses to supernatural stealth</div> </div> </div> </div>The Goblin's Eye Goblin Contract allows Kenning to Clash with supernatural stealth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and mental domination in 2E? I am planning to restart a game on a long hiatus and I expected changelings to have some pretty nifty tricks to go with their paranoia and a way to ensure their freedom from the Gentry or anyone else, but I'm not seeing them.<br /> <br /> What defenses would a reasonably s<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b well-off freehold in the 90s have against vampire, mage or other infiltration and possible assassination? </div> </div> </div>The general way changelings defend against a big problem is by not being there when it comes calling. Anything more direct is likely a Court or Goblin Contract or otherwise custom content.<br /> <br /> (Infiltration by non-changelings is usually managed by those things not readily able to pass as one of the Lost over an extended period of scrutiny.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T18:27:58-07:00","id":1522982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522875#post1522875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going into a situation where your Clarity is at risk, it is to your advantage to not be forced out of the dream faster because you got spooked too many times. Not every fight is to the death, but most setbacks cost time to make up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I missing something? As far as I was able to find one cannot be forced out of dream by clarity damage - it can at best reduce your dream health to a minimum determined by your Wyrd. I am not sure what happened with a dream form if changeling runs out of clarity and becomes Comatose - definitely not awakening as it seems - but physically pass out in someones dream seems worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522875#post1522875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use the character's Resolve + Composure. They still have those stats and the roll in no way benefits from how a character's Dream Form interacts with the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! It seems I was a bit blindsided by the description on CTL 2e 216. So, a little example just to confirm I understand it correctly - if a character goes to a dream to draft some legal papers because he does not have enough time in a day he will roll something Intelligence+Politics, but if he tries to snoop out someone secrets he will do it by rolling Presence+Politics and turning the dream in legal drama?<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry for a long string of questions - just started to look at the second edition of Changelings, and Oneiromancy is the area there it is hard to decyfer by myself by applying a common sense. I was instantly intrigued by the ability of changelings to go into the dreams in the flesh, but by reading the book myself I was not able to understand why one would abandon a safety net of a dream form - other then for getting items in and out the dream, thanks to the Neos01 for suggestion. I do believe that there should be some, but I could easily miss it - book structure can be a bit confusing.\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25483-seregnore","name":"Seregnore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T20:51:17-07:00","id":1522991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seregnore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522982#post1522982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something? As far as I was able to find one cannot be forced out of dream by clarity damage - it can at best reduce your dream health to a minimum determined by your Wyrd. I am not sure what happened with a dream form if changeling runs out of clarity and becomes Comatose - definitely not awakening as it seems - but physically pass out in someones dream seems worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a shorter healthbar means being ejected from the dream faster and there's an entire Merit for healing your physical Health faster in the Hedge, which the Dreaming Roads is part of, to say nothing of first aid and Contracts like Shared Burden. Having Dream Health equivalent to the physical Health of an extremely sickly person because you encountered supernatural sensory confusion in the easily confusing environment of a dream is generally undesirable compared to having that same Clarity damage not also push your existing damage into the realm of wound penalties if you are going into a dream expecting a physical confrontation to occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aha! It seems I was a bit blindsided by the description on CTL 2e 216. So, a little example just to confirm I understand it correctly - if a character goes to a dream to draft some legal papers because he does not have enough time in a day he will roll something Intelligence+Politics, but if he tries to snoop out someone secrets he will do it by rolling Presence+Politics and turning the dream in legal drama? </div> </div> </div>You use your character's Power for Intelligence, Strength, or Presence tasks in Dream Form. The rolls you were asking about that are specific to Dream Form (which seem to just be the roll to wake up, which logically isn't going to be benefited by your Dream Form traits any more than the roll to meditate through the Gate of Ivory) specifically say they're Resolve + Composure and presumably would just say it was a Resistance + Resistance roll otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for a long string of questions - just started to look at the second edition of Changelings, and Oneiromancy is the area there it is hard to decyfer by myself by applying a common sense. I was instantly intrigued by the ability of changelings to go into the dreams in the flesh, but by reading the book myself I was not able to understand why one would abandon a safety net of a dream form - other then for getting items in and out the dream, thanks to the Neos01 for suggestion. I do believe that there should be some, but I could easily miss it - book structure can be a bit confusing.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>As has been pointed out for similar situations in other gamelines, there largely <i>isn't</i> much specific benefit to going to mental worlds in physical form, unless your Dream Form would be a worse way to interact with those worlds than your waking self and anything you manage to bring in with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T23:47:09-07:00","id":1522995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522960#post1522960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general way changelings defend against a big problem is by not being there when it comes calling. Anything more direct is likely a Court or Goblin Contract or otherwise custom content.<br /> <br /> (Infiltration by non-changelings is usually managed by those things not readily able to pass as one of the Lost over an extended period of scrutiny.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks on the goblin's eye contract, I had forgotten about it. I can generally agree about changelings trying to get out of the way (when they can see it, at leaset), but being able to resist supernatural charms or infiltrators sounds like the kind of thing I expected in their toolbox considering their general fear of the gentry and desire to not get caught again. Sure, it's hard to stay undercover among them for long, but another supernatural could do a lot of damage even in a short time.<br /> <br /> I had a game where a vampire ended up at a court event and it seemed like no one had a good way to make it significantly harder for them if they could find and charm, dominate or blood bond a changeling into revealing that the location (unless the trick where you spend glamor to shed bonds would apply there, but as I understood it it was just for physical restraints). I thought about other supernaturals trying to cause trouble and I was curious what changelings could do to not be caught off-guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:23:08-07:00","id":1523016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1522995#post1522995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks on the goblin's eye contract, I had forgotten about it. I can generally agree about changelings trying to get out of the way (when they can see it, at leaset), but being able to resist supernatural charms or infiltrators sounds like the kind of thing I expected in their toolbox considering their general fear of the gentry and desire to not get caught again. Sure, it's hard to stay undercover among them for long, but another supernatural could do a lot of damage even in a short time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, that paranoia is there in part <i>because</i> they have no easy counter to hard mind control or hidden observers. They mostly get around it the same way everyone else does, i.e. raising their Supernatural Tolerance and keeping secrets. Pledgecraft can set consequences for breaking the trust of a made promise, but that requires establishing the boundary in the first place.<br /> <br /> Like, I understand wanting there to be something universal, but there's a reason the primary duties of the outward-facing Court in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495989-have-any-you-created-your-own-changeling-court?p=1496016#post1496016\">my freehold patronized by a pair of archdemons</a> are essentially the twin information-control axes of surveillance and misdirection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T02:44:43-07:00","id":1523400,"title":"","content":"When tearing one's Kith to become Kithless, does it sever ties to the True Fae also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T05:30:48-07:00","id":1523404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1523400#post1523400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When tearing one's Kith to become Kithless, does it sever ties to the True Fae also?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, since some Kithless are said to be the results of their Keeper just forgetting or neglecting them enough, and they don't get any less Lost than other changelings (Kithless or not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T16:07:49-07:00","id":1523478,"title":"","content":"Do Names work the same way as in Mage the Awakening with Shadow Names? Do True Faes instinctively know the Lost's Name to be able to track them down or send Huntsmen after them? Also, do Names affect the Changeling in some way physically or metaphysically that may shape their identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T17:01:04-07:00","id":1523479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1523478#post1523478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Names work the same way as in Mage the Awakening with Shadow Names?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because a mage's Shadow Name is a constructed magical identity. The only capital-N Name in Changeling is the core of a True Fae's expansive identity; the &quot;true name&quot; referenced in Fae mechanics is the more general occult phenomenon of a name that serves as a mystically potent identifier of a given person, which is one reason changelings tend to use a different name in their new lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do True Faes instinctively know the Lost's Name to be able to track them down or send Huntsmen after them? </div> </div> </div>Any given Fae to which you are connected may have gotten ahold of your name through direct or indirect magical channels, but as with everything else, the Fae may want to possess knowledge of a character's name and therefore will have to go to the trouble of getting it to get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do Names affect the Changeling in some way physically or metaphysically that may shape their identity? </div> </div> </div>Not by default, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T14:28:44-08:00","id":1525979,"title":"","content":"So, I do apologize for asking something that has been asked before, but as I cannot find the exact post I've got to ask, what does the line &quot;What a motley will do with the purest, powerless representation of their tormentor is anyone\u2019s guess.&quot; refer to, when it comes to freeing a Huntsman? I've been in an argument with others about the intended meaning and we aren't making any headway in convincing one another.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that it refers to the Huntsman, the one who bore the face of the Gentry and acted in their steed.<br /> <br /> Others have come to the conclusion it means the Title itself or the Gentry's desire for that particular Changeling (and thus that by having it the Gentry would no longer desire the Changeling), since the Huntsman is... not the Title.<br /> <br /> If someone could weigh in, or link me to the past discussions on this, I would be very grateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T18:17:10-08:00","id":1525988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1525979#post1525979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I do apologize for asking something that has been asked before, but as I cannot find the exact post I've got to ask, what does the line &quot;What a motley will do with the purest, powerless representation of their tormentor is anyone\u2019s guess.&quot; refer to, when it comes to freeing a Huntsman? I've been in an argument with others about the intended meaning and we aren't making any headway in convincing one another.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that it refers to the Huntsman, the one who bore the face of the Gentry and acted in their steed.<br /> <br /> Others have come to the conclusion it means the Title itself or the Gentry's desire for that particular Changeling (and thus that by having it the Gentry would no longer desire the Changeling), since the Huntsman is... not the Title.<br /> <br /> If someone could weigh in, or link me to the past discussions on this, I would be very grateful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The preceding sentence talks about the Huntsman expunging the Title once their heart is restored, so it's understandable where they're coming from.<br /> <br /> However, the thing that's powerless, as suggested by &quot;The Wild Hunt&quot; on the preceding page, is the Huntsman's heart, whose destruction stops them from reforming in the Hedge. The next lines talk about whether to spare or kill the Huntsman \u2014 the implicit decision being to return or destroy the heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T10:59:56-08:00","id":1527698,"title":"","content":"I apologize if someone already asked this before, but has anyone attempted to overlay CtL1e Seemings &amp; Kiths to CtL2e? If so, I would appreciate a link.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T13:27:19-08:00","id":1529037,"title":"","content":"What the dots in the Regalia Manifestation Merit (K&amp;K pg 65) actually do? You only get one Manifestation, it is capped at Regalia Contracts/2 and needs to be purchased separately for each Regalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T14:43:43-08:00","id":1529039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1529037#post1529037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the dots in the Regalia Manifestation Merit (K&amp;K pg 65) actually do? You only get one Manifestation, it is capped at Regalia Contracts/2 and needs to be purchased separately for each Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Next page, under &quot;Manifestation Powers.&quot; A permanent manifestation has a number of powers equal to your dots in the Merit for that Regalia, gaining more when you get more dots. Temporary manifestations instead have a number based on the roll result immediately preceding that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T15:10:42-08:00","id":1529041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1529039#post1529039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next page, under &quot;Manifestation Powers.&quot; A permanent manifestation has a number of powers equal to your dots in the Merit for that Regalia, gaining more when you get more dots. Temporary manifestations instead have a number based on the roll result immediately preceding that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>The merit itself contradicts that, but that makes so much more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T15:55:24-08:00","id":1529042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1529041#post1529041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit itself contradicts that, but that makes so much more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? The Merit says your dots in it are limited by the number of Contracts in that Regalia you know, and the section says a permanent manifestation (i.e. the thing the Merit represents) gets a number of benefits equal to the Merit dots for that Regalia's Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T22:37:09-08:00","id":1531456,"title":"","content":"Is Hollow capped at 5 dots total, or 5 dots per contributor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:39:12-07:00","id":1533960,"title":"","content":"Itens left in the Hedge become magical, does it hold truth for already magicall itens, like WtF Fetishes and MtA Soulstones? I know that nothing hinders me from saying so on my table, but is there any example of such things already happenning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:41:32-07:00","id":1533961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1531456#post1531456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Hollow capped at 5 dots total, or 5 dots per contributor?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW seens like capped at 5, or else you would have some Freeholds with Hollows 10+ completely immune to instrusion or detection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:02:18-07:00","id":1533966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1533960#post1533960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Itens left in the Hedge become magical, does it hold truth for already magicall itens, like WtF Fetishes and MtA Soulstones? I know that nothing hinders me from saying so on my table, but is there any example of such things already happenning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge-forged tokens are created from items of personal significance, and 1e included a note that tokens resist alterations to their form from outside sources (with examples including a werewolf dedicating it to make it transform along with their body or a mage using magic to change its shape potentially destroying the token or making its drawback more powerful). Kith and Kin makes it clear that the marinading process is at least adjacent to dramaturgy (since goblins can use dramaturgy to steer the power of a prospective token), and the way magic tends to work in general means the symbolic qualities of a magical item are already likely to relate to the abilities it provides.<br /> <br /> It's conceivably possible for the Hedge to twist the history and emotional context behind a Fetter or an Azothic Object or a gadget or what have you into a token, but no such examples exist on the books and the most plausible positive outcome would be a replacement of the original power rather than stacking on top of each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T09:52:39-07:00","id":1533981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1533966#post1533966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's conceivably possible for the Hedge to twist the history and emotional context behind a Fetter or an Azothic Object or a gadget or what have you into a token, but no such examples exist on the books and the most plausible positive outcome would be a <b>replacement of the original power</b> rather than stacking on top of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Thats what I'm trying to imagine and create, some Token that acts similar to a spirit Influence, but in whymsical ways, or a Soulstone that morphed its owner into a strange legacy because of the Hedge, that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> I'll write some things and open a topic to discuss about possibilities later. But thanks for the help. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-10-2024, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T13:28:58-07:00","id":1533994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1533981#post1533981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats what I'm trying to imagine and create, some Token that acts similar to a spirit Influence, but in whymsical ways, or a Soulstone that morphed its owner into a strange legacy because of the Hedge, that kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1533966#post1533966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's conceivably possible for the Hedge to twist the history and emotional context behind a Fetter or an Azothic Object or a gadget or what have you into a token, but <b>no such examples exist on the books</b> and the most plausible positive outcome would be a replacement of the original power rather than stacking on top of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1533960#post1533960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Itens left in the Hedge become magical, does it hold truth for already magicall itens, like WtF Fetishes and MtA Soulstones? <b>I know that nothing hinders me from saying so on my table, but is there any example of such things already happenning?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphases mine. If you want published examples there are none. The answer to &quot;are there any examples&quot; is &quot;no&quot; and the answer to &quot;what happens&quot; is &quot;here's what the game has said in this edition and the previous one that you may use to inform whatever conclusion you might try to draw in the absence of explicit statement in either direction.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oak, Ash and Thorn has a section on designing tokens. Mage has a section on designing Legacies. Hedge Ghosts have Influences that largely work the same as Influences do for other ephemeral beings and invisible entities. If you want to make a fae object with an unusual backstory you can just do that. If you want to justify a piece of strangeness in another gameline with &quot;a component of the process that created this was dunked in the Hedge for a while&quot; you can just do that. Anything more involved is going to be pure homebrew for which the needs of your table are a bigger concern than the basics of creating magical objects in Changeling: the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T10:03:24-07:00","id":1534197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1503371#post1503371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the Court Goodwill allow to buy Court specific merits (Firebrand, Grounded, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this once, just got a single answer from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> (thanks btw).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, can you use <b>Court Goodwill</b> to cover for merits like <b>Frightful Incantation</b> that ask for &quot;<i>Mantle \u2022\u2022 (the Mantle must impose fear-based Bedlam Conditions)</i>&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T10:21:32-07:00","id":1534198,"title":"","content":"I'd give the same answer as back then. Your effective Mantle level for the purposes of buying Merits would be the main limitation, since you <i>have </i>incorporated that Mantle into your mythos. (Still an &quot;OK at my table&quot; answer, ymmv)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:35:26-07:00","id":1536529,"title":"","content":"What's the scope on Courts as organisations? I would expect that every member of a Court within a Freehold has some level of congregation with one another, and acknowledgement of their internal hierarchy, but do they communicate with other chapters elsewhere at all? Or is it more like, once the agreement that is able to make something function as a Court is establishes, it becomes a kind of principle that changelings elsewhere can discover and adhere to.<br /> <br /> I suppose bound up in that question are follow ups of &quot;how much do different Freeholds recognise and engage with one another&quot; and &quot;to what extent do far flung changelings have a common culture that they can initiate new arrivals into?&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmm, as I'm asking this, I'm having a vague sense that there's an obvious role that the Hedge can play in a lot of this that I'm overlooking for lack of familiarity. I'm suddenly having a vague recollection of First Edition having a detail to the effect of &quot;changelings can actually readily migrate or even go on temporary trips, and not uncommonly run into changelings from elsewhere, due to the nature of spatial relationships in the Hedge&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T19:41:55-07:00","id":1536545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1536529#post1536529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the scope on Courts as organisations? I would expect that every member of a Court within a Freehold has some level of congregation with one another, and acknowledgement of their internal hierarchy, but do they communicate with other chapters elsewhere at all? Or is it more like, once the agreement that is able to make something function as a Court is establishes, it becomes a kind of principle that changelings elsewhere can discover and adhere to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cultural touchstones of a Court can build up from the groundwork of rituals performed as part of its Bargain, and the same patron is liable to have asking prices for its benefits that at least angle in the same direction even with different Bargains, and of course one of the reasons changelings join a court is to formally connect themselves with like-minded fae, but as far back as Grim Fears you got changelings who had Mantles but no functional ties with the Courts because they just carved out their own agreement with the seasons or what have you.<br /> <br /> Loosely speaking, the assumption is slightly more localized unity than the Tribes provide in Werewolf: Bargains as widespread as the Great Courts of the four seasons tend to have propagated traditions like Radio Free Fae or the Homecoming and members of a Court in the same freehold will keep in touch with each other by obligation if nothing else, but every freehold is liable to have their own spin on things from their lived experience and local pressures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose bound up in that question are follow ups of &quot;how much do different Freeholds recognise and engage with one another&quot; and &quot;to what extent do far flung changelings have a common culture that they can initiate new arrivals into?&quot; </div> </div> </div><i>Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn</i> discusses freeholds in the plural sense, noting that freeholds in a region tend to be friendly but somewhat distant, maintaining rapport but recognizing that being too entangled with an entirely separate body of fae and oaths compounds any problems a single freehold might face.<br /> <br /> Common culture, as mentioned, can at least be found in those rituals that are part of the court's Bargain as extensions of its patronage and coping strategies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, as I'm asking this, I'm having a vague sense that there's an obvious role that the Hedge can play in a lot of this that I'm overlooking for lack of familiarity. I'm suddenly having a vague recollection of First Edition having a detail to the effect of &quot;changelings can actually readily migrate or even go on temporary trips, and not uncommonly run into changelings from elsewhere, due to the nature of spatial relationships in the Hedge&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The degree to which new people come and go from an area is the closest 1e provided to a changeling population dynamic a la Vampire and Werewolf's early &quot;there's about one of this type of monster in the world per this many people&quot; statements, and while 1e's model of Clarity disincentivized travel for changelings who weren't dedicated to a wanderer's life or a routine circuit 2e certainly facilitates a greater degree of mobility, with the usual caveats of Touchstone-reliant monsters existing in geographical and emotional tension with the needs of those relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T20:16:08-07:00","id":1536548,"title":"","content":"The question kind of came to me as I was thinking about certain demographics and interrelationships and imagining that the original free might still have a claim to be the most numerous and organisationally sophisticated in the world of Chronicles of Darkness (and even among those, mage Orders probably functioning a few steps above with their caucuses and convocations to formally and regularly have members from across multiple polities gather and coordinate).<br /> <br /> I got to thinking &quot;changelings are probably somewhere in between those and the really small numbered ones like Prometheans (if disproportionately hard to notice with the Masque)&quot;, and just got to thinking about how I wasn't quite sure how international (or even national, really) they were.<br /> <br /> (On that note, I picture Sin-Eaters as comparably numerous but still a bit hard to tell because they're even more loosely organised, Unchained as a bit less numerous but being contiguously chained into a network of contacts, and there being relatively few Mummies even on those rare occasions when they're all active at once, but the kind of infrastructure they build for themselves when alive gives them a disproportionate amount of reach, especially when members of their own internal organisations have cause to gather for common purpose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T01:01:28-07:00","id":1536688,"title":"","content":"I apologize if this is the wrong thread to post this, but I'm looking for some clarification on hedge sorcery.<br /> <br /> The section Striding Though indicates a changeling collects a number of Hedge spinning successes equal to Doors + 2 during the scene that they will perform a conjuring.<br /> <br /> Are these successes separate from the extended action roll for the conjuring itself?<br /> <br /> For example, assume a sorcerer has already gathered the necessary hecatombs for a conjuring. They first perform mundane actions with a penalty (depending on their location in the hedge), spending glamor each time to bank excess successes = Doors + 2. Then they pay 2 Glamour and 1 Willpower to start the extended action conjuring roll.<br /> <br /> Each roll of the conjuring sacrifices 1 hecatomb and if the roll is a success, opens 1 door (regardless of the number of successes on the roll). After interval determined by Clarity they roll again, sacrificing the next hecatomb. Does the sorcerer pay the 2 Glamour and 1 Willpower cost again, or only the once?<br /> <br /> If a sorcerer scours their mask to use hedge sorcery outside the Hedge for the scene, how do they generate the hedge spinning successes needed to begin the conjuring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","user":"Arrested Scrimshank","date":". 06-02-2024, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T05:38:41-07:00","id":1536696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1536688#post1536688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section Striding Though indicates a changeling collects a number of Hedge spinning successes equal to Doors + 2 during the scene that they will perform a conjuring.<br /> <br /> Are these successes separate from the extended action roll for the conjuring itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, assume a sorcerer has already gathered the necessary hecatombs for a conjuring. They first perform mundane actions with a penalty (depending on their location in the hedge), spending glamor each time to bank excess successes = Doors + 2. Then they pay 2 Glamour and 1 Willpower to start the extended action conjuring roll.<br /> <br /> Each roll of the conjuring sacrifices 1 hecatomb and if the roll is a success, opens 1 door (regardless of the number of successes on the roll). After interval determined by Clarity they roll again, sacrificing the next hecatomb. Does the sorcerer pay the 2 Glamour and 1 Willpower cost again, or only the once? </div> </div> </div>Given that there are at least three Doors for every conjuring (and, unlike in Social Maneuvering, you can't open more than one Door per roll), it would seem reasonable to say the cost is up-front rather than per-roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a sorcerer scours their mask to use hedge sorcery outside the Hedge for the scene, how do they generate the hedge spinning successes needed to begin the conjuring? </div> </div> </div>Given the risks involved with scouring the Mask, it's likely a wholesale substitute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T08:19:28-07:00","id":1536698,"title":"","content":"This is of great help. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T18:18:59-07:00","id":1538398,"title":"","content":"When a Fae-Touch become a Hedge Denizen, can they increase their Wyld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:29:10-07:00","id":1538406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1538398#post1538398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Fae-Touch become a Hedge Denizen, can they increase their Wyld?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text of The Hedge notes that fae-touched being normally unable to raise their Wyrd means one who becomes a Geas (who all have to have had Wyrd 10 in the first place) would have to be more goblin than mortal. The same book's section diving into what being a Hedge Denizen is like is primarily concerned with the perspective of changelings who have undergone that transformation; much like there isn't direct guidance on what happens when a Goblin Queen foists their mantle onto a mortal child, there isn't any statement on how the Avowed handle the hobgoblin condition.<br /> <br /> The thrust of the material in The Hedge, though, seems to indicate that if you're a fae-touched who becomes a Hedge Denizen and you become able to raise your Wyrd, it's because you've committed to being a hobgoblin as far as the rest of the story goes, and considering what the Hedge does to fae-touched that's functionally a retirement in most games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T21:02:29-07:00","id":1538408,"title":"","content":"So, do you think a Fae-Touch with a Hedge Denizen condition could gain Wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T21:48:18-07:00","id":1538409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1538408#post1538408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think a Fae-Touch with a Hedge Denizen condition could gain Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as a player character in any way that doesn't end their time as a player character. They're still fae-touched and that means they still can't raise their Wyrd above 0 without completely abandoning one of the core aspects of their place in the narrative. &quot;Hobgoblin who used to be an Avowed&quot; is a tragic failstate for a fae-touched, or at best a retirement to the same sort of cozy semi-irrelevant liminality as most people who've become part of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T22:24:41-07:00","id":1538410,"title":"","content":"Can non fae-touch mortal gain Goblin Contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T04:59:04-07:00","id":1538419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1538410#post1538410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can non fae-touch mortal gain Goblin Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>By becoming Hedge Denizens, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T05:25:17-07:00","id":1538421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1538419#post1538419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By becoming Hedge Denizens, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you become a Hedge Denizen without Goblin Contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T05:29:56-07:00","id":1538422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1538421#post1538421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you become a Hedge Denizen without Goblin Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>By accepting hobgoblin deals. See page 256 of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T05:40:36-07:00","id":1538826,"title":"","content":"Is there sub-realm within the Hedge where you don't see the Hedge wall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T15:53:29-07:00","id":1539060,"title":"","content":"How does other major splats deal with Hobgoblins? Like, if they turn into Hedge Denizens, do they learn Goblin Contracts? Can they learn Goblin Contracts without turning into Hedge Denizens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T16:10:39-07:00","id":1539063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539060#post1539060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does other major splats deal with Hobgoblins? Like, if they turn into Hedge Denizens, do they learn Goblin Contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as stated in the text of the Hedge Denizen Condition about what happens to mortals and non-changelings unlucky enough to fall in with hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they learn Goblin Contracts without turning into Hedge Denizens? </div> </div> </div>Strong odds on no, though they keep one if they return to their former state and can accumulate Goblin Debt again that way, which opens the door for them to become a hobgoblin again; per the sidebar on p81 of The Hedge, becoming a hobgoblin removes any cost breaks they'd have on the powers they'd normally be purchasing with Experience (same as changelings buying Arcadian Contracts at non-affinity price) and becoming a Goblin Queen instates a hard lockout on buying new non-Contract powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T19:22:44-07:00","id":1539075,"title":"","content":"If you are born in the Hedge do you automatically become a hedge denizen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T20:03:10-07:00","id":1539076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539075#post1539075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are born in the Hedge do you automatically become a hedge denizen?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no textual statement one way or the other. Goblin Queens can hand over their place in the Hedge to a human child and may engineer an agreement for someone to give one to them, and the classic bit of mythology about being careful not to eat the food in fairyland or you won't be able to leave has a lot of interpretations, but both of those situations generally apply to babies who've been born already; being a hobgoblin can mean you were made into one or it can mean you came into existence as a part of the Hedge and without magic to look into it (like Goblin's Eye) it's hard to tell which kind a given hobgoblin is.<br /> <br /> What seems like a reasonable basic assumption to me would be that, without a biological parent who has at least some amount of Goblin Debt or other supernatural oddity, a child will not be born a hobgoblin.<br /> <br /> (The Hedge Denizen Condition is largely immaterial to this question unless you are making the assumption that a newborn child or infant has Traits suitable for a player character to engage with that are not themselves the product of Goblin Contracts and/or Dread Powers granted through the Condition.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T20:19:09-07:00","id":1539078,"title":"","content":"Is there any mention of what happen when Changeling have children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T21:09:07-07:00","id":1539081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539078#post1539078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any mention of what happen when Changeling have children?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in 2e, no. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\">1e had some stuff</a> that didn't make any hard statements beyond &quot;most changelings can't have kids because of the nature of their transformation or other trauma, and when they do there's not usually anything supernaturally notable about them like you'd get with ghoul children or demon-blooded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T16:03:11-07:00","id":1539116,"title":"","content":"As far as I know from the 1st edition it stated that Changelings found it very hard to have children as they weren't truly human anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T17:45:06-07:00","id":1539122,"title":"","content":"Does Court Goodwill ever get you the Court's extra method of gaining Glamour? It's not associated with any Mantle dot. So do you get it at Goodwill 1, Goodwill 3 (3-2 = 1, the first time Goodwill grants you effective Mantle), or never? Do Fae-Touched with Goodwill get it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T18:09:56-07:00","id":1539123,"title":"","content":"Can Changeling become a True Fae or something close to a True Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T19:04:29-07:00","id":1539126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539122#post1539122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Court Goodwill ever get you the Court's extra method of gaining Glamour? It's not associated with any Mantle dot. So do you get it at Goodwill 1, Goodwill 3 (3-2 = 1, the first time Goodwill grants you effective Mantle), or never? Do Fae-Touched with Goodwill get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No explicit statement to that effect, but given that it's the primary thing distinguishing a changeling with that Court's Mantle from an honorary member with Goodwill (and there's no hard cap on the number of Courts you can have Goodwill with), my reading is &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539123#post1539123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Changeling become a True Fae or something close to a True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are mechanics for it happening in 1e (Becoming Nightmare in The Equinox Road, plus the abbreviated/altered version in Dancers in the Dusk to go with the system hack where your Wyrd rating can move around wildly), and 2e has not presented any information that contradicts the possibility. It's a failure state to become a heartless magical solipsist in a game where your character's continued well-being depends on sustained connection with their former humanity; the 1e mechanics largely boiled down to &quot;after you reach Wyrd 10, at an unspecified point determined by your player and the Storyteller, you start rolling Clarity breaking points every time you wake up until you either drop to Wyrd 9 through magical detox or hit Clarity 0, jump into the Hedge, and run off to Arcadia to complete your metamorphosis.&quot;<br /> <br /> Powerful entitlements may textually enable one to become &quot;something close to a True Fae,&quot; particularly taken in combination with manifesting Regalia and/or becoming one of the Empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T20:50:18-07:00","id":1539128,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to use an Entitlement Token to become an Empty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T21:12:00-07:00","id":1539129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539128#post1539128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use an Entitlement Token to become an Empty?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have not gotten any new explicit answers to this question in the books or on these forums <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1374914#post1374914\">in the four years since this question was last asked</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T03:19:30-07:00","id":1539135,"title":"","content":"Does time spent in a limen count against a Goblin Queen's time limit out of the Hedge? Does a Goblin Queen or Hedge Denizen have the Deprived condition while in a limen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T09:02:51-07:00","id":1539145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539081#post1539081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in 2e, no. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\">1e had some stuff</a> that didn't make any hard statements beyond &quot;most changelings can't have kids because of the nature of their transformation or other trauma, and when they do there's not usually anything supernaturally notable about them like you'd get with ghoul children or demon-blooded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It was so hard there was a terrible Goblin Contract to get around it. Of course Goblin Contracts worked differently then. Probably best to just cut every especially thick bamboo shoot you see and hope to adopt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T09:16:51-07:00","id":1539147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539129#post1539129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have not gotten any new explicit answers to this question in the books or on these forums <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1374914#post1374914\">in the four years since this question was last asked</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry Satchel, I really forgot I had asked the same question 4 years ago, it was scratching my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T18:34:31-07:00","id":1539178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539135#post1539135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does time spent in a limen count against a Goblin Queen's time limit out of the Hedge? Does a Goblin Queen or Hedge Denizen have the Deprived condition while in a limen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the limen applies the usual reduction on Clarity attacks caused by things that aren't the Hedge, I'd say they alleviate the Deprived Condition, but the book's description of how the Hedge works around Goblin Queens and the description of the different levels of limen suggest to me that while the area itself would allow the Goblin Queen to step out of the Hedge proper, little to none of the materials in the limen would be suitable for crafting the necessary mantle to brave the outside world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T04:26:58-07:00","id":1539194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539178#post1539178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the limen applies the usual reduction on Clarity attacks caused by things that aren't the Hedge, I'd say they alleviate the Deprived Condition, but the book's description of how the Hedge works around Goblin Queens and the description of the different levels of limen suggest to me that while the area itself would allow the Goblin Queen to step out of the Hedge proper, little to none of the materials in the limen would be suitable for crafting the necessary mantle to brave the outside world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if &quot;wrapping pieces of it as a mantle around her&quot; is supposed to be a procedure or a poetic flourish. Does it take an action? Does it show? Is it more like a crude bio-hazard suit made of leaves and junk, or more like an aura of &quot;special effects&quot; perceptible to those who can pierce the Mask, like a Court Mantle? Could the Queen form the mantle - however that is supposed to work - in the Hedge proper, enter the limen, stay there indefinitely, and still have her whole Wyrd score in hours of survival in the mortal world beyond the limen? And what actually happens when that clock runs out?<br /> <br /> EDIT: After posting, thought of something along the lines of &quot;the plane of the Hedgeway resists the Goblin Queen like the surface of a soap bubble, covering her with a protective layer of gunk when it breaks.&quot; Which is an interpretation that I think might have legs.<br /> <br /> If a Goblin Queen just moved to a limen and stayed there, I assume her castle wouldn't just grow in the limen, but would her hobgoblin retainers try to pack it up and move it there? Could they succeed?<br /> <br /> (Sorry if this stopped being a &quot;simple&quot; question a while ago.)<br /> <br /> I also find from The Hedge that anyone can potentially become a Goblin Queen, and the two examples are a vampire (which is fine) and a mage. That second case raises a question, because mages don't track Touchstones any more than blue-book mortals do, so how did that happen?<br /> <br /> If a something-else becomes a Goblin Queen, is this a case where we should construe &quot;Wyrd&quot; strictly, or should strange Queens be able to use their Supernatural Tolerance to go home for a visit?<br /> <br /> (As an aside, per Dark Eras 2, it's frighteningly easy for a mage to conclude that paradox doesn't even <i>exist </i>in the Hedge, and you can't exactly <i>feel </i>Goblin Debt. Young-and-dumb Acanthus and Mastigos ought to be going Denizen pretty often.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 07-25-2024, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:41:21-07:00","id":1539257,"title":"","content":"The thumbs down poster strikes again for whatever reason that I don't understand.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T18:56:13-07:00","id":1539282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539194#post1539194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell if &quot;wrapping pieces of it as a mantle around her&quot; is supposed to be a procedure or a poetic flourish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly not a poetic flourish, given the verbiage is &quot;except by&quot; rather than the more ambiguous &quot;without&quot; \u2014 it's a thing they have to do rather than a thing that happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it take an action? Does it show? Is it more like a crude bio-hazard suit made of leaves and junk, or more like an aura of &quot;special effects&quot; perceptible to those who can pierce the Mask, like a Court Mantle? </div> </div> </div>It presumably takes as long as it takes and looks the way it looks using the method the Queen uses and is made of physical pieces of the Hedge, albeit with the broadened definition of physicality available in the Hedge. Whatever the result, the functional outcome is as subject to the Mask as any other fae thing and means you will not be seeing a Goblin Queen out in the world in a form that is visibly inhuman from a distance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could the Queen form the mantle - however that is supposed to work - in the Hedge proper, enter the limen, stay there indefinitely, and still have her whole Wyrd score in hours of survival in the mortal world beyond the limen? </div> </div> </div>My read would be that each constructed mantle works for one visit outside, and whatever normal rate of decay applies to the materials within the limen, but yes, they could linger in the limen just as one can hang out in the front entrance of their house with their coat on without going outside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what actually happens when that clock runs out? </div> </div> </div>My impulse is that the Hedge pulls them back in through the pieces they covered themselves in, in a similar phenomenon to Hedgeways that are more events than physical thresholds, given that there's no described effects for a Goblin Queen being outside of the Hedge without a mantle<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Goblin Queen just moved to a limen and stayed there, I assume her castle wouldn't just grow in the limen, but would her hobgoblin retainers try to pack it up and move it there? Could they succeed? </div> </div> </div>No. Possibly they or her subjects would leverage the obligations of her station to wheedle her into dealing with her business back home \u2014 remember that the station does not exist in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also find from The Hedge that anyone can potentially become a Goblin Queen, and the two examples are a vampire (which is fine) and a mage. That second case raises a question, because mages don't track Touchstones any more than blue-book mortals do, so how did that happen? </div> </div> </div>Possibly a bad choice of example that you can reasonably ignore the implications of unless you feel like making something of it. Possibly Fate shenanigans leveraging the same channels that allow a mortal child to become a Goblin Queen to transfer the Destiny-adjacent mantle of power to a mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a something-else becomes a Goblin Queen, is this a case where we should construe &quot;Wyrd&quot; strictly, or should strange Queens be able to use their Supernatural Tolerance to go home for a visit? </div> </div> </div>The same sidebar that has those two non-changeling-non-mortal examples explicitly says to use the character's Supernatural Tolerance in place of Wyrd where appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T19:08:34-07:00","id":1539284,"title":"","content":"what exactly are true fae anyway? they don't really fit with anything else in chronicles of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T19:10:12-07:00","id":1539285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539282#post1539282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The same sidebar that has those two non-changeling-non-mortal examples explicitly says to use the character's Supernatural Tolerance in place of Wyrd where appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does, sorry.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T20:37:53-07:00","id":1539292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539284#post1539284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what exactly are true fae anyway? they don't really fit with anything else in chronicles of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>In practical terms, they're the guiding intelligence behind the set of Titles, Regalia, Contracts, and other assets that collectively seek to acquire as much of reality as possible (with specific preferences varying by Fae), which leads them into conflict with changelings, hobgoblins, mortals, other monsters, and each other in the pursuit of their desires.<br /> <br /> In the &quot;standard model&quot; of the wider Chronicles, mages who've studied the Hedge identify it with the barrier they need to overcome to meditate from dreams or conscious thought into the deeper realms of the Astral, and its ability to lie to Mage Sight and apply Goblin Debt for released Paradoxes indicate it has some conceptual overlap with the Abyss, which of course suggests some conceptual overlap between Arcadia and the other part of the cosmology where mythic bastards bought their way into heaven, but for the most part the True Fae are the current rulers of Arcadia, who according to legend are a colonizing force who took over the land that gave them an endlessly complex collection of rules, manifested their greed as a hungry bramble laid over the land where dreams are found, and allowed them to pour their destinies into the natives to help fulfill their desires.<br /> <br /> They're gods who traded for their place in the land of miracles. They're a society of extremely powerful magical beings who each have enough influence on the force of reciprocity empowering them that exploiting the times when they make a poor decision is the best way to deal lasting damage to them.The ultimate nature of what they are is up in the air, such that most of the terminology for the core continuum of otherworlds in Changeling is self-referential and only descriptive at the level of end results \u2014 Faerie as it exists doesn't serve a singular purpose except insofar as it serves the individual wants of individual Fae, which are frankly all over the place with the only unifying thread being that every Fae wants something. The Strangers don't intrinsically represent or reflect anything except their own egoes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T06:41:01-07:00","id":1539375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539282#post1539282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same sidebar that has those two non-changeling-non-mortal examples explicitly says to use the character's Supernatural Tolerance in place of Wyrd where appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should a strange Denizen subtract Supernatural Tolerance from the successes required for a Hedge navigation chase? I assume non-Denizen strangers <i>don't</i>.<br /> <br /> Somewhat related:<br /> <br /> Does a changeling who becomes a Denizen <i>stop </i>subtracting current Clarity from the Hedge's Initiative? (Hedge Denizen says that the changeling is no longer a changeling, which is why Court Mantle is suspended while the Condition persists.) If not, should a strange Denizen subtract Clarity analog from the Hedge's Initiative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T09:23:16-07:00","id":1539378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539375#post1539375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a strange Denizen subtract Supernatural Tolerance from the successes required for a Hedge navigation chase? I assume non-Denizen strangers <i>don't</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes on both counts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a changeling who becomes a Denizen <i>stop </i>subtracting current Clarity from the Hedge's Initiative? (Hedge Denizen says that the changeling is no longer a changeling, which is why Court Mantle is suspended while the Condition persists.) If not, should a strange Denizen subtract Clarity analog from the Hedge's Initiative? </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you want non-native Hedge Denizens to work in your game. If former changelings ought to be distinguished from hobgoblins who used to be other things or were always what they are, then sure, let them keep the minor advantage; if you intend to have former changelings be indistinguishable from other hobgoblins, then don't. Given the way Hedge Navigation works, the practical outcome amounts to whether or not the character qualifies for an additional 1-3 successes off their required total on the outside chance that subtracting their Clarity (or equivalent) from 10 results in a number below their normal Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T14:28:26-07:00","id":1539441,"title":"","content":"Nobody really knows what the True Fae are other then the fact they are godlike in Acardia and just insanely powerful in our world but they're bound by contracts and oaths when they need to come to see us. They were never human to begin with and the Changelings had there own notions but never were sure about them and always had that doubt of did they really put one over them. They fit the chronicles of darkness well as the old fairy tales had darker origins and they could be quite cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-29-2024, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T14:58:30-07:00","id":1539501,"title":"","content":"Wich types of goblin fruits and oddments a Goblin Bounty merit provides?<br /> Book says common ones, but there is no easy distinctions between some of them. Like, Amaranthine is obviously a difficult one, but others are not that easily distinguishiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 07-29-2024, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T15:17:45-07:00","id":1539502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539501#post1539501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wich types of goblin fruits and oddments a Goblin Bounty merit provides?<br /> Book says common ones, but there is no easy distinctions between some of them. Like, Amaranthine is obviously a difficult one, but others are not that easily distinguishiable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to come down to individual tables and settings, because declaring a goblin fruit to be common makes a statement about the area, but as a universal practicality you may take it to mean that at the very least the Merit provides you access to thrice its rating in materially storable Glamour points separate from their personal pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T21:19:32-07:00","id":1539515,"title":"","content":"Does a weapon made with Pandora's Gift with the purpose of killing a Huntsmen act as a bane of sorts? Like, permanently killing it? Does the contract resists againts the touch of Cold Iron from his Panoply?<br /> <br /> Also, the contract allows the user to use the build equipment rules, but suppose the target touchs a piece of cloth but his innermost desire is a rare delicacy, does it transforms the material mystically into food for the duration of the Contract?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T12:45:06-07:00","id":1539548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539501#post1539501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wich types of goblin fruits and oddments a Goblin Bounty merit provides?<br /> Book says common ones, but there is no easy distinctions between some of them. Like, Amaranthine is obviously a difficult one, but others are not that easily distinguishiable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Common goblin fruits are those that only provide nourishment and a point of Glamour, without any special effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T13:00:02-07:00","id":1539552,"title":"","content":"What made the True Fae scary to me is the seeming randomness of there actions when they would abduct a person to Arcadia be it taking something that belonged to them or you caught there eye at that particular moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T15:21:04-07:00","id":1539664,"title":"","content":"Just finished scanning trough some threads but still didn't find much about the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539515#post1539515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a weapon made with Pandora's Gift with the purpose of killing a Huntsmen act as a bane of sorts? Like, permanently killing it? Does the contract resists againts the touch of Cold Iron from his Panoply?<br /> <br /> Also, the contract allows the user to use the build equipment rules, but suppose the target touchs a piece of cloth but his innermost desire is a rare delicacy, does it transforms the material mystically into food for the duration of the Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, is there any way for getting more Chrysalis forms? Like new ones or replacing old ones for new ones?<br /> <br /> I kinda feel that all that falls under homebrew territory, but would love suggestions anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T19:20:53-07:00","id":1539673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1539664#post1539664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished scanning trough some threads but still didn't find much about the following:</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reasonably certain that Pandora's Gift is not exempt from the universal drawback of Contracts and that the reference to being able to kill a Huntsman is an artifact of a previous draft of the game where Huntsmen worked differently.<br /> <br /> I see no reason for the material not to count as food in the case of a food-based product, though it's worth noting that the verbiage of the Contract indicates that, like the 1e Contract of the same name, Pandora's Gift can create things from nothing more than the target's desire \u2014 the thing the target has to touch is a material <i>or tool</i> that the changeling will use in the crafting, and if a power that removes the need for tools is used then the target need only touch the changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, is there any way for getting more Chrysalis forms? Like new ones or replacing old ones for new ones?<br /> <br /> I kinda feel that all that falls under homebrew territory, but would love suggestions anyway. </div> </div> </div>Firmly within the realm of per-table decisions. This is the gameline to allow for various means of trading off alternate forms or buying weird trinkets to add on; a relatively inexpensive Merit to allow one to e.g. take a point of Goblin Debt X times per story to change out one's alternate forms wouldn't be out of the ordinary, nor would a seeming bonus to allow workarounds (e.g. None More Dark Publishing's Book of Seemings provides an Elemental bonus for Chrysalis allowing them to use the highest traits and their choice of Size by combining their two animal forms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T00:27:45-07:00","id":1540169,"title":"","content":"Hello there, for 1E, I was wondering about damage, in particular healing time. Character take damage and recover in minutes/days/week based on the type, but does he need just to wait? Rest? Treat the wound in some way? Because looking up, only if he's filled with lethal damage there's no risk of bleeding out or do something to the wounds before the character start healing. Healing itself might speed up the process, I know that, but I was wondering if a character can take bashing damage and then basically continue doing his activity without worries and in a short amount of time it will recover just fine<br /> <br /> btw sorry for asking in changeling, wanted to ask in the general section","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","user":"Pyro165","date":". 08-11-2024, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","name":"Pyro165","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T06:13:00-07:00","id":1540171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyro165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1540169#post1540169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there, for 1E, I was wondering about damage, in particular healing time. Character take damage and recover in minutes/days/week based on the type, but does he need just to wait? Rest? Treat the wound in some way? Because looking up, only if he's filled with lethal damage there's no risk of bleeding out or do something to the wounds before the character start healing. Healing itself might speed up the process, I know that, but I was wondering if a character can take bashing damage and then basically continue doing his activity without worries and in a short amount of time it will recover just fine</div> </div> </div> </div>From p175 of the 1e core rulebook: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Your character doesn\u2019t have to rest or receive special attention to clear Health squares.</b> They are cleared automatically as the prescribed amount of time passes. The exception is if he is ever reduced in Health such that he is dying (see above); this requires intensive medical care. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T18:25:21-07:00","id":1540254,"title":"","content":"Not to mention some Goblin Fruits can aid in the healing of injuries of said person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T14:50:46-07:00","id":1540389,"title":"","content":"Can a Goblin Queen, changeling or otherwise, spend Experiences to improve a Supernatural Tolerance trait?<br /> In the case of the strange Queens from the example, vampire Queens can't raise Disciplines, but should they be able to &quot;fill in&quot; Devotions for which they already qualified before they became Queens? Should mage Queens be able to acquire Rotes, if they can get teachers or grimoires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-14-2024, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T15:23:17-07:00","id":1540391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1540389#post1540389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Goblin Queen, changeling or otherwise, spend Experiences to improve a Supernatural Tolerance trait?<br /> In the case of the strange Queens from the example, vampire Queens can't raise Disciplines, but should they be able to &quot;fill in&quot; Devotions for which they already qualified before they became Queens? Should mage Queens be able to acquire Rotes, if they can get teachers or grimoires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural Tolerance yes, any powers that aren't Goblin Contracts no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T15:41:53-07:00","id":1540392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1540391#post1540391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural Tolerance yes, any powers that aren't Goblin Contracts no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now I feel vindicated in my &quot;worst idea ever, yet something that someone might actually do.&quot; (I've played Ordo Dracul, and run games focused on the Ordo Dracul, so this is familiar territory to me.) Who needs more Arcana, or Rotes, if you can bump up your dice pool and Yantra-stacking ceiling, and Malleable Thorns will already give you everything you want? Stamp your soul on a magical world - just like a Wending! (I know it isn't.) Get respect from magical creatures - it's like ruling a spirit court! (I know that's not true either.)<br /> The temptation to grow one's hair out and learn contact juggling should be just <i>overwhelming</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:49:48-07:00","id":1540715,"title":"","content":"Does other courts have Bargains that the Huntsmen need to respect like the Seasonal Courts? I may have missed the part that explains why this is exclusively a Seasonal Court thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T11:41:50-07:00","id":1540719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1540715#post1540715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does other courts have Bargains that the Huntsmen need to respect like the Seasonal Courts? I may have missed the part that explains why this is exclusively a Seasonal Court thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. It's not exclusive to the Seasonal Courts. The sidebar in the Huntsmen section is talking about how although a Huntsman counts as an agent of the Fae for the purposes of a Bargain's constraints, loopholes exist in those Bargains that mean the Bargain offers little obstacle. The sidebar talks about this in relation to the Seasonal Courts' Bargains because the Seasonal Courts are the ones with full writeups in the corebook and thus the most directly needing addressed re: their usual defensive measures versus an unusual antagonist.<br /> <br /> By way of a comparable example, the Wind Court of Chicago's Bargain doesn't help much directly against Huntsmen \u2014 it renders the Gentry and their agents easily memorable and their witnesses indelible (still not something you want when dealing with a Court of gossips and reputation-builders who rely more on personal connections than institutional ones), but a Huntsman who doesn't care about leaving an impression has little deterrent compared to, say, hobgoblins and privateers who have to do business with the black mark of having meddled with the assets of a famously litigious and possessive demon even if the more concrete magical warding methods in circulation around the freehold didn't do the trick. (Notably, the Fire Court's Bargain doesn't have any such readily available loophole, because Fire rules the roost while those wards are down and being compelled to help restore them simply means picking one's moment and maybe giving the rest of the Court conflicted feelings about any concessions one might ask for.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T17:40:07-07:00","id":1541043,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain in simple terms how the Digital Hedge(BriarNet) works? Like, I have several questions that I find hard to understand.<br /> How difficult is to get in/out? How do you travel outside the Trods on the Information Superhighway? What exactly the Autonomous Payload contract does? Can you use a computer to open a Digital Hedge portal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T20:00:09-07:00","id":1541051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541043#post1541043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain in simple terms how the Digital Hedge(BriarNet) works?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a space within the Hedge accessed through its own Hedgeways (called nodes), much like the Halls of Mirrors or the Dreaming Roads; it allows characters to engage with digital data in metaphorical dressing the same way they would with the rest of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How difficult is to get in/out? </div> </div> </div>Traveling through a node to reach a destination in the Hedge makes travel very slightly harder (per The Hedge's notes on accessing BriarNet Goblin Markets), but reaching a node doesn't have to be a declared goal like the Gate of Horn or the Hall of Mirrors would be.<br /> <br /> Outside the context of its interfering with navigation, you have to Hedgespin a means of access symbolically appropriate to your current location in the Hedge with a six-success paradigm shift, and in order to physically get from the BriarNet to the real world you need to exit to the Hedge first. Locations referred to as BriarNet Caf\u00e9s can provide a ready place to make the jump from fairyland to the sprite-cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you travel outside the Trods on the Information Superhighway? </div> </div> </div>The same way you travel outside of trods in the regular Hedge. The Information Superhighway is just the spine of cyberspace, much as there's more to the Dreaming Roads than its eponymous trods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly the Autonomous Payload contract does? </div> </div> </div>Lets you poke around in the actual data of a networked device using Hedgespinning instead of simply meddling with the liminal space of the internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you use a computer to open a Digital Hedge portal? </div> </div> </div>A device used to access online Goblin Markets often enough will eventually develop into a dormant Hedgeway that leads to the BriarNet and can be opened from the inside by one-time Keys from its Goblin Markets (referred to as broadsides).<br /> <br /> Popular BriarNet Goblin Markets might develop trods routing metaphorical traffic toward them and doing too much online shopping might let a hobgoblin into your home through your PC, but developing a stable connection between reality and cyberspace would be huge news for the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T04:48:00-07:00","id":1541054,"title":"","content":"So, it is a 6 success paradigm shift to enter and another 6 success paradigm shift to exit the Digital Hedge?<br /> <br /> And the Autonomous Payload can be used(Activated) only when inside the Digital Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 08-27-2024, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T05:27:35-07:00","id":1541055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541054#post1541054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it is a 6 success paradigm shift to enter and another 6 success paradigm shift to exit the Digital Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing in the books indicating you need a paradigm shift to leave the Digital Hedge. The paradigm shift to enter is to leverage suitable digital symbolism like driving on a highway (of information) in an urban environment or (web) surfing in the vicinity of an ocean or climbing fiber optic cables between the points of light in the starry night sky; there isn't really a consistent analog counterpart to that since the rest of the Hedge is the full-spectrum breadth of symbolic options.<br /> <br /> Nodes are described in Kith and Kin as milestones representing mortal-work hardware on BriarNet-specific trods representing network connections, and are then described as analog-digital Hedgeways within the Hedge used to access the BriarNet in The Hedge, which says that passing through a node across the divide isn't significant enough to necessarily qualify as a goal for navigation purposes by itself.<br /> <br /> Given that The Hedge's additional information comes in the context of accessing Goblin Markets and most characters who aren't changelings, enTitled Huntsmen, or Fae can't use paradigm shifts, and given that the products of Hedgespinning tend to persist until shaped away (mechanical bonuses or penalties notwithstanding), it seems reasonable to parse the combined mechanics such that the Hedgespinning method is a shortcut allowing you to make use of the pervasive nature of the internet rather than an essential step in going in either direction across the digital divide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T06:19:41-07:00","id":1541057,"title":"","content":"Got it. So, suppose I can make a Hollow inside the BriarNet. Would getting the Easy Access enhancement still allow me to just unlock any door and go inside my Hollow inside the Digital Hedge?<br /> Rules wise, I don't see anything impeding that, but seems more like a RAW than RAI to me. Since its supposed to be really difficult to stablish a stable connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T07:54:31-07:00","id":1541061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541057#post1541057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it. So, suppose I can make a Hollow inside the BriarNet. Would getting the Easy Access enhancement still allow me to just unlock any door and go inside my Hollow inside the Digital Hedge?<br /> Rules wise, I don't see anything impeding that, but seems more like a RAW than RAI to me. Since its supposed to be really difficult to stablish a stable connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be inclined to agree, since Clouds are consistently described as corresponding to a secret web address and floating in the sky. The closest comparable situation I can think of would be that a Shared Bastion can spend half of its available dots to have a consistent entrance in a Hollow that itself can have Easy Access, but direct player-accessible physical routes between OpSpace and the BriarNet seem to be intended as off-limits in the game's presented defaults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541054#post1541054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Autonomous Payload can be used(Activated) only when inside the Digital Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The usage specifies standing on a trod within the BriarNet, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T11:04:24-07:00","id":1541300,"title":"","content":"When members of the Crystal Web free company cause Bedlam, what emotion (and Condition) would they be especially good at causing? <br /> <br /> They have a Bargain, they have a Mantle, I see no reason they wouldn't have a specialty (hell, the Bay City Marshals / Court of the Leafless Tree have TWO, iirc). Informed seems like a fairly on-brand Condition, but it lacks the kind of intoxication-that-can-go-too-far that Bedlam is all about imo. And I dunno how to describe that emotion in a useful way that lends itself to multiple reactions and interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T16:55:51-07:00","id":1541309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tristissima et alia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541300#post1541300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When members of the Crystal Web free company cause Bedlam, what emotion (and Condition) would they be especially good at causing?<br /> <br /> They have a Bargain, they have a Mantle, I see no reason they wouldn't have a specialty (hell, the Bay City Marshals / Court of the Leafless Tree have TWO, iirc). Informed seems like a fairly on-brand Condition, but it lacks the kind of intoxication-that-can-go-too-far that Bedlam is all about imo. And I dunno how to describe that emotion in a useful way that lends itself to multiple reactions and interpretations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the book they're introduced in, the Crystal Web is not a Court, and that means something.<br /> <br /> As a Free Company, the Silicon Guild has a non-traditional Mantle built on a weaker Bargain, meaning it has no Crown, cannot provide Goodwill to non-members, and does not favor any emotion for Bedlam (in addition to causing its benefits to lapse if its members don't successfully host the web-based gatherings described in their writeup at least once per story), but provides Allies dots equal to Mantle, makes Motley Merits more effective, and grants the ability to purchase the Royal Contract Donning the Grand Mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T16:30:51-07:00","id":1541710,"title":"","content":"Could you use the Hidden Reality contract to find a file or shortcut to a folder inside a computer, or even create such files with the Wizened blessing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T17:53:34-07:00","id":1541716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541710#post1541710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use the Hidden Reality contract to find a file or shortcut to a folder inside a computer, or even create such files with the Wizened blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that any changes the Contract makes have to be plausible for anyone who hasn't seen it established that they couldn't be there and that such changes vanish at the end of the scene or when nobody's paying attention to them (whichever comes first), sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T08:47:04-07:00","id":1541780,"title":"","content":"Is there anyway to live longer or become immortal other than becoming true fae or becoming empty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T09:18:42-07:00","id":1541781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541780#post1541780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anyway to live longer or become immortal other than becoming true fae or becoming empty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get extended lifespan for free with every dot of Wyrd and there are some entitlements that also extend their bearer's lifespan. Other than that, 1e provided a precedent for Goblin Contracts that can suspend or delay aging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T13:23:20-07:00","id":1541797,"title":"","content":"Goblin Fruits that extend life aren't a hard sell, either.<br /> <br /> While for narrative purposes they're better being rare and/or hard to properly prepare, lifespan is rarely an actual, relevant balance issue for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T15:22:05-07:00","id":1541807,"title":"","content":"That sounds appropriate for Changeling the Lost that special Goblin Fruits that can extend lifespans considerably should be rare and have a big drawback of some type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:13:45-07:00","id":1541813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541781#post1541781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get extended lifespan for free with every dot of Wyrd and there are some entitlements that also extend their bearer's lifespan. Other than that, 1e provided a precedent for Goblin Contracts that can suspend or delay aging.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are some entitlement that can extend lifespan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:42:01-07:00","id":1541816,"title":"","content":"The Giant merit is kinda worded ambiguously, but it only grants +1 Health due to Size, not +2 (+1 from Size and the mentioned +1 Health), correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T21:29:22-07:00","id":1541830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541813#post1541813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some entitlement that can extend lifespan?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of them are detailed; the one named in the Blessings and Curses subsection of Oak Ash &amp; Thorn is the Forever Queen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541816#post1541816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giant merit is kinda worded ambiguously, but it only grants +1 Health due to Size, not +2 (+1 from Size and the mentioned +1 Health), correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T22:04:14-07:00","id":1541834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1541813#post1541813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are some entitlement that can extend lifespan?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the Enteral Vizer style entitlement that will stop a Changelings aging process, but you have to at least a 7 in Wyrd, considerable knowledge of the Contracts and you serve the Freehold various seasonal monarchs and never take a front and center position in ruling as it violates the agreement and you will reach your true age. <br /> <br /> That entitlement was mainly used as t last resort to treat high Wyrd and low clarity Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T22:08:16-07:00","id":1541835,"title":"","content":"Another was the Lost Pantheon where the Changeling no longer sees themselves as remotely human and become something akin to gods. That entitlement was said to increase there lifespans. But the limitations were that you needed at least a Wyrd rating of 6, 4 dots in your court mantle and your Clarity could not be higher then 6 and the lower it was the better perception bonuses you would get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T04:46:29-07:00","id":1542042,"title":"","content":"How long do Hob Goblin and Hob Goblin Queen live?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T06:09:35-07:00","id":1542044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1542042#post1542042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long do Hob Goblin and Hob Goblin Queen live?</div> </div> </div> </div>As needed per specimen. It's not a metaphysical category that comes with agelessness or a universal set lifespan.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins run the gamut from little mayfly creatures to living landscape features and Goblin Queens are a subset of hobgoblins. Some of them will live until they're killed and others have lifespans measured in days. There are Goblin Contracts and Dread Powers that can preserve, extend, and/or steal life and the Hedge is a place where the flow of time is not always consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T07:25:45-07:00","id":1542045,"title":"","content":"What are some Goblin Contract and Dread Power that can preserve, extend, and/or steal life?<br /> <br /> Does Changeling age slower when they in the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T08:26:15-07:00","id":1542052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1542045#post1542045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some Goblin Contract and Dread Power that can preserve, extend, and/or steal life?<br /> <br /> Does Changeling age slower when they in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a 1st edition Goblin Contract that could extend the target life for 7 years.<br /> On 2nd edition, there is the effects Wyrd, that extend the lifespan of changelings.<br /> Also, there is some hints about Titles or Bargains that can grant eternal youth, but nothing stated with rules.<br /> <br /> Changelings age normally on the Hedge, but some places on the Hedge(usually near Arcadia) have a funny timescale, so you could spend 2 years inside the hedge, aging 2 years, but coming out in like a couple days for everyone outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:28:11-07:00","id":1542057,"title":"","content":"Yes time works funny in Acardia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:37:17-07:00","id":1542060,"title":"","content":"Assuming they know about the materials, can a Wizened blessing turn Metals into their Perfected versions, like Gold into Orichalcum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:59:12-07:00","id":1542064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1542060#post1542060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming they know about the materials, can a Wizened blessing turn Metals into their Perfected versions, like Gold into Orichalcum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Mage doesn't allow unalloyed perfected metals to be made uniformly Lasting via spell and the Wizened blessing doesn't have a duration on its effect (to say nothing of the fact that the blessing doesn't have any requirements on what material is being turned into what material), I'd say definitely not on its own.<br /> <br /> You might develop a Merit that enhances the blessing's scope or get ahold of a rare Contract that enables it instead, but the Wizened blessing already treats turning normal mundane materials into other normal mundane materials as a Build Equipment action of the highest possible difficulty, and allowing it to make lasting specimens of a magical material that takes at least a couple dozen trips through other dimensions with no more difficulty than turning twigs into plastic straws feels firmly out-of-scope with a power placed equivalent to being very intimidating, spending Willpower on behalf of other people, treating nearby elements as extensions of yourself, merging with smoke, or being faster and more dangerous in hand-to-hand combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T09:03:19-07:00","id":1542820,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a changeling to sell one or more of her Contracts? Like, not teaching them, but selling, losting it in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T15:54:44-07:00","id":1543224,"title":"","content":"I don't know Horodrigo, I can't honestly not seeing a problem with it as Changelings gain powers through pledges/oaths and it could fall under it, but maybe Satchel can give a definite answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T17:04:22-07:00","id":1543230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1542820#post1542820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a changeling to sell one or more of her Contracts? Like, not teaching them, but selling, losting it in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypothetically almost anything that belongs to you can be sold to goblins, though mechanically there's no special process for it.<br /> <br /> A changeling who has become a Hedge Denizen can sell Goblin Contracts they know to applicable buyers using the systems described in the corebook and The Hedge.<br /> <br /> The worth of a given Contract may be skewed by the means by which you got it any any strings attached, but I don't see any reasonable explanation for a negotiated power over reality to be less saleable than a kith or an Icon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T17:48:43-07:00","id":1543234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1543230#post1543230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hypothetically almost anything that belongs to you can be sold to goblins, though mechanically there's no special process for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems similar to Demon Pacts, is defined anywhere what counts enough as <b>yours </b>to be sold?<br /> <br /> I want to sell my capacity for aging, feasible? Does it make me unaging? I imagine a very unintended consequences as you owing your future aging days to the Hobgoblin.<br /> <br /> But what if I want sell my lung cancer at least? Does it cure me?<br /> <br /> Or my marriage? The marriage case sounds interesting because if it is yours, it is also your spouse's, how much can you sell something that is shared?<br /> <br /> Could a Vampire/Werewolf/etc sell its Vampiric/Werewolf/etc condition?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T18:13:07-07:00","id":1543236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1543234#post1543234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems similar to Demon Pacts, is defined anywhere what counts enough as <b>yours </b>to be sold?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want to sell my capacity for aging, feasible? </div> </div> </div>Not without some serious changes in assumptions about how the setting works. Agelessness through a goblin bargain is typically a knock-on consequence of agreement for something else. The effects of time on mortal biology (or reasonable facsimiles thereof) are terms you agreed to by being born living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what if I want sell my lung cancer at least? </div> </div> </div>Selling something that is an impediment to you is more typically referred to in terms of buying relief. You'd be trading for the means of getting rid of it or convincing whatever creditor benefits from you having lung cancer to sell a debt they're theoretically collecting on by your disease, when selling debt is conventionally done to get reduced returns from the buyer rather than none at all from the debtor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or my marriage? The marriage case sounds interesting because if it is yours, it is also your spouse's, how much can you sell something that is shared? </div> </div> </div>You can sell your side of a relationship to something with the means and motivation to buy it, and that's managed in whatever way is contextually appropriate to how they collect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a Vampire/Werewolf/etc sell its Vampiric/Werewolf/etc condition? </div> </div> </div>No hard &quot;no&quot;s, but see the note about disease and the note about relationships. Few if any goblins are likely to have the pull and gall to disinherit Moon's children or prune the family trees of the great Curses, especially given that if they were able to undo the Fae's handiwork in the template closest to their own metaphysical framework (outside the context of a unique plot device) it would've come up in the fiction somewhere in either edition.<br /> <br /> The theoretical universality of fae trading does not override the fact that it's a market built on incentives for buying and selling. Being theoretically capable of selling personal possession of the worst luck in the world doesn't matter if you can't find anybody willing to buy it even for a pittance, because the handling equipment for various maladies and abstractions is not part of every goblin's toolkit and arranging for it has costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T19:36:32-07:00","id":1543240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1543234#post1543234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems similar to Demon Pacts, is defined anywhere what counts enough as <b>yours </b>to be sold?<br /> <br /> I want to sell my capacity for aging, feasible? Does it make me unaging? <br /> <br /> That might be beyond the capacity of the Wryd as it would entail lots of conditions. Such as you can stay ageless in Arcadia or the Hedge and if you return to our world. The biological clock restarts again with sometimes dramatic results or you can must ingest a goblin fruit or trinket but has major drawbacks in using it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what if I want sell my lung cancer at least? Does it cure me?<br /> <br /> I can see Goblins selling relief from the pains of cancer for future consideration.<br /> <br /> Could a Vampire/Werewolf/etc sell its Vampiric/Werewolf/etc condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even back bin the 1st edition this was a hard no and even in Mage The Awakening that it wasn't sure if archmasters could even undo a vampire or lupine supernatural nature and I don't think that even the god like True Fae could pull off an agreement.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T20:23:51-08:00","id":1547839,"title":"","content":"If the Gristlegrinder eats a vampire, what damage does the vampire get from the acid? Lethal or bashing?<br /> <br /> Also, if the swallowed enemy deals less then 5 damage in one strike to the Gristlegrinder, does the Gristlegrinder actually takes this damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 01-20-2025, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T05:34:49-08:00","id":1547845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1547839#post1547839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Gristlegrinder eats a vampire, what damage does the vampire get from the acid? Lethal or bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that To Serve Man requires successfully grappling a target that is smaller than them and them a successful Stamina + Survival roll that costs Glamour to swallow them, as well as the fact that chemicals are one of the sources of aggravated damage described that vampires still take lethal damage from, I'd say lethal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if the swallowed enemy deals less then 5 damage in one strike to the Gristlegrinder, does the Gristlegrinder actually takes this damage? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though the fact that targets needed to be grappled to end up in there suggests the possibility that while such attacks ignore Defense and Armor they may still be handled as grapple checks to perform the Damage maneuver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T05:23:08-08:00","id":1547999,"title":"","content":"Is it possible, and does it comply with the rules, to interrupt or make it impossible for a changeling to enact a contract by denying a required condition (such as the ability to speak, vision, or the use of an item for certain contracts)?<br /> It is not directly referenced in the rules (CtL 2nd Ed), but to me, this seems logical.<br /> It also seems logical that some contracts cannot be stopped this way - specifically in cases where the contract text does not reference any such condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28462-gerleim","name":"gerleim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T06:22:13-08:00","id":1548001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1543240#post1543240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even back bin the 1st edition this was a hard no and even in Mage The Awakening that it wasn't sure if archmasters could even undo a vampire or lupine supernatural nature and I don't think that even the god like True Fae could pull off an agreement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Resurrection Numen (Chronicles of Darkness, p. 138) can resurrect a dead supernatural as: &quot;Mages become Sleepwalkers, and werewolves, wolf-blooded.&quot; Won't work on Vampires, &quot;Supernatural beings that have already died as part of their transformation \u2014 vampires, mummies, and Sin-Eaters \u2014 can\u2019t be resurrected&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> On a side note, I don't think there's anything that excludes Changelings - they might resurrect as Fae-touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28462-gerleim","name":"gerleim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T14:06:09-08:00","id":1548008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gerleim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1547999#post1547999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible, and does it comply with the rules, to interrupt or make it impossible for a changeling to enact a contract by denying a required condition (such as the ability to speak, vision, or the use of an item for certain contracts)?<br /> It is not directly referenced in the rules (CtL 2nd Ed), but to me, this seems logical.<br /> It also seems logical that some contracts cannot be stopped this way - specifically in cases where the contract text does not reference any such condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that paying Glamour instead of utilizing a Contract's Loophole is the most likely vector for &quot;preventing a changeling from using a Contract&quot; outside of more generalized measures like iron or anti-magical supernatural powers, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T16:24:48-08:00","id":1548380,"title":"","content":"Have any you tried to create your own Contracts by following the guidelines in Equinox Road? If so how hard was it to make it seem proper for the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T19:38:06-07:00","id":1551795,"title":"","content":"In the Striding Through section under Hedge Sorcery, it says that the Witches player <i>may</i> generate Hedgespinning successes to apply to an upcoming Conjuring, not <i>must</i>. Is it intended that a player <i>must</i> begin a Conjuring with banked Hedgespinning successes equal to Doors +2, followed by a Paradigm Shift? Or is this method meant as an option/alternative to rolling for the successes to open a Door? (ie. instead of rolling Presence or Manipulation + Occult + Wyrd vs whatever, the banked Hedgespinning success is used?)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T22:54:20-07:00","id":1551798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1551795#post1551795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Striding Through section under Hedge Sorcery, it says that the Witches player <i>may</i> generate Hedgespinning successes to apply to an upcoming Conjuring, not <i>must</i>. Is it intended that a player <i>must</i> begin a Conjuring with banked Hedgespinning successes equal to Doors +2, followed by a Paradigm Shift? Or is this method meant as an option/alternative to rolling for the successes to open a Door? (ie. instead of rolling Presence or Manipulation + Occult + Wyrd vs whatever, the banked Hedgespinning success is used?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that's &quot;You <i>may</i> generate Hedgespinning successes as normal <i>at any time during the scene</i>,&quot; as opposed to, say, having to split your focus during the extended action to open the Doors; the subsequent section on Teamwork describes how the players can pool their banked Hedgespinning successes to collect enough to begin the conjuring, so it's evidently not optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T10:13:38-07:00","id":1553039,"title":"","content":"Hi! does the Elemental Seeming Benefit of the Thistle\u2019s Rebuke Contract(from Kith &amp; Kin) allow to regrow the thorns faster after firing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T12:23:26-07:00","id":1553042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553039#post1553039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! does the Elemental Seeming Benefit of the Thistle\u2019s Rebuke Contract(from Kith &amp; Kin) allow to regrow the thorns faster after firing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the function seems to be allowing the changeling to control whether contact with her deals damage from turn to turn, I would say no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T13:06:36-07:00","id":1553044,"title":"","content":"If a player starts the game with an appropriate mentor, could their Changeling begin the game with the Seeming Benefits of their Mentor's Seeming as well as that of their own Seeming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T13:27:13-07:00","id":1553045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553044#post1553044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player starts the game with an appropriate mentor, could their Changeling begin the game with the Seeming Benefits of their Mentor's Seeming as well as that of their own Seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div>It costs an Experience per benefit and requires a personal oath to be defined, so even without the statement of &quot;you'd need to clear it with the ST&quot; it's not happening in a game where you aren't starting with bonus Experiences or e.g. allowing starting Merit dots to be spent as Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T10:42:36-07:00","id":1553327,"title":"","content":"So, first post I have made in a while. I have a question on Talon and Wing that has proven weirdly contentious when I asked elsewhere. I apologize for the length, I just need to elaborate on this a bit;<br /> <br /> Talon and Wing's first option effect is thus: &quot;The character gains the mode of transportation of a beast, increasing his Speed by 10.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most people I have brought this up with state that it obviously means it allows flying, since it's &quot;a mode of transportation&quot;... but they then disagree this means that they get a spider's means to climb walls or a cricket's ability to jump far, even though those are modes of transportation that are relatively plausible for a person to emulate compared to unaided flight, bringing up other contracts do those effects.<br /> <br /> What bothers me about this is that across the current 2e materials there are a few different means and methods for flight, but each of them comes with an explicit drawback;<br /> <b>Chrysalis</b> requires you to become an animal, and most animals that can fly are not as durable as a mundane person, nor can they do contracts. On top of this, being an animal limits what kinds of actions you're able to do (at least without significant difficulty).<br /> <br /> <b>Props and Scenery</b> likewise requires that you become an object that can fly under its own power, like an arial drone, but this is even more limited than an animal would be as they are a lot more rigid.<br /> <br /> <b>Riding The Falling Leaves</b> turns you into flying leaves, which can interact <i>even less</i> with the physical world unless you get an exceptional success, and cuts your speed down as well.<br /> <br /> The <b>Draconic</b> kith (and any other that uses its Trickery) does allow for flight, and boosted at that (speed 60 is no joke), but not only does it last for turns equal to your Wyrd before you need to spend a glamour for it to activate again, you have to be in your fae form for it to work.<br /> <br /> There may be others, but the point I'm trying to make is that all options for explicit flight have a number of conditions to them, which they all go into detail over. Talon and Wing, by comparison, has a single sentence over it, no details, no drawbacks - you go up by 10 speed, you don't need to change form at all and you can even select other options from Talon and Wing for it in one go. It simply doesn't match any of the other examples' design logic, not even a &quot;including flying&quot; line.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something obvious here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T11:11:18-07:00","id":1553328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553327#post1553327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, first post I have made in a while. I have a question on Talon and Wing that has proven weirdly contentious when I asked elsewhere. I apologize for the length, I just need to elaborate on this a bit;<br /> <br /> Talon and Wing's first option effect is thus: &quot;The character gains the mode of transportation of a beast, increasing his Speed by 10.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most people I have brought this up with state that it obviously means it allows flying, since it's &quot;a mode of transportation&quot;... but they then disagree this means that they get a spider's means to climb walls or a cricket's ability to jump far, even though those are modes of transportation that are relatively plausible for a person to emulate compared to unaided flight, bringing up other contracts do those effects.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> There may be others, but the point I'm trying to make is that all options for explicit flight have a number of conditions to them, which they all go into detail over. Talon and Wing, by comparison, has a single sentence over it, no details, no drawbacks - you go up by 10 speed, you don't need to change form at all and you can even select other options from Talon and Wing for it in one go. It simply doesn't match any of the other examples' design logic, not even a &quot;including flying&quot; line.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something obvious here?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it right, Talon and Wing's &quot;mode of transport&quot; option just increases your Speed by 10 \u2014 adding a whole new movement axis would be like interpreting &quot;The character gains the senses of a beast&quot; to mean they can see in the ultraviolet or infrared spectrum or interpreting &quot;gains the claws of a beast&quot; to provide a different damage profile because different creatures can have more dangerous claws.<br /> <br /> &quot;A beast&quot; is an abstraction for the purposes of this Contract that provides the mechanical benefits described that you choose from the menu and any others you have from seeming bonuses and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T11:19:52-07:00","id":1553329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553327#post1553327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, first post I have made in a while. I have a question on Talon and Wing that has proven weirdly contentious when I asked elsewhere. I apologize for the length, I just need to elaborate on this a bit;<br /> <br /> Talon and Wing's first option effect is thus: &quot;The character gains the mode of transportation of a beast, increasing his Speed by 10.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most people I have brought this up with state that it obviously means it allows flying, since it's &quot;a mode of transportation&quot;... but they then disagree this means that they get a spider's means to climb walls or a cricket's ability to jump far, even though those are modes of transportation that are relatively plausible for a person to emulate compared to unaided flight, bringing up other contracts do those effects.<br /> <br /> What bothers me about this is that across the current 2e materials there are a few different means and methods for flight, but each of them comes with an explicit drawback;<br /> <b>Chrysalis</b> requires you to become an animal, and most animals that can fly are not as durable as a mundane person, nor can they do contracts. On top of this, being an animal limits what kinds of actions you're able to do (at least without significant difficulty).<br /> <br /> <b>Props and Scenery</b> likewise requires that you become an object that can fly under its own power, like an arial drone, but this is even more limited than an animal would be as they are a lot more rigid.<br /> <br /> <b>Riding The Falling Leaves</b> turns you into flying leaves, which can interact <i>even less</i> with the physical world unless you get an exceptional success, and cuts your speed down as well.<br /> <br /> The <b>Draconic</b> kith (and any other that uses its Trickery) does allow for flight, and boosted at that (speed 60 is no joke), but not only does it last for turns equal to your Wyrd before you need to spend a glamour for it to activate again, you have to be in your fae form for it to work.<br /> <br /> There may be others, but the point I'm trying to make is that all options for explicit flight have a number of conditions to them, which they all go into detail over. Talon and Wing, by comparison, has a single sentence over it, no details, no drawbacks - you go up by 10 speed, you don't need to change form at all and you can even select other options from Talon and Wing for it in one go. It simply doesn't match any of the other examples' design logic, not even a &quot;including flying&quot; line.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something obvious here?</div> </div> </div> </div>On reading Talon and Wing, it is clear that the intended contract is to either:<br /> Increase your character's speed by 10<br /> Add a 3 die bonus to perception rolls<br /> Give them a +0L unarmed attack.<br /> <br /> The fact that the contract has the word wing in it, and mentions dreams of flying doesn't seem to coincide with the mechanics as presented, and that may be where the &quot;contraversy&quot; is coming from.<br /> <br /> I guess it depends on your table how you want to run things. And whether it is unbalanced compared to other methods of flying.<br /> <br /> Or a combination of those three depending on how much glamour is spent.<br /> <br /> It says nothing mechanically about flying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T11:59:41-07:00","id":1553333,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for the rapid replies. In a similar vein, where I got likewise contentious replies, is it weird for an elemental to be able to make mundane perception rolls and speak via their element? (A gemstone elemental being able to peer and whisper through others' jewelry at a party, for example) I kept getting told that &quot;actions =/= actions&quot;, aka something you roll for doesn't count as a mundane action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:12:23-07:00","id":1553334,"title":"","content":"The elemental blessing is to act through your element by touch or suffusion. In the party example, you don't have a link of touch or suffusion through the element. The jewelry is over there, you're not touching or suffused with it. Think of your choice of element as something that can serve as a conduit or connector. Fire, steam, frost, water: if you're steeped in it, you can shape it up to three yards away in ways that accomplish mundane tasks. An earth elemental could stand on the bare earth and use the elemental blessing to reach up and knock over an object sitting on the ground from underneath. Whether your ST considers peering and whispering to be valid for the blessing is a judgment call (I think I would allow it), but my take is that you need that physical connection to reach through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:44:41-07:00","id":1553337,"title":"","content":"That is a sensible read on it; I had interpreted it as more of a network, where so long as you had a touch to one example of it, any others within the three meter radius would also react to you. Otherwise, certain esoteric or specific elements are harder to work with. On the plus side, that also makes for a nice limiter to the old &quot;air element vs wind element&quot; chestnut, even if it's still an overly strong element on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T14:34:04-07:00","id":1553611,"title":"","content":"On the Changeling 2E character sheet, there are numbers beneath the Clarity boxes. What are they for? I cannot find an answer in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","name":"csctnfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T15:00:21-07:00","id":1553613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>csctnfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553611#post1553611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Changeling 2E character sheet, there are numbers beneath the Clarity boxes. What are they for? I cannot find an answer in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indicating which Touchstone is attached to that Clarity box using the numbered list immediately below the track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T16:06:30-07:00","id":1553614,"title":"","content":"Okay! That makes sense. Thank you!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","name":"csctnfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T18:21:44-07:00","id":1553781,"title":"","content":"How does fae cunning interact with situations that reduce a character's defense, ie. attacked by multiple opponents, making an all-out attack and armor penalties?<br /> <br /> Does the contract allow them to keep full defense through supernatural means (body doubles, preternatural speed, or improbable ricochets) or is their defense still reduced, like a strain on their wyrd as they get overwhelmed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T18:46:31-07:00","id":1553784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553781#post1553781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does fae cunning interact with situations that reduce a character's defense, ie. attacked by multiple opponents, making an all-out attack and armor penalties?<br /> <br /> Does the contract allow them to keep full defense through supernatural means (body doubles, preternatural speed, or improbable ricochets) or is their defense still reduced, like a strain on their wyrd as they get overwhelmed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fae Cunning makes the character ignore effects that would ignore their Defense. It does not interact with effects that simply reduce their Defense rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T21:07:01-07:00","id":1553789,"title":"","content":"Questions for when a changeling uses its regalia manifestation for the the Koschei the Deathless like effect.<br /> <br /> How strict is the \u201cshort ritual\u201d? Can it be performed during an action scene (eg. in the middle of combat)?<br /> <br /> How hidden must the manifestation be? Is simply slipping it into a pocket or leaving it in plain sight acceptable for a dramatic reveal later on?<br /> <br /> The manifestation doesn\u2019t have to stay on the changeling\u2019s person. But how is it handled if the manifestation is an item they're actively using, like a sword or amulet they\u2019re wearing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T06:30:32-07:00","id":1553797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553789#post1553789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How strict is the \u201cshort ritual\u201d? Can it be performed during an action scene (eg. in the middle of combat)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the ritual needed to make a temporary manifestation on the same page, one turn, or six seconds outside of an action scene, but considering example rituals include stuff like filling a Chalice with wine and putting it in a cabinet or burying it, narrative and Initiative should probably also be considered re: whether it's feasible in a given moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How hidden must the manifestation be? Is simply slipping it into a pocket or leaving it in plain sight acceptable for a dramatic reveal later on? </div> </div> </div>I would say plain sight is probably too much unless you're doing a needle-in-a-haystack sort of thing, but the crux of it to my mind is that the ritual you're performing is thematically appropriate to the Regalia in question; you're gating your death behind a puzzle for the scene, and the solution to that puzzle requires whoever wants to kill you to know, suspect, or figure out that you possess a Regalia capable of such a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The manifestation doesn\u2019t have to stay on the changeling\u2019s person. But how is it handled if the manifestation is an item they're actively using, like a sword or amulet they\u2019re wearing? </div> </div> </div>Considering both the famous example you yourself cite at the top of this post and the description of the ritual as being performed &quot;over the spot where [you hide] it,&quot; I would say you have to hide it somewhere that is not on your person; the effect only says it doesn't have to be on hand because that's a universal requirement of Regalia abilities unless otherwise stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T19:25:02-07:00","id":1553803,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thanks for the response, its really helpful, <span style=\"color:black\">but I\u2019m still wrestling with the strong emphasis on the concealment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">Mechanically, the effect (and any temporary manifestation) lasts only for a scene. If someone gets their hands on the manifestation, they can usurp it and end the effect early, or wait out the scene. That makes sense to me as the &quot;solution to the puzzle&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">Here are a few examples I\u2019m thinking about, and whether or not they &quot;work&quot; within the intended boundaries:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">- Sword theme; A Summer courtier plants the freehold\u2019s flag in the ground, swearing to fight until the banner falls. Her death is now pinned beneath it.<br /> - </span><span style=\"color:black\">Shield theme; A Darkling closes her mother\u2019s pocket watch after setting it to the time she always wished they\u2019d had more of together. If she leaves it behind, it might buy her just enough time to escape.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:black\">- Mirror/Jewels theme: Sisyphus, on his second escape from death, whispers final instructions to his wife before he\u2019s dragged to the Underworld. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">Merope doesn\u2019t get buried or locked in a cupboard, but this is exactly how I imagine using a touchstone manifestation with this effect active, if allowed by the rules, would play out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">My instinct is that as long as the ritual is narratively appropriate, placing the token/person/fetch/icon in \u201cplain sight\u201d should be valid.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">Still, am I overlooking any thematic or mechanical reasons for why strict concealment might matter more than I\u2019m giving it credit for?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T16:45:32-07:00","id":1553820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553803#post1553803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, am I overlooking any thematic or mechanical reasons for why strict concealment might matter more than I\u2019m giving it credit for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Separation of a vulnerability and the same dramaturgical forces that a galoshin uses to confuse the Wyrd into thinking you are your hated enemy: from a practical standpoint, this use of a manifested Regalia exists to force someone who wants to kill you to either leave you alone or commit resources to being in two different locations (or at least physically moving you or preventing you from being moved), and the narrative being spun for &quot;find my death and crack the egg of its potential&quot; doesn't work if your death is held in a thing you are still holding on your person or standing directly in front of; it's there as a way to help you not die, not to make you bodily imperishable as long as you keep a particular ring in your pocket \u2014 this is a different process from becoming one of the Empty, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T05:02:32-07:00","id":1553834,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Okay, so correct me if I\u2019m mistaken; the ritual isn\u2019t really about sealing away the changeling\u2019s death as some kind of death-ward. That kind of magic would be too blatant a violation of the bargain between life-and-death, far too gauche for a little changeling. No clause entitles them to such authority. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">What it <i>does</i> instead is trick death with sleight-of-hand: symbolic misdirection that hides the changeling\u2019s life just long enough to temporarily fool causality, like a ball hidden under a magician\u2019s cup. In my analogy the changeling\u2019s body and their regalia manifestation are the cups, dressed up to look the same, and their life now exists in some quantum state between the two. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:black\">this use of a manifested Regalia exists to force someone who wants to kill you to either leave you alone or commit resources to being in two different locations (or at least physically moving you or preventing you from being moved)</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:black\">From what I understand, once your health track is full, you begin rolling to stay conscious and start bleeding out. As long as you're conscious, you can continue acting in the scene (even with a full track of aggravated damage). There\u2019s a narrow window to reach safety before the curtain falls on the scene. </span><span style=\"color:black\">If you lose consciousness, you're effectively dead, but in a kind of \u201cplaying possum\u201d way. If your attacker walks away, there\u2019s still a slim chance an ally could step in and revive you.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:black\">it's there as a way to help you not die, not to make you bodily imperishable as long as you keep a particular ring in your pocket</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:black\">But\u2026 doesn\u2019t it <i>kind of</i> make you bodily imperishable, at least for a little while? Just with the ring \u201cover there\u201d instead of \u201con you\u201d? That\u2019s the vibe I\u2019m picking up.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T16:48:41-07:00","id":1553843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1553834#post1553834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so correct me if I\u2019m mistaken; the ritual isn\u2019t really about sealing away the changeling\u2019s death as some kind of death-ward. That kind of magic would be too blatant a violation of the bargain between life-and-death, far too gauche for a little changeling. No clause entitles them to such authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes. You would need an actual Contract or the more dramatic alteration of becoming Empty to have the effect be a straightforward &quot;I can't die unless break this rock you can clearly see&quot; sort of thing.<br /> <br /> It lasts for a scene as a concession to it being a limited-use single power of an item that can have multiple such powers that can't be stocked up far ahead of time and incentivizing you to drop the reveal to your assailant in some way to keep them from sticking around you long enough to shank you when the cameras start rolling again, moreso than as an arbitrarily long countdown to renewed vulnerability. You do this before a potentially lethal situation that you think you can get out of with this extra bit of insurance rather than before diving into a lake of fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I understand, once your health track is full, you begin rolling to stay conscious and start bleeding out. As long as you're conscious, you can continue acting in the scene (even with a full track of aggravated damage). There\u2019s a narrow window to reach safety before the curtain falls on the scene. If you lose consciousness, you're effectively dead, but in a kind of \u201cplaying possum\u201d way. If your attacker walks away, there\u2019s still a slim chance an ally could step in and revive you. </div> </div> </div>I'd say mechanically the effect stops your last box of lethal damage from converting to agg before the scene ends, but otherwise yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But\u2026 doesn\u2019t it <i>kind of</i> make you bodily imperishable, at least for a little while? Just with the ring \u201cover there\u201d instead of \u201con you\u201d? That\u2019s the vibe I\u2019m picking up. </div> </div> </div>I will clarify my meaning: The effect is clearly not meant to make &quot;you are personally serving as an obstacle to the destruction of the thing that needs to be destroyed to kill you in a human-mortality version of putting a key behind its own lock&quot; a legitimate narrative outcome \u2014 if you want to make it harder for someone to get to your Regalia, you put other people and obstacles in front of it and keep away for the rest of the scene, and if you want to take advantage of your Regalia allowing you to not die, you do it away from the Regalia instead of adding a particular called shot mechanic to the duel to the death you're about to engage in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T03:40:32-07:00","id":1553852,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that phrasing <i>&quot;putting a key behind its own lock&quot;</i> really nails it for me. I was circling around the concept but hadn\u2019t quite landed on that imagery. It clears up a lot about the intent behind how the effect is supposed to function. Thanks for breaking it down. I think this all clicks now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","user":"Arrested Scrimshank","date":". 09-16-2025, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T02:40:24-07:00","id":1554288,"title":"","content":"Our oath sworn motley includes a Playmate and a Gristlegrinder.<br /> <br /> Per the rules each member can, once per chapter, when representing their motley, use another member\u2019s kith blessing.<br /> <br /> So here's the situation: the Playmate is separated from the motley and fending for themselves in the hedge, while the Gristlegrinder has escaped with an injured companion.<br /> <br /> Could the Playmate use the Gristlegrinder\u2019s kith blessing once per chapter to try and eat a hobgoblin?<br /> <br /> Likewise, could the Gristlegrinder use the Playmate\u2019s blessing to heal the injured companion member's wounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T07:37:32-07:00","id":1554292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1554288#post1554288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our oath sworn motley includes a Playmate and a Gristlegrinder.<br /> <br /> Per the rules each member can, once per chapter, when representing their motley, use another member\u2019s kith blessing.<br /> <br /> So here's the situation: the Playmate is separated from the motley and fending for themselves in the hedge, while the Gristlegrinder has escaped with an injured companion.<br /> <br /> Could the Playmate use the Gristlegrinder\u2019s kith blessing once per chapter to try and eat a hobgoblin?<br /> <br /> Likewise, could the Gristlegrinder use the Playmate\u2019s blessing to heal the injured companion member's wounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the rest of the text of that option, I'm pretty sure that's just talking about the lowered exceptional success threshold; the option is very clearly socially-oriented, and the inclusion of &quot;present in the group&quot; in the verbiage suggests it's not for when you're split up so much as when you want your spokesperson to do as well as they can on a roll \u2014 &quot;you can use your motleymate's Trickery arbitrarily once per chapter&quot; is dramatically more substantial than teamwork on Contract rolls or evenly splitting everyone's Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T16:21:32-07:00","id":1554297,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That\u2019s fair. It <i>is</i> a substantial option, exactly why I\u2019m asking the question.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m wondering if kith &quot;trickery&quot; is maybe more of a 1e holdover? But in 2e, the wording around the societal oaths open some interpretive space.<br /> <br /> Thematically, I immediately thought of a Court herald going to negotiate with another Court\u2019s ruler. Even though the rest of their motley isn\u2019t physically present, the symbolic weight of their oath is. All the motley\u2019s presence is felt through the herald\u2019s words and actions. Maybe the group is known to have painted marvellous dream landscapes. So, when the monarch asks for a portrait as the price for aid, it makes sense that the herald can use their Artist mate\u2019s tools of the trade, even if the Artist isn\u2019t physically there.<br /> <br /> The social focus of the oath is clear; social oath, social impact\u2026 but I don\u2019t think that necessarily restricts the scope only to social <i>manoeuvring</i>. To me, the lowered exceptional success threshold seems like it's intended for more than just schmoozing monarchs or winning debates. It should apply to things like hedgespinning and oniromancy.<br /> <br /> I picture it like: \u201cI\u2019m up against a wall, but I saw my motleymate once convince a wall to turn into stairs. They\u2019re not here, but through our oath, I can channel a bit of that same skill, once per chapter, and maybe have an easier time of convincing it too.\u201d The power of friendship has made the obstacle easier to overcome.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It reminds me a bit of how the pupil\u2019s devotion personal oath works, which lets you access an oath bound teacher\u2019s contact seeming benefit across any distance, as often as needed. In contrast, the societal oath gives you a single use of a single motleymate\u2019s kith blessing once per chapter. That\u2019s a much more limited mechanical effect, but still thematically consistent.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maybe what I\u2019m describing veers more into storyteller-approved personal oath territory? Similar to how a pair can share damage or conditions over distance. Given how broad magic in changeling is and how important motifs and metaphor are, I think there's room for it. If not RAW, then certainly RAI.<br /> <br /> Curious how others would run this at their table.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","user":"Arrested Scrimshank","date":". 10-10-2025, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T18:27:34-08:00","id":1555831,"title":"","content":"So I'm planning on homebrewing an entitlement based on the headless Horseman. My main question is... can an entitlement let a changeling survive not having their head attached or wearing other people's head for peak thematic imagery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T19:37:12-08:00","id":1555836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1555831#post1555831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm planning on homebrewing an entitlement based on the headless Horseman. My main question is... can an entitlement let a changeling survive not having their head attached or wearing other people's head for peak thematic imagery?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would depend pretty heavily on your mechanical and narrative definition of either of those qualities. Higher Wyrd generally enables greater flexibility in diverging from the standard human body plan and entitlements can have Wyrd prerequisites, but the nature of entitlements as <i>fungible identities</i> with duties and badges of office suggest you may need to figure out what you actually want this thing to be <i>for</i> besides the imagery if you want it to be attached to a station instead of, say, a kith blessing or a Goblin Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T04:02:40-08:00","id":1555908,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:15px\">How do the True Fae use hedge spinning and oneiromancy when it comes to changing another character\u2019s form?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Under sealing, there\u2019s an example of a True Fae turning someone into a weasel.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Under oneiromancy, paradigm shifts can turn a person into a cockroach (as opposed to Hedge Shifts, which affect the environment only).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Under the Faerie template, it says True Fae can perform any oneiromantic or hedge dpinning action and treat other characters as eidolons.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">It also says they automatically succeed at these actions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Is this the mechanism by which rrue fae transforms a character into something?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">(i.e., they\u2019re treating the target as an eidolon and applying a Paradigm Shift )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Where it says they \u201cautomatically succeed,\u201d does that mean they still roll, automatically &quot;succeed&quot; but need to hit the required successes?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">OR</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">they do not roll at all and the effect is considered successful for the intended outcome of transforming someone into a weasle?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">I\u2019m wondering if true fae transformations operate on a similar logic to </span><span style=\"font-size:15px\">ORT from the Fate series, whos reality marble transforms anything/anyone within it into the environment</span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> of Mercury.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Does the Fae overwrite a being\u2019s nature to match their own story logic/thematic domain while within dreams and the hedge? (i.e a fairy tale fae might make hero's brave while damsel's are in distress ect.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T07:40:53-08:00","id":1555911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1555908#post1555908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the True Fae use hedge spinning and oneiromancy when it comes to changing another character\u2019s form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, they don't. They use Contracts, tokens, Regalia, and other abilities, much like there's no paradigm shift for turning an eidolon into a bauble.<br /> <br /> Since the &quot;do the impossible&quot; dreamweaving paradigm shift is the only instance of this in those sections and doesn't have an expiration condition and everything else is pretty clear that you can't really mess with important eidolons beyond the level of imposing Conditions, it seems prudent to interpret the offhand weasel transformation in the sealing section as referring to the kind of powers a Stranger may have.<br /> <br /> By pretty much every metric the Fae have used historically in this game, automatic success without a roll on interpersonal effects doesn't fly; my interpretation would be that they still have to take relevant mundane actions, roll for them at the applicable penalty, and spend the necessary Glamour, but the roll doesn't need to allocate successes between the mundane effect and the Hedgespinning/dreamweaving effects.<br /> <br /> The edition's material on dramaturgy makes it pretty plain that the Fae have their powers by emulating the other parties to their pledgecraft through the medium of the Wyrd, such that a King of Black Cats can turn things into black cats because that's something the conceptual root of Black Cats that lends its name to and benefits from the Title can do (whether by amplifying feline traits, propagating a bit of itself into the world like a kitty version of Sun Wukong's hair-clone trick, evoking the &quot;void cats&quot; phenomenon on anything dark enough, etc).<br /> <br /> Wholesale transformation of another character is a degree of violence that is kind of beyond the scope of the semi-passive/environmental powers of the shaping mechanics for much the same reason that, while wandering in the Hedge may turn you into a hobgoblin whose form may change as you make deals, no amount of casual fae exposure is going to turn you into a quadroped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T13:12:20-08:00","id":1556186,"title":"","content":"Do Gentry ever abduct other supernaturals? I know you can't change major templates even if the Gentry tried, but it seems a bit unlikely one of the Others wouldn't occasionally want an exotic pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:10:58-08:00","id":1556191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556186#post1556186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Gentry ever abduct other supernaturals? I know you can't change major templates even if the Gentry tried, but it seems a bit unlikely one of the Others wouldn't occasionally want an exotic pet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Caveats apply as they would be hard to procure for many, many reasons, and the trip would probably leave very few if any supernatural marks (if they do, that would have more to do with the target than the fae).<br /> <br /> But there's no reason for this to be impossible, even by accident. And some True Fae may actually specialize on it, who knows...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T17:26:44-08:00","id":1556209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556191#post1556191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Caveats apply as they would be hard to procure for many, many reasons, and the trip would probably leave very few if any supernatural marks (if they do, that would have more to do with the target than the fae).<br /> <br /> But there's no reason for this to be impossible, even by accident. And some True Fae may actually specialize on it, who knows...</div> </div> </div> </div>I could even see this as one way a 'ling could get in with a pack of werewolves as per the Pack book. Saving one of their own from a Gentry, with you escaping in the process, or if a werewolf joined up with a motley of 'lings because they feel they owe them for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27579-icefyer2","name":"Icefyer2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T22:39:06-08:00","id":1556226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556209#post1556209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could even see this as one way a 'ling could get in with a pack of werewolves as per the Pack book. Saving one of their own from a Gentry, with you escaping in the process, or if a werewolf joined up with a motley of 'lings because they feel they owe them for the help.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could go further and in many ways.<br /> <br /> A Pack that finds out about the Gentry, especially in an area where they're particularly active, may end up getting involved with the fae on a regular basis as they take upon themselves the role of defending their territory against such entities. They may even specialize on hunting things from the Hedge, and frequently add to the Pack survivors from that place, Changeling or not.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, more than simply owing them for the help, a supernatural that spent too much time as a slave to the True Fae may <i>feel</i> more Changeling than whatever they are.<br /> <br /> We have to remember that the characters aren't really bound to their splat societies, they're just societies in the end. And the Durance is particularly prone to make a character of other splat feel a greater need to be with the Courts who share their experience and trauma than with their kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T06:38:58-08:00","id":1556236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556186#post1556186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Gentry ever abduct other supernaturals? I know you can't change major templates even if the Gentry tried, but it seems a bit unlikely one of the Others wouldn't occasionally want an exotic pet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that other Major splat can became Hedge denizens and Goblin queens, i think that a fae kidnapping a vampire for example would not change his nature as a vampire<br /> If the vampire escapes he would simply carry any change as a Hedge denizen condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T21:43:41-08:00","id":1556280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556226#post1556226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could go further and in many ways.<br /> <br /> A Pack that finds out about the Gentry, especially in an area where they're particularly active, may end up getting involved with the fae on a regular basis as they take upon themselves the role of defending their territory against such entities. They may even specialize on hunting things from the Hedge, and frequently add to the Pack survivors from that place, Changeling or not.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, more than simply owing them for the help, a supernatural that spent too much time as a slave to the True Fae may <i>feel</i> more Changeling than whatever they are.<br /> <br /> We have to remember that the characters aren't really bound to their splat societies, they're just societies in the end. And the Durance is particularly prone to make a character of other splat feel a greater need to be with the Courts who share their experience and trauma than with their kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf pack inducted as honorary members of the Autumn court would be wild. All that lunacy-induced fear. Wonder how a werewolf going through a durance might change them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27579-icefyer2","name":"Icefyer2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T07:00:14-08:00","id":1556291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556280#post1556280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A werewolf pack inducted as honorary members of the Autumn court would be wild. All that lunacy-induced fear. Wonder how a werewolf going through a durance might change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given their inherent shape-changing nature (and susceptibility to a contagion which messes with that) I would assume flexibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T13:29:57-08:00","id":1556309,"title":"","content":"Non-mortals can't really be changed by a durance in Arcadia...<br /> <br /> ...but it <i>is</i> a neat excuse to pick up strange Merit or a Merit to that creatures specific splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T18:30:19-08:00","id":1556327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556280#post1556280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A werewolf pack inducted as honorary members of the Autumn court would be wild. All that lunacy-induced fear. Wonder how a werewolf going through a durance might change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>For story purposes they don't even have to be honorary members, they me be actual members.<br /> <br /> Of course that for Rules purposes they only have Court Goodwill or something similar, but the Court may very well take them a full members if they went through the Durance.<br /> <br /> In any in-character evaluation, a Changeling is defined by the experience, not by having this or that power. And those supernaturals may even have their own Fetches running amok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556309#post1556309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-mortals can't really be changed by a durance in Arcadia...<br /> <br /> ...but it <i>is</i> a neat excuse to pick up strange Merit or a Merit to that creatures specific splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Into a Changeling</i>.<br /> <br /> They can't be changed <i>into a Changeling</i> by a Durance, or be changed deliberately by the Gentry.<br /> <br /> But they can be changed in weird ways, especially if they're NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:29:46-08:00","id":1556413,"title":"","content":"In a similar vein...<br /> <br /> Briarwolves:<br /> Werewolves forever lost to the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T15:26:37-08:00","id":1556417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1556413#post1556413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a similar vein...<br /> <br /> Briarwolves:<br /> Werewolves forever lost to the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of several possible origins for any given briarwolf, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T13:51:42-08:00","id":1557063,"title":"","content":"So, to my knowledge there is little to nothing on Goblin Princesses besides of ffew mentions of them existing and dealing drugs in some areas in the Hedge book. If you were to stat them or expand on them and what they are, how would you lovely people do it? In my mind I was thinking of them existing stat wise as what should be a goblin queen when there is already a goblin queen present in a region","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T15:08:35-08:00","id":1557068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1557063#post1557063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to my knowledge there is little to nothing on Goblin Princesses besides of ffew mentions of them existing and dealing drugs in some areas in the Hedge book.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're literally only mentioned once in that offhand example list of ways traversing the Hedge is never dull; they aren't a ludonarratively defined position in Changeling's wider cosmology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you were to stat them or expand on them and what they are, how would you lovely people do it? In my mind I was thinking of them existing stat wise as what should be a goblin queen when there is already a goblin queen present in a region </div> </div> </div>That's a reasonable take, as is the goblin equivalent of the apprentices and prospective heirs to the station of an entitlement mentioned in Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn. Like Kith and Kin's expansion on Goblin Contracts via the primer on dramaturgy, this is something that exists below the abstraction layer of game mechanics, and the breadth of possibilities for goblin stuff means they could be almost anything in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixed typos. 01-22-2026, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T04:26:48-07:00","id":1558884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558877#post1558877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings lose bits of their souls in the transition into and out of Arcadian servitude (crossing through a realm that exists on the boundary between conscious and unconscious experience) in a way that takes some of their memories with it in solidified metaphors and leaves them prone to evoking sudden bursts of emotion in those who perceive them, stitching those missing pieces back into their souls by taking them out of the Hedge. The Lost liches known as the Empty do not remove their souls \u2014 quite the opposite \u2014 but instead remove their hearts for safekeeping as part of their immortality, and Contracts (and the Wyrd more generally) work on sympathetic principles that heavily involve names and identity and reciprocity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking here because it seems more pertinent.<br /> <br /> Changeling still have Wyrd and clarity even if they recover all their Icons, right? And there is no way to really cure what happens to them during their durance? (I mean without timetravel, I guess...) <br /> <br /> Like there is something beyond the damage to their soul which results in their power...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T06:11:40-07:00","id":1558887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1558884#post1558884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling still have Wyrd and clarity even if they recover all their Icons, right? And there is no way to really cure what happens to them during their durance? (I mean without timetravel, I guess...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Icons do not serve as a means of restoring one's humanity, correct \u2014 they can contain memories and aspects of the character that didn't exist until the durance, and the generally-understood point of their creation is during the changeling's escape through the Thorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T06:58:05-07:00","id":1558888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1558887#post1558887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Icons do not serve as a means of restoring one's humanity, correct \u2014 they can contain memories and aspects of the character that didn't exist until the durance, and the generally-understood point of their creation is during the changeling's escape through the Thorns.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding was that the are parts of the identity that get ripped off by the thorns.<br /> <br /> And getting them back makes the Changeling more whole.<br /> <br /> Avoiding using the word soul here, as it doesn't seem specific.<br /> <br /> What they become in the Hedge is a seperate question. I know there was some suggestion that a bunch of Icons could be sown together into a Hedge Ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T10:06:11-07:00","id":1558893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1558888#post1558888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding was that the are parts of the identity that get ripped off by the thorns.<br /> <br /> And getting them back makes the Changeling more whole.<br /> <br /> Avoiding using the word soul here, as it doesn't seem specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, an Icon is part of the changeling's identity <i>as a changeling</i>, with some of those bits coming from who the changeling was before the durance. A loose comparison can be made to the identifiers that slough off of characters immersed in the Ocean of Fragments, but no amount of gathered eggshells will allow the Lost to uncrack an egg.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What they become in the Hedge is a seperate question. I know there was some suggestion that a bunch of Icons could be sown together into a Hedge Ghost? </div> </div> </div>In a process that is similarly mechanically undefined to how the True Fae turn Dreamborn into baubles, yes. The Hedge does not want for strange bits of reality given life, animation, and/or personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T05:34:25-07:00","id":1559160,"title":"","content":"Does media (film and tv recordings, photographs, etc) store the Mien or the Mask?<br /> <br /> And technological devices (especially facial recognition software), with what do they actually deal with, Mien or Mask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T07:38:19-07:00","id":1559163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1559160#post1559160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does media (film and tv recordings, photographs, etc) store the Mien or the Mask?<br /> <br /> And technological devices (especially facial recognition software), with what do they actually deal with, Mien or Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer for all is the Mask","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T04:44:40-07:00","id":1561816,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Apologies, this question is in a similar vein to one I asked previously, but it's distinct and specific to our current chronicle.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Golden-Grand-Duke-Who-Never-Misses becomes vulnerable for the rest of the scene and permanently loses access to its Sword Regalia if it \u201cmisses\u201d with its bow; the Promise-bent-into-Wood.<br /> <br /> In Arcadia and the Hedge, if Duke uses an attack as a form of Hedgespinning, with the intent of binding its target in their bowstrings, does the target have to spend a WP point before they can apply their Defense? Or does defense apply normal, with spending WP only giving the target a chance to resist the Hedgespinning's effects?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T06:00:50-07:00","id":1561819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1561816#post1561816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Arcadia and the Hedge, if Duke uses an attack as a form of Hedgespinning, with the intent of binding its target in their bowstrings, does the target have to spend a WP point before they can apply their Defense? Or does defense apply normal, with spending WP only giving the target a chance to resist the Hedgespinning's effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter would be my take. The Hedgespinning effect is distinct from whatever action it is attached to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T19:28:32-07:00","id":1561864,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One thing I'm still unclear on:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Title\u2019s in Arcadia and the Hedge &quot;automatically succeed&quot; at oneiromantic or Hedgespinning actions unless the target spends a Willpower point for the chance to resist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, Hedgespinning is attached to an action that is itself resolved normally, and many of those actions are resisted or contested.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If the underlying action is resisted or contested, how is a Title's automatic success meant to interact with that?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T20:03:26-07:00","id":1561865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1561864#post1561864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm still unclear on:<br /> <br /> Title\u2019s in Arcadia and the Hedge &quot;automatically succeed&quot; at oneiromantic or Hedgespinning actions unless the target spends a Willpower point for the chance to resist.<br /> <br /> However, Hedgespinning is attached to an action that is itself resolved normally, and many of those actions are resisted or contested.<br /> <br /> If the underlying action is resisted or contested, how is a Title's automatic success meant to interact with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't normally need to target the subject of a shift with the action you're using to make the shift and the action still needs to have the part of it that isn't Hedgespinning or dreamweaving resolved. Any reality-warping action that isn't trying to do two things at once doesn't need to worry about contending with the will of scenery.<br /> <br /> This is a notoriously unclarified mechanic and the best we can currently do is try to parse it in a way that makes sense. Narratively it exists to allow the Fae to do things on the Hedgespinning and Oneiromancy Shift charts appropriate to a Title's portfolio while in Faerie and its borderland. The Duke is not going to do Hedgespinning to bind a target if he has more appropriate concrete powers to accomplish this, which are mechanically more likely to be Contracts and/or token powers of his Regalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:56:34-07:00","id":1561877,"title":"","content":"The narratively important limitation is that this authority does not extend into the mortal world. If the Duke had a Contract or Token that replicated the same effect, that ability would (at least in most cases) work on the iron-side of the fence as well. Such is the case for most Contracts and Tokens - granted not all. Whereas the Hedgespinning/Oneiromancy ability;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Specifically addresses the boundary by distinguishing what the Duke can impose upon dreams and the Hedge because of its Title and what it cannot do once removed from that environment; and</li> <li>How it exercises that authority in a way different from Changelings and Huntsmen</li> </ol>Thus, we are wanting to engage with this mechanic specifically. I\u2019ll rephrase the question with a hypothetical.<br /> <br /> A Changeling and a True Fae are both in the Thorns. They each yell really loudly at the thorns to rise up and strike the other. Both choose to resolve the action as Hedgespinning, taking a -2 penalty for acting in the Thorns, and both roll Presence + Persuasion. After resolving the rolls, both succeed and each get 2 successes beyond the 1 that was required for yelling at some inanimate briar-like growths. They then each spend 1 glamour to perform a subtle shift, introducing a personal tilt like leg wrack (one leg) onto the other.<br /> <br /> At what point in this process does the True Fae\u2019s automatic success apply?<br /> <br /> At what point does the Changeling spend WP to gain a chance to resist the True Fae?<br /> <br /> One interpretation is that the True Fae does not roll at all, merely spending 1 glamour to impose the Tilt unless the Changeling spends a willpower. It must now roll and generate enough successes to impose the tilt.<br /> <br /> Another is that the True Fae still rolls, but is able to apply the personal tilt so long as they succeeded at the original action, even if they had rolled 0 success beyond what was needed, again, unless the changeling spends a willpower. Now unless 2 or more successes beyond what was need were rolled the True Fae fails at imposing the personal tilt.<br /> <br /> Which interpretation is more accurate, or is there some other interaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28154-arrested-scrimshank","name":"Arrested Scrimshank","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T06:50:58-07:00","id":1561893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrested Scrimshank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1561877#post1561877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Changeling and a True Fae are both in the Thorns. They each yell really loudly at the thorns to rise up and strike the other. Both choose to resolve the action as Hedgespinning, taking a -2 penalty for acting in the Thorns, and both roll Presence + Persuasion. After resolving the rolls, both succeed and each get 2 successes beyond the 1 that was required for yelling at some inanimate briar-like growths. They then each spend 1 glamour to perform a subtle shift, introducing a personal tilt like leg wrack (one leg) onto the other.<br /> <br /> At what point in this process does the True Fae\u2019s automatic success apply?<br /> <br /> At what point does the Changeling spend WP to gain a chance to resist the True Fae?<br /> <br /> One interpretation is that the True Fae does not roll at all, merely spending 1 glamour to impose the Tilt unless the Changeling spends a willpower. It must now roll and generate enough successes to impose the tilt.<br /> <br /> Another is that the True Fae still rolls, but is able to apply the personal tilt so long as they succeeded at the original action, even if they had rolled 0 success beyond what was needed, again, unless the changeling spends a willpower. Now unless 2 or more successes beyond what was need were rolled the True Fae fails at imposing the personal tilt.<br /> <br /> Which interpretation is more accurate, or is there some other interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest approach I would take is that unless the original action is being used for more than just shaping and directly targeting a subject capable of contesting or resisting that original action, the True Fae doesn't need to roll; the subject of the shaping can spend a point of Willpower to resist the shaping for the turn that it would affect them or be introduced to them personally (i.e. you can't stop a Stranger from introducing a hazard to the scene or changing the properties of Hedge features or creating weapons, but you can stop them from lowering your Speed, applying Personal Tilts, forcing failed rolls to become dramatic failures, etc).<br /> <br /> The resistance doesn't require a roll or impose a penalty above and beyond what the Fae would get for trying to shape reality as a changeling; the subject is simply down one Willpower and the Fae is down the amount of Glamour they would normally spend to make a subtle or paradigm shift and (in Initiative) has used their turn to accomplish nothing. Hedgespinning and oneiromancy aren't normally resisted directly because the character doing the shaping is instead interfacing with the world itself.<br /> <br /> Combined with the note that having a Contract/token/other power doesn't need to spend successes or use a paradigm shift (the former being less relevant in this case) to make applicable changes normally, this mechanic is the representation of &quot;A given Title has limited omnipotence within the confines of its role&quot; \u2014 the Princess of Red Crowns can completely change the scenery to summon her Crimson Keep, make a location change to drag off wicked children to her Keep, or (guessing at the mechanical translation here) impose a Condition or Personal Tilt to nail her hats to people's heads, but the latter two can be forestalled for as long as the targets have Willpower to spare.<br /> <br /> The Princess doesn't get to bypass the mechanics for rolling to see if a normal action succeeds regardless of what her Title is (at least not purely by virtue of that Title) \u2014 she has to go through the reality-warping filter relating to her Title, which has people (read: phenomena anthropomorphized through the lens of the Wyrd) for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixed typos in the last line. 07-22-2026, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T11:57:59-07:00","id":1563997,"title":"","content":"Could the venom option of Fang &amp; Talon apply to the thorns from the Thistle's Rebuke Contract?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T12:26:55-07:00","id":1563998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1563997#post1563997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the venom option of Fang &amp; Talon apply to the thorns from the Thistle's Rebuke Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Thistle's Rebuke modifies the changeling's clothing or armor and the Talon &amp; Wing bonus is giving the character themselves fangs or claws; even without drawing a distinction between &quot;change to the character's equipment&quot; and &quot;change to the character's body,&quot; they're separate vectors of attack/damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T06:08:54-07:00","id":1564118,"title":"","content":"Would a Changeling gain Glamour from eating a goblin beast, as well as from goblin fruits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T06:54:55-07:00","id":1564119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1564118#post1564118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Changeling gain Glamour from eating a goblin beast, as well as from goblin fruits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 103 of the corebook: &quot;Eating certain Hedge beasts provides Glamour, but doing so risks perception-warping indigestion if not prepared correctly \u2014 and proper preparations are not always obvious.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T20:39:10-07:00","id":1564598,"title":"","content":"How does the Soulless condition affects a changeling Clarity? Does it deal more damage? Can a Changeling slip into the Thrall condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T23:16:18-07:00","id":1564599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1501118-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-new-thread?p=1564598#post1564598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Soulless condition affects a changeling Clarity? Does it deal more damage? Can a Changeling slip into the Thrall condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>No published material besides the stuff in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed and the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle establishing that the Lost are susceptible to magic capable of stealing Awakened souls. Without speculating about how breaking points from indulging the Vice you don't have translate, changelings with the Soulless Condition lose two dice on contested rolls to fight off possession and do not regain Willpower from restful sleep or surrendering in a violent encounter, and that's it.<br /> <br /> Since Clarity does not represent the same thing as Integrity or even Wisdom or Humanity, you might take cues from the Empty mechanics and have a Soulless changeling gain a version of the Soul Shocked Condition that cannot resolve until they recover their soul or a suitable replacement; whether to allow the Condition to progress to Enervated is a decision for your game, but offhand I'd suggest having it replace Comatose or the other Conditions from Kith and Kin once you hit Clarity 0, triggering the loss of Willpower dots from suffering Clarity attacks due to actions on which you spent Willpower, possibly having such actions also use the base mechanic for risking Willpower from Hunter (succeeding at the action gives you the Willpower point back plus an extra point).<br /> <br /> Switching to Thrall at Willpower 0 is likewise a decision for your table, but considering the Condition specifically says you should only continue playing the character if they stand a chance of regaining a soul things have gone quite far south if one of the Lost has gotten into such dire straits outside of the usual idiom the fae-adjacent world uses for such things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.j